hadiths[679]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","On the authority of the Commander of the Faithful, Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: ""Verily, deeds are judged by their intentions, and every person will be rewarded according to what he intended. Thus, whoever emigrated for the sake of Allah and His Messenger, his emigration is counted for Allah and His Messenger. But whoever emigrated for worldly gain or to marry a woman, his emigration is for that which he emigrated to."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"2","On the authority of the Mother of the Believers, 'Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""An army will advance against the Ka'bah, and when they reach the desert plain of Bayda', the first and the last of them will be swallowed up by the earth."" She said: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, how will the first and the last of them be swallowed when among them are their merchants and others not part of the army?"" He replied: ""The first and the last of them will be swallowed, then they will be resurrected according to their intentions."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim - this is the wording of Al-Bukhari]"
"3","On the authority of 'Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""There is no migration after the conquest of Makkah, but rather jihad and sincere intention remain. And if you are called to battle, then go forth."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"4","On the authority of Abu 'Abdullah Jabir ibn 'Abdullah al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) on a campaign when he said: ""There are men in Madinah who accompany you on whatever journey you travel and through whatever valley you cross — they were kept back by illness."" In another narration: ""...they share with you in the reward."" [Muslim] [Al-Bukhari] narrated on the authority of Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: We returned from the Battle of Tabuk with the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said: ""There are people left behind in Madinah — we did not pass through any mountain pass or valley except that they were with us, held back by a valid excuse."""
"5","And on the authority of Abu Yazid Ma’an bin Yazid bin Al-Akhnas, may Allah be pleased with them, who, along with his father and grandfather, were companions. He said: Abu Yazid had taken out dinars to give in charity, so he placed them with a man in the mosque. I came and took them and brought them to him, and he said: By Allah, I did not want you. So I argued with him to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: “You have what you intended, O Yazid, and you have what you took, O Ma’an.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"6","On the authority of Abu Ishaq Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him), one of the ten who were given glad tidings of Paradise, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to visit me during the Farewell Pilgrimage when I was suffering from a severe illness. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I am in severe pain as you can see, and I have wealth but only one daughter will inherit from me. Should I give away two-thirds of my wealth in charity?"" He said: ""No."" I said: ""Half, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""No."" I said: ""One-third, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""One-third, and one-third is plenty. It is better to leave your heirs well-off than to leave them poor, begging from people. You will not spend anything seeking the pleasure of Allah except that you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you put into your wife's mouth."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, will I be left behind after my companions?"" He said: ""You will not be left behind to do a righteous deed seeking the pleasure of Allah except that it will raise you in rank and status. Perhaps you will be left behind so that some people may benefit from you and others be harmed by you. O Allah, complete the migration of my companions and do not turn them back on their heels. But the unfortunate one is Sa'd ibn Khawlah"" — the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) grieved for him because he died in Makkah. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"7","On the authority of Abu Hurairah Abd al-Rahman bin Sakhr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah does not look at your bodies, nor at your images, but rather looks at your hearts and your deeds” [Muslim]."
"8","On the authority of Abu Musa 'Abdullah ibn Qays al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about a man who fights out of bravery, fights out of tribal zeal, and fights out of ostentation — which of these is in the path of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is supreme, he is in the path of Allah."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"9","On the authority of Abu Bakra Nafi` ibn al-Harith al-Thaqafi, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “When two Muslims met with their swords, the killer and the killed will be in the Fire.” I said, O Messenger of Allah, this is the killer, so what about the killed? He said: “He was keen to kill his friend” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"10","On the authority of Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer in his home and marketplace by twenty-seven degrees. This is because when one of them performs ablution and does it well, then comes to the mosque wanting nothing but prayer — nothing moves him except prayer — every step he takes raises him one degree and removes one sin until he enters the mosque. When he enters the mosque, he is considered to be in prayer as long as prayer keeps him there. The angels send blessings upon any of you as long as he remains in the place where he prayed, so long as he does not break his wudu."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim - this is the wording of Muslim]"
"11","On the authority of Abu Abbas Abdullah bin Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in what is narrated on the authority of his Lord, Blessed and Most High, he said: “Allah has written down good deeds and bad deeds, and then he explained that: Whoever intends to do a good deed and does not do it, Allah, Blessed and Most High, writes it down with Him as a complete good deed, and if he intends to do it and does it, Allah writes it down as ten good deeds up to seven hundred times many times over, and if he intends to do a bad deed and does not do it, Allah, Blessed and Most High, records it with Him as a complete good deed; and if he intends to do it and does it, Allah writes it down as one bad deed.” (Agreed upon)"
"12","On the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah bin Omar bin al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Three people from those who were before you set off until they had spent the night in a cave, and they entered it. Then a rock descended from the mountain, blocking the cave for them, and they said: He will not save you from this rock unless you pray to Allah for the good of your deeds.” One of them said: Oh Allah, I had two old fathers. They were old, and I was not going to lose their family or wealth. One day they turned away from me in pursuit of the trees, and I did not go to them until they fell asleep, so I milked their sleep for them, and I found them sleeping, so I hated to wake them up and to lose their family or wealth, so I remained - with the mug in my hand - waiting for them to wake up until the light of dawn, and the boys were teasing at my feet - and they woke up and drank their sleep. Oh Allah, if You had done that. Seeking Your face, so relieve us of the situation we are in from this rock, and it released something from which they cannot get out. The other said: Oh Allah, I had a cousin who was the dearest person to me. And in a narration: I loved her as much as men love women, so I wanted her for myself, so she abstained from me until she had suffered from me for a year, so she came to me, so I gave her twenty and a hundred dinars on the condition that she would separate herself from me, so I did, even if I was able to. ""And in a narration: ""And when she sat between her legs, she said: Fear Allah and do not reveal the ring except by his right. Then she turned away from her, and she was the most beloved of people to me, and left the gold that you had given her. Oh Allah, if you did that seeking Your face, then release us from what we are in. Then the rock released, but they cannot get out of it. The third said: Oh Allah, I hired workers and gave them their wages, except for one man who left the one who left. And he went, and his reward yielded until his money increased. He came to me after a while and said: O Abdullah, give me my reward. I said: Whatever you see of your reward: camels, cows, sheep, and slaves. He said: O Abdullah, do not mock me! I said: I do not mock you. So he took it all and sipped it, leaving nothing of it. Oh Allah, if I did that seeking Your face, then relieve me. We were in a state of what we were in, so the rock released and they went out walking” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"13","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “By Allah, I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him more than seventy times a day” [Al-Bukhari]."
"14","On the authority of Al-Aghar bin Yasar Al-Muzani, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O people, repent to Allah and ask Him for forgiveness, for I repent a hundred times a day” [Muslim]."
"15","On the authority of Abu Hamza Anas bin Malik al-Ansari, the servant of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah is more joyful with the repentance of His servant than one of you who fell off his camel and lost it in a desert land” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim: Allah is more joyful with the repentance of His servant when he repents to Him than [the joy of] a man who is on his mount in a desert land, and it escapes from him with his food and drink, and he loses all hope of finding it, so he comes to a tree and lies down in its shade, having given up all hope of his mount, and while he is in that state, he finds it standing beside him, so he grabs its halter and then says out of overwhelming joy: ‘O Allah, You are my servant and I am Your Lord’ – he misspoke out of overwhelming joy.”"
"16","On the authority of Abu Musa Abdullah bin Qais Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Allah Almighty extends His hand at night so that the sinner of the day may repent, and He extends His hand during the day so that the sinner of the night may repent, until the sun rises from the west” [Muslim]."
"17","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever repents before the sun rises from the west, Allah will accept his repentance” [Muslim]."
"18","On the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “Allah Almighty accepts the servant’s repentance as long as his soul does not reach his throat” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"19","On the authority of Zar bin Hubaish, he said: I came to Safwan bin Assal, may Allah be pleased with him, to ask him about wiping over the socks. He said: What brought you, Yazr? I said: Seeking knowledge. He said: The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge who is satisfied with what he seeks. I said: One of the companions of the Prophet (ﷺ). So I came to ask you: Did you hear him mention anything about that? He said: Yes, he was ordering us that if we were traveling, we should not remove our leather socks for three days and nights except in the case of ritual impurity, but we could remove them for defecation, urination, and sleep. I said: Travel. While we were with him, a Bedouin called out to him in a loud voice: O Muhammad, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called back to him with a similar loud voice: 'Haoum.' So I said to him: Woe to you, lower your voice, for you are in the presence of the Prophet (ﷺ), and I have forbidden this to you! He said: By Allah, I will not lower my voice. The Bedouin said: Why does a person love a people before he joins them? The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'A person will be with those he loves on the Day of Resurrection.' He continued speaking to us until he mentioned a door in the west, before the direction of the Levant, whose width is the distance a rider would travel in forty or seventy years. Sufyan, one of the narrators, said: Allah Almighty created it on the day He created the heavens and the earth, open for repentance, and it will not be closed until the sun rises from it. [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"20","On the authority of Abu Sa`id Sa`d bin Malik bin Sinan al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Among those before you was a man who killed ninety-nine people, so he asked about the most knowledgeable people on earth, and he was directed to a monk. He came to him and said: I have killed ninety-nine people, so is there any repentance for me? He said: No, so he killed him and completed one hundred, then he asked about the most knowledgeable people on earth, and he was directed to a man of knowledge. He said: I have killed one hundred souls. Is there any repentance for me? He said: Yes, and who will prevent him from repenting? He went to such-and-such a land, for there are people who worship Allah Almighty, so worship Allah with them, and do not return to your land, for it is a land of evil. So he set off until, when he was halfway through, death came to him, and the angels of mercy and the angels of torment quarreled over him. The angels of mercy said: He came repentant, heading with his heart to Allah. Allah Almighty, and the angels of torment said: He had never done good, so an angel came to them in the form of a human, and they placed him between them - that is, an arbiter - and he said: Measure what is between the two lands, and to whichever of them he was closer, then it is his. So they measured and found that he was closer to the land that he wanted, so the angels of mercy seized him [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"21","On the authority of Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik, who was the leader of Ka’b, may Allah be pleased with him, one of his sons when he became blind. He said: I heard Ka’b bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, narrating his hadith when he lagged behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the Battle of Tabuk. Ka’b said: I never lagged behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in a battle he fought except in the Battle of Tabuk, except that I lagged behind in the Battle of Badr, and I did not and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not blame anyone who stayed behind, but the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out while the Muslims were seeking the caravan of Quraysh until Allah Almighty brought them together with their enemy without a deadline. I witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the night of Aqaba when we agreed upon Islam, and I would not like to have the sight of Badr there, even if Badr was more memorable among the people than it. It was from my experience when he lagged behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the Battle of Tabuk that I I had never been stronger or easier than when I lagged behind him in that battle. By Allah, I had never combined two mounts before that until I combined them in that battle. the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not want a battle unless he thought of another one. Until that battle, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) invaded it in intense heat. He faced a long and arduous journey. He received a large number, so it became clear to the Muslims that they should be ready for their battle. So he told them with the face he wanted, and there are many Muslims with the Messenger of Allah, and no register/record-keeper keeps track of them. “He means by that the Diwan.” Ka’b said: So say a man wants to be absent unless he thinks that this will be hidden from him unless a revelation from Allah descends on him. the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) launched that expedition when the fruits and shadows were good, and I am heading for it. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prepared and the Muslims were with him, and I set out in the morning to prepare. So I went back and did not fulfill anything, and I said to myself: I am able to do that if I wanted, so he continued to push me until I continued with the serious people, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was going out and the Muslims were with him, and I did not spend anything from my preparation, then I went back and did not fulfill anything, and he continued to go too far with me until they hastened and the desire had passed, so I decided to leave and catch up with them. After the departure of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) it saddens me to see a role model for me, except a man steeped in hypocrisy. Or a man whom Allah Almighty has excused as an example, except a man who is immersed in hypocrisy, or a weak man whom Allah Almighty has excused. the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not mention me until he reached Tabuk, and he said while he was sitting among the people in Tabuk: What did Ka’b bin Malik do? A man from Banu Salama said, O Messenger of Allah, imprison him. flog him and look at his sides. So Muadh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: “What an evil thing you said! By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we have only learned good about him.” The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) remained silent, and while he was doing that, he saw a man with white hair that removed the mirage. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Be Abu Khaythamah. So, behold, Abu Khaythamah Al-Ansari, and he He who gave alms for a share of dates when the hypocrites slandered him. Ka’b said: When I was informed that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had set off in a caravan from Tabuk and attended me with my share, I began to think of lying and say: How can I get out of his anger tomorrow and I will seek help from all of my family’s opinionated people in that matter. When it was said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) may keep coming, the falsehood was removed from me until I knew that I had not escaped anything from it. Never, so I resolved to be truthful, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was arriving. Whenever he came from a journey, he would start with the mosque and kneel in it two rak’ahs, then sit down for the people. When he did that, the people who had left behind came to him, apologizing to him and swearing to him, and they were eighty-odd men. He accepted their public actions, pledged allegiance to them, asked forgiveness for them, and entrusted their secrets to Allah Almighty until I came. When I greeted him, I smiled, and the angry person smiled, and then he said: Come, So I started walking until I sat in front of him, and he said to me: What prevented you? Did you not buy your mount? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, if I were to sit with someone else from the people of the world, I would think that I would get out of his anger with an excuse. I gave an argument, but by Allah, I knew that if I told you a false story today that you would be satisfied with, Allah would soon displease you with me, and if I told you a truthful story, you would find me in it, and I would hope for Allah's retaliation in it. Almighty, by Allah, I had no excuse, and by Allah, I was never stronger or easier than I was when I lagged behind you. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “As for this man, he has spoken the truth, so stand up until Allah decides on you.” Men from Banu Salamah walked and followed me, and they said to me: By Allah, we did not know that you had committed a sin before this. I was incapable of not having apologized to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the same way that those who left behind had apologized to him. Your sin was sufficient for you to seek forgiveness from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: By Allah, they continued to scold me until I wanted to go back to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and lie to myself. Then I said to them: Did anyone meet this with me? They said: Yes, two men met with you and said as you said. And it was said to them the same as what was said to you. He said: I said: Who are they? They said: Marara bin al-Rabi’ al-Umari and Hilal bin Umayyah al-Waqifi? He said: They mentioned to me two righteous men who had witnessed Badr, and they had role models. He said: So I went on when they mentioned them to me. And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade us from speaking. You three are among those who stayed behind. He said: So we avoided people - or He said: They changed for us - until I disguised myself in the same land, but it is not the land that I know, so we stayed in that for fifty nights. As for my two friends, they remained silent and sat in their homes crying, and as for me, I was the strongest of the people and the most stubborn of them, so I would go out and witness the prayer with the Muslims, and go around the markets and no one would speak to me, and I would go to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and greet him while he was in his seat after the prayer, so I would say to myself: Will I? He moved his lips to return the greeting or greeting? Then I prayed close to him and caught his gaze. When I approached my prayer, he looked at me, and if I turned towards him, he turned away from me, until after that had prolonged the harshness of the Muslims, I walked until I reached the wall of Abu Qatada’s wall. He is my cousin and the most beloved of people to me. So I greeted him, but by Allah he did not return my greeting. So I said to him: O Abu Qatada, I implore you by Allah, do you teach me to love Allah and His Messenger? So I remained silent, so I went back and appealed to him and he remained silent, so I appealed to him again and he said: Allah and His Messenger know best. Then my eyes welled up and I turned until I reached the wall. While I was walking in the market of Medina, one of the people of the Levant who had brought food to sell it to Medina came running down, saying: Who can point to Ka’b bin Malik? So the people started pointing to him until he came to me and a letter from the king of Ghassan came to me, and I was He wrote. So I read it and found in it: As for what follows, we have been informed that your friend has estranged you, and Allah has not placed you in a place of humiliation or loss, so join us with your pendulums. When I read it, I said, “This is also a calamity,” so I lit the oven with it and burned it. Until forty of the fifty had passed and the revelation had taken hold, a messenger from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me and said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commands you to separate from your wife. So I said: Divorce her, or what should I do? He said: No, rather separate from her and do not approach her, and he sent a similar message to my friend. So I said to my wife: Go to your family and be with them until Allah will decide this matter, so the wife of Hilal bin Umayyah came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Hilal bin Umayyah is an old man who is lost and has no servant. Do you dislike me serving him? He said: No, but he will not come close to you. She said: By Allah, he has no movement for anything, and by Allah he is still crying since he was in a state of affairs until this day. He said to me some My family: If you ask permission from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding your wife, has he given permission to the wife of Hilal bin Umayyah to serve him? So I said: I will not ask permission from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and I do not know what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would say if I asked him for permission when I was a young man! So I stayed in that for ten nights, completing fifty nights for us since the time he forbade us from speaking. Then I prayed. Fajr prayer on the morning of fifty nights on the roof of one of our houses. While I was sitting in the state that Allah Almighty mentioned of us, and my soul became crowded and the earth was constricted with all its spaciousness, I heard the voice of a crier, Awafa Ali Sila’, saying at the top of his voice: O Ka’b bin Malik, give good tidings, so I fell down prostrating, and I knew that relief had come. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) announced to the people the repentance of Allah Almighty upon us when he prayed the dawn prayer, so the people went. Giving us good tidings, so my companions went before my companions giving good tidings, and a man ran to me on a horse and chased the one who had converted to Islam before me and fulfilled his duty on the mountain, so the voice was faster than the horse, so when the one whose voice I heard giving me good tidings came to me, I took off my dress for him and covered them with him with good tidings. By Allah, I had no other than them that day, and I borrowed two clothes, put them on, and went off to follow the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). People greeted me, crowd after crowd, congratulating me on my repentance and saying To me: May Allah’s repentance be upon you, until I entered the mosque and saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with people sitting around him. Then Talha bin Ubaidullah, may Allah be pleased with him, got up and ran until he shook my hand and congratulated me. By Allah, no man from among the immigrants stood up except him. Ka'b did not forget it for Talha. Ka'b said: When I greeted the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said, with his face shining with happiness: Good tidings for the day that has passed since your mother gave birth to you. I said: Is it with you, O Messenger of Allah, or from Allah? He said: No, but from Allah Almighty, and whenever the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was illuminating. His face looked like a piece of the moon, and we knew that from him, so when I sat in front of him, I said: O Messenger of Allah, part of my repentance is that I give up some of my wealth as charity to Allah and to His Messenger. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Keep some of your money for yourself, for it is better for you. So I said: I will keep my share that is in Khaybar. And I said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah Almighty only saved me with honesty, and it is part of my repentance that I do not I have narrated nothing but the truth as long as I remain. By Allah, I have not known any Muslim whom Allah has done with the truthfulness of the hadith since I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) better than what Allah Almighty has done to me. By Allah, I have not deliberately told a lie since I said that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) until this day. And I hope that Allah Almighty will protect me for what remains. He said: Then Allah Almighty revealed: “Indeed, Allah has turned to the Prophet and the Emigrants.” And the helpers who followed him in the hour of difficulty) until he reached: {Indeed, He is Most Compassionate and Merciful to them. And to the three who were left behind, even when the earth was narrow to them with all its spaciousness} until he reached: {Fear Allah and be with the truthful} [At-Tawbah 117, 119] Ka’b said: By Allah, Allah has never bestowed upon me any blessing. After Allah guided me to Islam, it is greater in my soul than my sincerity with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that I should not be a lie to him and then perish just as those who lied perished. Indeed, Allah Almighty said to those who lied when the revelation was sent down, “The evil of what He said to anyone.” Then Allah Almighty said: {They will swear to Allah to you that if you turn to them, you will turn away from them. So turn away from them. Indeed, they are an abomination, and their abode is Hell, a recompense for what they used to earn. They swore. You may be satisfied with them, but if you are satisfied with them, then Allah is not satisfied with the transgressing people.} [At-Tawbah: 95,96]. Ka’b said: O three of us, we were behind in the matter of those from whom the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) accepted when they swore to him, so he pledged allegiance to them and asked forgiveness for them. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) postponed our matter until Allah Almighty decreed that. Allah Almighty said: {And upon the three who were left behind}. What was mentioned is not that we left behind in the battle, but rather it is his abandoning us and deferring our command from the one who swore to him and apologized to him, and he accepted from him. Agreed upon. And in a narration, “The Prophet (ﷺ) went out in the Battle of Tabuk on a Thursday, and he loved That he should leave on a Thursday.” And in a narration: “He would not arrive from a journey except in the afternoon, so when he arrived, he would start with the mosque, pray two rak’ahs there, and then sit there.”"
"22","On the authority of Abu Nujaid - Dam al-Nun and Fath al-Jim - Imran bin al-Husayn al-Khuza’i, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a woman from Juhayna came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while she was pregnant as a result of adultery, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed the hadd, so impose it on me. So the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) called her guardian and said: Be kind to her, and if she gives birth, come to me. So he did and the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) ordered her to do so. So she pulled her clothes over her, then he ordered her to be stoned, then he (ﷺ) prayed the funeral prayer over her. Omar said to him: Pray for her, O Messenger of Allah, even though she has committed adultery. He said: She has repented with a repentance that, if it were divided among seventy of the people of Medina, would have sufficed them, and has she found anything better than that she sacrificed herself for Allah Almighty?! “[Muslim]”"
"23","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would love to have two valleys, and nothing would fill his mouth except dust, and Allah would forgive him who repents” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"24","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah Almighty laughs at two men, one of whom kills the other, [both] entering Paradise. This one fights in the way of Allah and is killed, then Allah turns to the killer and he becomes Muslim and is martyred.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"25","On the authority of Abu Malik Al-Harith bin Asim Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Purity is half of faith, and praise be to Allah fills the scale, and Glory be to Allah and praise be to Allah fill - or fill - what is between the heavens and the earth, and prayer is light, charity is proof, patience is light, and the Qur’an is proof for you or against you. “Every person rises in the morning, so one who sells himself, he frees her or ruins her” [Muslim]."
"26","On the authority of Abu Sa’id Saad bin Malik bin Sinan Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with them both: “Some people from the Ansar asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he gave them, then they asked him and he gave them, until he ran out of what he had, and he said to them when he had spent everything with his hand: ‘Whatever good I have, I will not spare it for you. No one has been given a gift better and more extensive than patience.” (Agreed upon)"
"27","On the authority of Abu Yahya Suhaib bin Sinan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “How amazing is the affairs of the believer. His whole affair is good for him, and that is not the case for anyone except the believer. If good befalls him, he gives thanks and it is good for him, and if calamity befalls him he is patient and it is good for him” [Muslim]."
"28","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Prophet (ﷺ) became burdened, he began to be overcome with distress. Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, said: And distressed his father. He said: “There is no distress for your father after today.” When he died, she said: Oh, his father, he responded to a Lord who called upon him. Oh, his father, the Garden of Firdaus, his abode. Oh, to Gabriel, we mourn him. When he was buried, she said Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her: Would you please yourselves to throw dust on the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)? [Al-Bukhari]."
"29","On the authority of Abu Zaid, Osama bin Zaid bin Haritha, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), his beloved one and the son of his beloved, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I sent the daughter of the Prophet (ﷺ) saying: My son was dying, so attend us, so he sent to recite the greeting and say: “To Allah belongs what He takes, and to Him belongs what He gives, and everything with Him has a set term, so be patient and seek reward.” So she sent to him to swear by him. To go to her. So he stood up and with him was Saad bin Ubadah, Muadh bin Jabal, Ubayy bin Ka’b, Zaid bin Thabit, and men, may Allah be pleased with them. He brought the boy to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he made him sit in his lap while his soul was rattling, and his eyes filled with tears. Saad said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: “This is a mercy that Allah Almighty has placed in the hearts of His servants.” And in a narration: “In the hearts of whomsoever He wills of His servants, and Allah only has mercy on those of His servants who are merciful.” (Agreed upon)"
"30","And on the authority of Suhaib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There was a king among those who came before you, and he had a magician. When he grew up, he said to the king: I have grown up, so send me a boy to teach him magic.” So he sent him a boy to teach him, and on his way, when he walked, a monk; when he passed by him he sat and heard his words, and he liked him. When the magician came, he passed by the monk and sat with him, and when the magician came, he would hit him, and he complained. So he went to the monk, and he said: When you fear the magician, say: My family has imprisoned me, and if you fear your family, then say: The magician has imprisoned me. While he was doing that, he came upon a large animal that had detained the people, and he said: Today I know which magician is better, or is the monk better? So he took a stone and said: Oh Allah, if the monk’s order is more beloved to you than the magician’s order, then kill this animal so that the people may move on, so he shot it, killed it, and the people moved on, so he came. The monk told him. The monk said to him: “My son, today you are better than me. Your situation has reached what I see, and you will be tested. If you are tested, do not point to me.” The boy used to heal the blind and the lepers, and heal people from all kinds of diseases. Then a companion of the king who had been blind heard it, and brought him many gifts. He said: “This is all for you if you heal me.” So he said: “I do not heal anyone.” Only Allah Almighty heals anyone. If you believe in Allah, I will pray to Allah and He will heal you. Then believe in Allah Almighty and Allah Almighty will heal him. Then the king came and sat with him as he used to sit. The king said to him: Who restored your sight to you? He said: My Lord. He said: Do you have a Lord other than me? (He said: My Lord and your Lord is Allah. So he took him and continued to torture him until he pointed out the boy, so he came. With the boy, the king said to him: “O my son, your magic has reached such a level that you heal the blind and the leper, and you do and do it.” So he said: “I do not heal anyone, but Allah Almighty heals.” So he took him and continued to torture him until he pointed to the monk. The monk was brought and was told: “Return from your religion.” He refused, so he called for a saw and placed the saw in the joint of his head, so he split it until it split open, then the king’s companion was brought. He was told: Return from your religion, but he refused. So he placed the saw in the middle of his head, and cut it with it until he broke into pieces. Then the boy was brought and told him: Return from your religion, but he refused. So he gave him to a group of his companions and said: Take him to such-and-such a mountain and climb the mountain with him. He said: Oh Allah, protect them with whatever you wish. Then the mountain shook and they fell. He came walking to the king, and the king said to him: What did your companions do? He said: Allah Almighty sufficed me against them, so he gave him to a group of his companions and said: Take him and carry him in Qarqour and take him to the sea, and if he turns away from his religion, otherwise throw him away. So they took him and he said: Oh Allah, suffice me for them with whatever you wish. The ship capsized and they drowned, and he came walking to the king. The king said to him: What did your companions do? He said: Allah Almighty sufficed me against them. Then the king said: Allah Almighty sufficed me against them. You are not my killer until you do what I command you to do. He said: What is it? He said: Gather the people in one level, and crucify me on a trunk, then take an arrow from my quiver, then put the arrow in the bow, then say: In the name of Allah, Lord of the boy, then shoot at me, for if you do that, you will kill me. So he gathered the people in one level, crucified him on a trunk, then took an arrow from his quiver, then put the arrow in the bow, then He said: In the name of Allah, Lord of the boy. Then he shot it, and the arrow fell into his temple, so he put his hand in his temple and died. Then the people said, “We believe in the Lord of the boy.” Then the king came and was told: “Have you seen what you were warning about? By Allah, your warning has come down to you. The people have believed.” So he ordered the grooves to be made at the mouths of the rails, so they were taken and they were set on fire. He said: “Whoever does not turn away from his religion, throw him into it,” or he was told: “Put in.” So they did so until a woman came with a boy of hers, but she hesitated to have sex with her, so the boy said to her: O mother, be patient, for you are upon the truth” [Muslim]."
"31","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) passed by a woman crying at a grave, and he said: “Fear Allah and be patient.” She said: “Stay away from me, for you did not suffer from my calamity” (and she did not know him). So it was said to her: He is the Prophet (ﷺ) so she came to the door of the Prophet (ﷺ) but did not find any gatekeepers with him. She said: I did not know you, and he said: “Patience is only at the first shock” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"32","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah Almighty says: There is no reward for my faithful servant with Me if I take away his chosen one from the people of this world and and he bears it patiently and seeks reward (from Me) except Paradise” [Al-Bukhari]."
"33","And on the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that she asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the plague, and he told her that it was a torment that Allah Almighty sends on whomever He wills, so Allah Almighty made it a mercy for the believers. There is no servant who falls into the plague and stays in his country patiently and seeking reward, knowing that nothing will befall him except what Allah has decreed for him, except that he will have the reward of a martyr.” ((Narrated by) Al-Bukhari).."
"34","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Allah Almighty said: If I test my servant with two beloved ones and he is patient, I will compensate him with Paradise from them” [Al-Bukhari]."
"35","On the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, he said: Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said to me: “Should I not show you a woman from the people of Paradise?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “This black woman came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: I have epilepsy, and I am uncovered, so pray to Allah Almighty for me.” He said: “If you wish, (you) be patient and you will have Paradise, and if you wish, I will pray to Allah Almighty to He will heal you.” She said: Be patient. She said: I am uncovered, so pray to Allah that I do not become uncovered. So he prayed for her. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"36","On the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) narrating a prophet from among the prophets, may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon them. His people beat him and made him bloody, and he was wiping the blood from his face, saying: “O Allah, forgive my people for they do not know” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"37","On the authority of Abu Saeed and Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with them, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “No fatigue, sickness, worry, grief, harm, or distress befalls a Muslim, not even a thorn that pricks him, except that Allah expiates some of his sins because of it” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And “sickness”: illness."
"38","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (ﷺ) and he was unwell, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, you are very unwell. He said: “Yes, I am unwell just as two men among you are.” I said: Is that for you two rewards? He said: “Yes, likewise. No Muslim is afflicted with harm, a thorn or anything above it, except that Allah expiates his bad deeds because of it.” And his sins were removed from him just as a tree sheds its leaves.” (Agreed upon)"
"39","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever Allah intends good for, He will pour from it”: [Al-Bukhari]."
"40","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “None of you should wish for death because of some harm that has befallen him. If he must do so, let him say: O Allah, grant me life as long as life is good for me and let me die if death is good for me” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"41","On the authority of Abu Abdullah Khabbab bin Al-Art, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was leaning against his cloak in the shade of the Kaaba. We said: Will you not seek help for us? Will you not pray for us? He said: Before you, a man would be taken and a hole would be dug for him in the ground and placed in it. Then a saw would be brought and placed on his head, cut into two halves, and combed with iron combs between his flesh and bone. Yet nothing turns him away from his religion, and by Allah, Allah will complete this matter until the rider travels from Sana’a to Hadramaut fearing nothing but Allah and the wolf for his sheep, but you are in a hurry” [Al-Bukhari]."
"42","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) preferred people in the division, so he gave Al-Aqra’ ibn Habis one hundred camels, and he gave Uyaynah ibn Hisn the same, and he gave some of the noble Arabs and preferred them that day in the division. A man said: By Allah, this is an division in which there is no justice, and I do not want the pleasure of Allah in it. I said: By Allah, I will inform the Messenger of Allah. so I went to him and informed him of what he had said. Then his face changed until it looked like silver. Then he said, “Who will be just if Allah and His Messenger do not be just?” Then he said: “May Allah have mercy on Moses. He was hurt more than this, but he was patient.” So I said: “I will certainly not report any matter to him after this.” (Agreed upon)"
"43","And on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If Allah wants good for His servant, He hastens punishment for him in this world, and if Allah wants evil for His servant, He withholds the punishment for his sin from him until he receives his full recompense on the Day of Resurrection.” The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “The greatness of the reward comes with the greatness of the affliction, and if Allah Almighty loves a people, He tests them, so whoever is pleased with Allah’s decree, for him is Allah’s satisfaction, and for him who is displeased with it is Allah’s discontent.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"44","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A son of Abu Talha, may Allah be pleased with him, was complaining, so Abu Talha went out and took the boy, and when Abu Talha returned, he said: What did my son do? Umm Salim, who was the boy’s mother, said: He is as calm as he was, so she brought dinner to him and he had dinner, then he had intercourse with her, and when he finished she said: Bury the boy, and when morning came, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). So he told him, and he said: “Did you have a wedding tonight?” He said: Yes. He said: “Oh Allah, bless them both.” She gave birth to a boy, and Abu Talha said to me: Carry him until you bring him to the Prophet (ﷺ). He sent dates with him, and he said: “Does he have anything with him?” He said: Yes, dates, so the Prophet (ﷺ) took them. So he chewed it, then took it from his mouth and placed it in the boy’s mouth, then palate it and named him Abdullah. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim: A son of Abu Talha bin Umm Sulaym died, and she said to her family, “Do not speak to Abu Talha about his son until I speak to him.” So he came, and she brought dinner to him, and he ate and drank, then she prepared for him the best of what she had done before that. He had intercourse with her, and when she saw that he was satisfied, she said: O Abu Talha, what do you think if a people lent their loaned items to a family and they asked for their naked ones, would they stop them? He said: No, and she said: So count on your son. He said: He became angry, then said: You left me until, when I was stained, you told me about my son?! So he told him what had happened, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “May Allah bless your night.” He said: So she became pregnant. He said, “The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was on a journey and she was with him. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came from a journey, he would not leave it by any means. They approached Medina, and she went into labor, and Abu Talha held on to her, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set off.” He said: Abu says: Talha: You know, Lord, that I like to go out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he goes out, and to enter with him when he enters, and I was overwhelmed by what she saw. Umm Sulaym said: O Abu Talha, I do not find what I used to find. Go, so we went, and labor struck her when they arrived and she gave birth to a boy. My mother said to me: O Anas, no one should breastfeed him until she brings him to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the morning. So when morning came She bore him and took him to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he mentioned the entirety of the hadith"
"45","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The strong man is not the one who fights, but the one who controls himself when angry” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"46","On the authority of Suleiman bin Sarrad, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet (ﷺ) and two men were quarreling with each other, and one of them had his face red and his veins swollen. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I know a word that if he had said it, what he found would have gone away from him. If he had said: I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan, what he found would have gone from him.” He said to the angry man: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan.' (Agreed upon)"
"47","On the authority of Muadh bin Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever suppresses his anger, and is able to unleash it, Allah Almighty will call him before the heads of creation on the Day of Resurrection until He gives him the choice of whichever of the houris he wishes” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"48","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said to the Prophet (ﷺ): Advise me. He said: “Do not get angry,” and he repeated it several times. He said: “Do not get angry.” [Al-Bukhari]"
"49","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The affliction of the believer, male and female, continues in his life, his children, and his wealth until he meets Allah Almighty, and he has no sin upon him” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"50","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Uyaynah ibn Hisn came and came to visit his nephew al-Hurr ibn Qays, and he was one of the people whom Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, was close to. The reciters were the companions of Omar’s council, may Allah be pleased with him, and his consultations, whether they were old or young. Uyaynah said to his nephew: O son of my brother, you have a position with this prince, so ask permission for me to meet him. So he asked for permission, and Omar granted permission. When he entered, he said: Hey, O son of Al-Khattab! By Allah, you do not give us dignity and do not judge us with justice. Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, became so angry that he was about to attack him, and Al-Hurr said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, Allah Almighty said to his Prophet (ﷺ): {Take pardon, command what is right, and turn away from the ignorant} [Al-A’raf: 199]. Indeed, this is one of the ignorant, and by Allah, Omar did not exceed it. When he recited it, he was standing still at the Book of Allah Almighty. [Al-Bukhari]."
"51","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “After me there will be favoritism (atharah) and matters that you will reject! They said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us to do? He said: You will fulfill the right that is upon you, and ask Allah for what is rightfully yours” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"52","On the authority of Abu Yahya Usayd bin Hudayr, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man from the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not use me as you used so-and-so? Then he said: “You will encounter favoritism (atharah) after me, so be patient until you meet me at the Basin” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"53","On the authority of Abu Ibrahim Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on some of his days when he met the enemy, waited until when the sun was setting, he rose up among them and said: “O people, do not wish to meet the enemy, but ask Allah for well-being, so when you meet them, be patient, and know that Paradise is under the shade of swords.” Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “O Allah, the Revealer of the Book and the Sender of the clouds.” The clouds, and the defeater of the parties, defeat them and give us victory over them” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] And Allah grant us success."
"54","The first is on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “Truthfulness leads to righteousness and righteousness leads to Paradise, and a man tells the truth until he is recorded with Allah as a friend, and lying leads to immorality, and immorality leads to Hell, and a man lies until he is recorded with Allah as a liar” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"55","The second: On the authority of Abu Muhammad al-Hasan bin Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): “Leave what doubts you for what does not doubt you, for truth is reassurance, and lying is doubt” [Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and said a good, authentic hadith]."
"56","Third: On the authority of Abu Sufyan Sakhr bin Harb, may Allah be pleased with him, in his long hadith on the story of Heraclius, Heraclius said: What does he command you - meaning the Prophet (ﷺ)? Abu Sufyan said: I said: He says: “Worship Allah alone and do not associate anything with Him, and abandon what your fathers say, and He commands us to pray, to be truthful, to be chaste, and to uphold family ties.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"57","Fourth: On the authority of Abu Thabit, and it is said that Abu Sa`id, and it is said that Abu al-Walid, Sahl bin Hanif, who is Badri, may Allah be pleased with him, said that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever asks Allah, the Almighty, for martyrdom honestly, Allah will grant him the status of martyrs, even if he dies on his bed” [Muslim]."
"58","Fifth: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A prophet from the prophets, may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon them, invaded and said to his people: No man who is married to several wives will follow me. and who wants to build a home for his family but has not yet built it. No one built houses without raising their roofs, and no one bought sheep or offspring while waiting for their children. Then the Prophet approached the village around the time of the Asr prayer or close to that, and he said to the sun: You are commanded and I am commanded, O Allah, withhold it from us, so it was held until Allah granted him victory, so he gathered the spoils, and it came - meaning the fire - to consume them, but it did not consume them, so he said: There is embezzlement (ghulul) among you, so let a man from every tribe pledge allegiance to me. A man’s hand stuck to his hand, and he said: There are slaves among you, so let your tribe pledge allegiance to me. Then the hand of two or three men stuck to his hand, and he said: Among you are the slaves. Then they brought a head like a cow’s head made of gold. He placed it down, and the fire came and consumed it. The spoils were not permissible for anyone before us. Then Allah made the spoils permissible for us when he saw our weakness and inability, so he made them permissible for us.” (Agreed upon)"
"59","Sixth: On the authority of Abu Khaled Hakim bin Hizam, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The two parties to a sale have the option (to cancel) unless they separate. If they are truthful and clear, they will be blessed in their sale, and if they conceal and lie, the blessing of their sale will be erased” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"60","As for the hadiths: The first: On the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, “While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) one day a man appeared to us whose clothes were very white and whose hair was very dark. No traces of travel could be seen on him, and none of us knew him. Until he sat next to the Prophet (ﷺ) and he leaned his knees against the Prophet's knees and placed his palms on the Prophet's thighs and said: O Muhammad, tell me about Islam. He, peace and blessings be upon him: Islam is to bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, to perform prayers, to pay zakat, to fast Ramadan, and to make pilgrimage to the House if you are able to make a way to it. He said, “You have spoken the truth.” We were amazed at him asking him and believing him! He said, “So tell me about faith.” He said, “To believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and the Last Day, and to believe in destiny, its good and its evil.” He said, “You have spoken the truth.” He said, “Then tell me about ihsan.” He said, “To worship Allah as if you see Him, and if you do not see Him, then He sees you.” He said, “Then tell me about the Hour.” He said, “The one asked about it knows no better than the questioner.” He said, “Then tell me about its signs.” He said, “That the female slave will give birth to her mistress, and that you will see the barefoot, naked, destitute shepherds competing in building buildings.” Then he departed, and I stayed for a long time., then said: O Omar, do you know who the questioner was? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: For it is Gabriel who came to you to teach you about your religion” [Muslim]."
"61","The second: On the authority of Abu Dharr Jundub ibn Junada and Abu Abd al-Rahman Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with them, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who said: “Fear Allah wherever you are, and follow a bad deed with a good deed and it will be erased, and treat people with good morals” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"62","Third: On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: “I was behind the Prophet (ﷺ) one day, and he said: “O boy, I teach you the words: “Obey Allah, and He will protect you. Preserve Allah, and you will find Him with you. If you ask, ask Allah, and if you seek help, seek help from Allah, and know that if the nation were to gather to benefit you with anything, they would not benefit you except with something that Allah has ordained for you.” Allah has written it for you, and if they gather to harm you with anything, they will not harm you with anything except with something that Allah has written for you. The pens have been lifted, and the pages have dried.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"63","Fourth: On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: “You do deeds that are more insignificant in your eyes than a hair. We used to consider them during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) among the ruinous things.” [Al-Bukhari] “And he said: The ruinous things are the ruinous ones.”"
"64","Fifth: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Allah Almighty is jealous, and Allah Almighty’s jealousy is when a person does what Allah has forbidden to him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"65","Sixth: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: “Three of the children of Israel: a leper, a bald man, and a blind man. Allah wanted to afflict them, so he sent to them an angel. The leper came, and the angel asked him: What is the thing you desire most? He said: Good colour, good skin, and it will remove from me what people have made me filthy with. So he wiped him, and his filth went away from him.” And he was given a good color. He said: What kind of money do I love to you? He said: Camels - or he said cows - the narrator doubted - so he gave him a pregnant she-camel, so he said: May Allah bless her for you. Then the bald man came, and the angel asked him: What is the thing you desire most? He said: Good hair, and it takes away from me that which people have made me filthy, so he wiped it and it went away and I was given good hair. He said: Which money do I love to you? He said: Cows, so he gave a pregnant cow, and he said, “May Allah bless her for you.” Then the blind man came and said: “Which thing do I love most to you?” He said: “For Allah to restore my sight to me so I can see people.” So He wiped it and Allah restored his sight to him. He said: “Which wealth do I love to you?” He said: “Sheep,” so he gave him a fertile sheep that gives birth. These two (the camel and cow) produced offspring, and this one (the sheep) gave birth. So this one (the leper) had a valley of camels, this one (the bald man) had a valley of cows, and this one (the blind man) had a valley of sheep. Then he came to the leper in his form and appearance, and said to him: A poor man and a wayfarer. My ropes have been cut off on my journey, so today I have no communication except by Allah and then by you. I ask you, by the one who gave you the good colour, the good skin, and money, for a camel with which I can reach my journey. He said: The rights are many. He said: It is as if I know you. Were you not a leper who was filthy by people and poor, so Allah gave you all this. He said: I only inherited this wealth from my ancestors, generation after generation., and he said: If you are a liar, then Allah will make you become what you were. Then the bald man came and said to him the same as what he said to this man, and he responded to him the same as he responded, so he said: If you are a liar, then Allah will make you become what you were. Then the blind man came in his form and appearance and said: A poor man and a wayfarer. My ropes were cut off during my journey, so I have no way to reach my destination today except by Allah and then by you. I ask you by the One who restored your sight to give me a sheep with which I can complete my journey? He said: I was blind and Allah restored my sight, so take what you want and leave what you want. By Allah, I have not burdened you today with something that you took for Allah Almighty. He said: “Keep your money for yourself, for you have only been tested. Allah has been pleased with you, and displeasure with your two companions” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"66","Seventh: On the authority of Abu Ya’la Shaddad bin Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “The prudent one is he who holds himself accountable and works for what comes after death, and the helpless is he who follows his soul’s whims and makes presumptuous demands of Allah” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"67","Eighth: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Part of the goodness of a person’s Islam is that he abandons what does not concern him” [A good hadith narrated by Al-Tirmidhi and others]"
"68","The ninth: On the authority of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: ""A man should not be asked why he beat his wife."" (Narrated by Abū Dāwūd and others)."
"69","As for the hadiths, the first: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the most honorable of people? He said: “The most pious of them.” They said: We are not asking you about this. He said: “So Joseph is the Prophet of Allah, son of the Prophet of Allah, son of the Prophet of Allah, son of Khalil Allah.” They said: We are not asking you about this. He said: “So are you asking me about the lineage of the Arabs? They were the best in pre-Islamic times and the best in Islam if they understood it.” (Agreed upon)"
"70","The second: On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “The world is beautiful and green, and Allah has appointed you as successor in it and will see how you do, so fear the world and fear women, for the first temptation of the Children of Israel was with women” [Muslim]."
"71","Third: On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to say: “O Allah, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity, and wealth” [Muslim]."
"72","Fourth: On the authority of Abu Zarif Adi bin Hatim Al-Tai, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Whoever takes an oath and then sees that he is more fearful of Allah than it, let him attain piety” [Muslim]."
"73","Fifth: On the authority of Abu Umamah Siddi bin Ajlan al-Bahili, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivering a sermon during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he said: Fear Allah, pray your five (daily obligatory prayers), fast your month, pay the zakat on your wealth, and obey your leaders, and you will enter the Paradise of your Lord. [Tirmidhi, who said: This is a good and authentic hadith.]"
"74","The first is on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: The nations appeared before me, and I saw the Prophet and with him a group, and the Prophet and with him one and two men, and the Prophet and no one with him, when a great crowd of people was shown to me, so I thought they were my nation, and I was told: This is Moses and his people, but look at the horizon. So I looked and saw a great crowd, and I was told: Look at the other horizon, and there was a great crowd. To me: This is your nation, and with them are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without judgment or punishment. Then he got up and entered his house. The people discussed those who will enter Paradise without judgment or punishment. Some of them said: Perhaps they are those who accompanied the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Some of them said: Perhaps they are those who were born in Islam, but they did not associate anything with Allah - and they mentioned things - so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out to them and said: “What are you delving into?” So they told him, and he said: “They are the ones who do not perform ruqyah (spiritual healing) on others, do not seek ruqyah from others, and do not believe in superstitious omens, but they put their trust in their Lord.” So Ukasha bin Muhsin stood up and said: “Pray to Allah to make me one of them,” so he said: “You are one of them.” Then another man stood up and said: “Pray to Allah to make me one of them,” so he said: “Ukasha beat you to it.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"75","The second: On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: “O Allah, to You I have submitted, and in You I have believed, and in You I have put my trust, and to You I return, and in You I have disputed. O Allah, I seek refuge in Your glory, there is no god but You, that you should lead me astray. You are the Living One who does not die, and the jinn and humans die” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. [This is the wording of Muslim, and Al-Bukhari summarized it.]"
"76","Third: On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he also said: “Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs. Abraham, (ﷺ) (ﷺ) said it when he was thrown into the fire, and Muhammad, (ﷺ) (ﷺ) said it when they said: The people have gathered against you, so fear them, so it increased their faith, and they said: Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs: [Al-Bukhari]."
"77","Fourth: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “There will enter Paradise a people whose hearts are like the hearts of birds” [Muslim]."
"78","Fifth: On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that he went on a campaign with the Prophet (ﷺ) before Najd. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) closed, he withdrew with them, and the tribe overtook them in a valley full of biters, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) descended, and the people dispersed to take shade in the trees. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) descended under a tree and hung his sword on it. We slept, and then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called us. And when a Bedouin was with him, he said: “This is my sword drawn while I was asleep, so I woke up and it was drawn in his hand. He said: Who will protect you from me? I said: Allah - three times.” He did not punish him and sat down. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration: Jabir said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in Dhat ar-Riqa': So, if We came to a shady tree that we left for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and a man of the polytheists came, and the sword of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was hanging from the tree. He drew it and said: Are you afraid of me? He said: No. He said: Who will protect you from me? He said: Allah. And in the narration of Abu Bakr al-Ismaili in his Sahih: He said: Who will protect you from me? He said: Allah. He said: Then the sword fell from his hand, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took the sword and said: Who will protect you from me? He said: Be the best taker. He said: Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but I promise you that I will not fight you nor will I be. With a people fighting you, so he was released, and he came to his companions and said: I came to you from the best of people."
"79","Sixth: On the authority of Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “If you had put your trust in Allah as you should, He would have provided for you just as He provides for birds."
"80","Seventh: On the authority of Abu Amara Al-Baraa bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O so-and-so, when you go to your bed, say: Oh Allah, I surrender myself to You, and turn my face to You: I entrust my affairs to You, and I turn my back to You, out of desire and fear for You. There is no refuge or refuge from You except in You. I believe in Your Book which You have revealed, and in Your Prophet who You were sent, for if you die during that night, you will die according to your nature, and if you die in the morning, you will achieve good.” (Agreed upon)"
"81","Eighth: On the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Amer bin Omar bin Ka’b bin Saad bin Taym bin Murrah bin Ka’b bin Luay bin Ghalib Al-Qurashi Al-Taymi, may Allah be pleased with him - and he, his father and his mother were companions, may Allah be pleased with them - he said: I looked at the feet of the polytheists while we were in the cave and they were on our heads, so I said, O Messenger of Allah, if one of them had looked under his feet, he would have seen us. So he said: “What is your opinion, O Abu Bakr, of two, Allah being the third of them?” (Agreed upon)."
"82","Ninth: On the authority of the Mother of the Believers, Umm Salamah, whose name is Hind bint Abi Umayyah Hudhayfah Al-Makhzoumiyah, may Allah be pleased with her, that when the Prophet (ﷺ) left his house, he would say: “In the name of Allah, I put my trust in Allah. Oh Allah, I seek refuge in You lest I go astray or go astray, or be humiliated or humiliated, or be wronged or be wronged, or be ignorant or be ignorant of me.” [An authentic hadith narrated by Abu Dawud, Al-Tirmidhi and others with authentic chains of narration.) ((Al-Tirmidhi said: It is a good and authentic hadith, and this is the wording of Abu Dawud]."
"83","Tenth: On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says - meaning, when he leaves his house -: In the name of Allah, I put my trust in Allah, and there is no power nor strength except in Allah, it will be said to him: You have been guided, you have been sufficed, and you have been protected, and Satan has departed from him.” [Abu Dawud] Al-Tirmidhi said: Hadith Hasan, Abu Dawud added: “So he says - meaning Satan - to another Satan: How can you do with a man who has been guided, sufficient and protected?"
"84","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: There were two brothers during the time of the Prophet (ﷺ) and one of them used to come to the Prophet (ﷺ) and the other used to practice professionally. The professional complained about his brother to the Prophet (ﷺ), so the Prophet said: “Perhaps you will be blessed through him.” [Narrated by al-Tirmidhi with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of Muslim]."
"85","On the authority of Abu Amr, and it was said: Abu Amra Sufyan bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me something about Islam that I will not ask anyone but you about. He said: “Say, ‘I believe in Allah.’ Then be upright” [Muslim]."
"86","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him: He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Approach and repay, and know that none of you will be saved by your action.” They said: “Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Not even me unless Allah covers me with His mercy and bounty” [Muslim]."
"87","The first: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Hasten to do good deeds before tribulations come, which are like the dark parts of the night: a man may be a believer in the morning and an unbeliever in the evening, and a believer in the evening and an unbeliever in the morning, selling his religion for a fleeting gain of this world.” [Muslim]."
"88","The second, on the authority of Abu Saru’ah - by breaking the neglected sin and opening it - Uqba Ibn Al-Harith, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I prayed behind the Prophet (ﷺ) in Medina in the afternoon, so he said his salutations, then he quickly got up and crossed over the people (quickly, stepping over those who were seated) to the rooms of some of his wives. The people were startled by his haste, so he came out to them, and seeing that they were surprised by his speed, he said: “I remembered some gold/silver we had at home, and I feared I would be detained [from distributing it], so I ordered that it be divided.” [Al-Bukhari]. And in a narration by Al-Bukhari: I had left behind some money from charity in the house, but I hated to give it up. [Al-Bukhari] pieces of gold or silver."
"89","Third: On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man said to the Prophet (ﷺ) on the day of Uhud: I saw that if I were killed, where would I be? He said: “In Paradise,” so he threw some dates that were in his hand, then he fought until he was killed. Agreed upon."
"90","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A man came to the Prophet and said: O Messenger of Allah, which charity has the greatest reward? He said: “To give alms when you are healthy and stingy, fearing poverty and hoping for wealth, and not delaying until when you reach the throat, you said to so-and-so and to such-and-such, and it was to so-and-so.” Agreed upon."
"91","Fifth: On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took a sword on the day of Uhud and said: “Who will take this from me?” So they spread out their hands, and each one of them said: “It is me.” He said: “So who will take it by his right?” The people hesitated, and Abu Dujana, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I will take it by his right. So he took it and split open the heads of the polytheists with it. [Muslim]."
"92","Sixth: On the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adi, who said: We came to Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, and we complained to him about what we were seeing from the pilgrims. He said: “Be patient, for there will not come a time without another worse than it until you meet your Lord.” I heard it from your Prophet (ﷺ). [Al-Bukhari]."
"93","Seventh: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Hasten to do seven deeds. Are you waiting for anything but forgotten poverty, or overwhelming wealth, or a corrupting disease, or ruined old age, or imminent death, or the Antichrist, an absent and waiting evil, or the Hour, for the Hour is worse and more bitter!” [Al-Tirmidhi] He said: It is a good hadith"
"94","Eighth: On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said on the day of Khaybar: “I will give this banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, may Allah grant victory at his hands.” Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I had never desired leadership except at that very moment, so I rushed forward for it hoping that I would be called to it. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and he gave it to him and said: “Walk and do not turn around.” Until Allah gives you victory.” So Ali walked for a while, then stood up and did not turn around, so he shouted: O Messenger of Allah, for what should I fight people? He said: “Fight them until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. If they do that, then they have withheld from you their blood and their wealth except by right, and their reckoning is with Allah.” [Muslim]: (14)"
"95","The first: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah Almighty said: Whoever is hostile to a friend of Mine, I have declared war upon him. My servant does not draw near to Me with anything more beloved to Me than what I have made obligatory upon him, and My servant continues to draw near to Me with voluntary acts of worship until I love him. If I love him, I will be his hearing with which he hears, his sight with which he sees, and his hand with which he strikes. And his foot with which he walks, and if he asks Me, I will give him; and if he seeks My refuge, I will grant him refuge.” [Al-Bukhari]"
"96","The second: On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) in what he narrated on the authority of his Lord Almighty, he said: “If a servant draws near to Me by a span, I draw near to him by a cubit, and if he draws near to Me by a cubit, I draw near to him by a length, and if he comes to Me walking, I come to him at a trot” [Al-Bukhari]."
"97","Third: On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There are two blessings of which many people are neglected: health and free time” [Al-Bukhari]."
"98","Fourth: On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to get up during the night until his feet were swollen and cracked, and I said to him: Why did you do this, O Messenger of Allah, and Allah has forgiven you for your past and future sins?! He said: “Should I not like to be a grateful servant?” (Agreed upon. This is the wording of Al-Bukhari, and similar narrations in the Two Sahihs) Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah).."
"99","Fifth: On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: “When the ten days (of Dhul Hijjah) began, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would revive the night, wake up his family, gird himself and tighten his waist wrapper” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"100","Sixth: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A strong believer is better and more beloved to Allah than a weak believer and in everything is good. Strive for what will benefit you, and seek help from Allah and do not be helpless. And if something befalls you, do not say: If I had done such and such, it would have been such and such, but say: Allah decreed, and what He willed, He did; for if you do, you will open the work of Satan.” [Muslim]."
"101","Seventh: On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Hell is obscured by desires, and Paradise is obscured by hardships” (Agreed upon)."
"102","Eighth: On the authority of Abu Abdullah Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (ﷺ) one night, and he opened Al-Baqarah, so I said, “He should bow at the hundred,” and then he went on. So I said he should pray it in one rak’ah, so he went on. So I said he should kneel with it, then he opened Surah An-Nisa, and recited it. So he recited it, then he opened with Al Imran and recited it, reciting slowly. If he came across a verse that contained praise, he glorified Allah, and if he came across a verse of supplication, he supplicated, and if he came across a verse of seeking refuge, he sought refuge. Then he bowed and began to say: “Glory be to my Lord the Great,” so his bowing was similar to his standing, then he said: “Allah hears those who praise Him. Our Lord, praise be to You.” Then he stood for a long time, close to what he bowed, then He prostrated and said: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.” So his prostration was close to his standing” [Muslim]."
"103","Ninth: On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (ﷺ) one night, and he kept standing for so long that I was thinking of doing something bad! It was said: And what was I thinking about? He said: I was thinking of sitting down and leaving him. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"104","The tenth, on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who said: “The dead are followed by three things: his family, his money, and his work; two will return and one remains: his family and money will return, and his work will remain” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"105","Eleventh: On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Paradise is closer to one of you than the straps of his sandals, and Hell is like that” [Al-Bukhari]."
"106","Twelfth: On the authority of Abu Firas Rabi’ah bin Ka’b Al-Aslami, the servant of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and one of the people of Suffah, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: “I was spending the night with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and I came to him for his ablution and his need, and he said: ‘Ask me.’ I said: I ask you to accompany you in Paradise. He said: “Or other than that?” “That?” I said: “It is that.” He said: “So help yourself with many prostrations” [Muslim]."
"107","Thirteenth: On the authority of Abu Abdullah - and it is said: Abu Abdul Rahman - Thawban, the client of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “You should prostrate a lot, for you will not prostrate to Allah except that Allah will raise you a degree because of it, and remove a sin from you because of it.” [Muslim]."
"108","Fourteenth: On the authority of Abu Safwan Abdullah bin Basr al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The best of people are those who live long and do good deeds” [Narrated by al-Tirmidhi, and he said: a good hadith. “Bisr”: with the addition of the ya and the omitted s]."
"109","Fifteenth: On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: My uncle Anas Ibn al-Nadr, may Allah be pleased with him, was absent from the battle of Badr, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, I was absent from the first fight that you fought against the polytheists. If Allah made me witness in fighting the polytheists, Allah would show what I will do. When it was the day of Uhud the Muslims were exposed, he said, O Allah, I apologize to you for what these people did - meaning his companions - and I disavow before you what these people did - meaning the polytheists - then he went forward, and Saad bin Muadh met him. He (Anas) said: O Saad bin Muadh, by the Lord of the Kaaba, Paradise, I smell its scent without anyone else. Saad said: I could not, O Messenger of Allah, what he did! Anas said: We found on him eighty-some wounds with a sword, or stab wounds with a spear, or shot with an arrow, and we found him killed and the polytheists mutilated him, so no one recognized him except his sister by his fingertips. Anas said: We saw or We believe that this verse was revealed about him and those like him: “Among the believers are men who are true to what they covenanted with Allah” [Al-Ahzab: 23] and so on. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"110","Sixteenth: On the authority of Abu Masoud Uqba bin Amr Al-Ansari Al-Badri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the verse on charity was revealed, we were carrying on our backs. Then a man came and gave a lot of charity in charity, and they said: A hypocrite, and another man came and gave in charity a saa’, and they said: Indeed, Allah has no need of this saa'! So the verse was revealed: [Al-Tawbah: 79]. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"111","Seventeenth: On the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Dharr Jundub bin Junada, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) in what is narrated on the authority of Allah, Blessed and Most High, that he said: “O My servants, I have forbidden injustice to Myself and made it forbidden among you, so do not oppress one another. O My servants, all of you are astray except those whom I guide; so seek guidance from Me.” I guide you. O My servants, all of you are hungry except those whom I have fed. So seek food from Me and I will feed you. O My servants, all of you are naked except for those whom I have clothed, so seek clothing from Me and I will clothe you. O My servants, you err by night and by day, and I forgive all sins, so ask forgiveness from Me and I will forgive you. O My servants, you will never be able to harm Me so as to harm Me, and you will never be able to benefit Me so as to benefit Me. O My servants, if only The first of you and the last of you, the human of you and the jinn of you, were as pious as the most pious heart of any one of you. That would not increase My kingdom anything, O My servants. If only the first of you and the last of you were. And your humans and your jinn were as ungodly as the most ungodly heart of a single man, that would not decrease My dominion in the slightest. O My servants, if the first of you and the last of you, the human of you and your jinn, were to stand on one level and ask of Me and I gave every human being what he asked for, that would not decrease what I have any more than a needle decreases what is put into the sea. O My servants. It is only your deeds that I count for you, then I will repay you for them. Whoever finds good should praise Allah, and whoever finds other than that should blame no one but himself.” Saeed said: Whenever Abu Idris narrated this hadith, he would kneel down. [Muslim] (20)"
"112","As for the hadiths, the first: on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “Allah excuses a person whose term (of death) is deferred until he reaches sixty years of age.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"113","The second: On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to bring me in with the sheikhs of Badr, and it was as if some of them found it within themselves and said: Why did this one enter with us when we have sons like him? So Omar said: He is from where you know! So he called me one day and brought me in with them, and I did not see that he invited me that day except to show them. He said: What do you say about the words of Allah Almighty: {When there comes the victory of Allah and the conquest?) [Victory: 1] Some of them said: We are commanded to thank Allah and seek His forgiveness when He grants us victory and conquest over the enemy. Some of them remained silent and did not say anything. So he said to me: Is that what you say, O Ibn Abbas? I said: No. He said, so what do you say? I said: It is the term of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He (the Prophet) had informed him of it. He said: {When Allah's victory and conquest come} and that is a sign of your term {so glorify the praise of your Lord and ask His forgiveness for indeed He is ever Accepting of repentance} [Al-Fath: 3] Then Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I do not know of her except what she says. [Al-Bukhari]."
"114","Third: On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not pray a prayer after {When Allah’s victory and conquest came} was revealed to him except that he said in it: “Glory be to You, our Lord, and with Your praise, O Allah, forgive me” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration in the Two Sahihs “from her: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was And (ﷺ) often said in his bowing and prostration: “Glory be to You, O Allah, our Lord, and with Your praise, O Allah, forgive me.” He interprets the Qur’an. And in a narration by Muslim: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to often say before he died: “Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You.” Aisha said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? The words that I see you saying? He said: “It has been made for me a sign among my nation (through the revelation of Surah An-Nasr). When I saw it, I said it, ‘When Allah’s victory and conquest come’ until the end of the surah.” And in his narration: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to often say: “Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him. I seek forgiveness from Allah and turn to Him in repentance.” She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah! I see you saying a lot: Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him. Do I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him? He said: “My Lord told me that I will see a sign in my nation. If I see it, I often say: Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him, I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him. I have seen it: {When the victory of Allah and the conquest comes} the conquest of Mecca, {and I see people entering into the religion of Allah in droves. So glorify the praise of your Lord and ask His forgiveness. Indeed, He is ever Accepting of repentance"
"115","Fourth: On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Allah Almighty continued to send revelation to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) until his death, and most of the revelation had been sent down before that. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"116","Fifth: On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Every servant will be resurrected in what he died in.” [Muslim]."
"117","The first: On the authority of Abu Dharr Jundub bin Junada, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best? He said: “Belief in Allah and jihad in His cause.” I said: Which slaves are best? He said: “The most precious ones are with their owners, and the most valuable.” I said: If I don’t do it? He said: “You assist a skilled worker or you make them.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if you are weak in some work? He said: Refrain from doing evil to the people, for it is a charity from you towards yourself. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"118","The second: On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “In the morning, every joint of each of you has a charity due on it,, so every tasbihah is a charity, every tahmidah is a charity, every tahlila is a charity, every takbeer is a charity, enjoining what is right is a charity, and forbidding what is evil is a charity, and two rak’ahs that he offers in the forenoon (duha) are sufficient for that.” [Muslim] Al-Salami, by adding the neglected sīn, lightening the lam, and opening the mim: the joint."
"119","The third, on his authority, said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “The good and bad deeds of my nation were presented to me, and I found in the good deeds of their deeds the dirt removed from the road, and I found in the bad deeds the spittle (phlegm) that is in the mosque and not buried” [Muslim]."
"120","The fourth from him: that people said: O Messenger of Allah, the wealthy people have taken the rewards (for their good deeds), they pray as we pray, they fast as we fast, and they give in charity with the excess of their money. He said: “Has not Allah given you what you give in charity? Indeed, for every tasbihah there is a charity, and every takbeer is a charity, and every praise is a charity, and every tahlila is a charity, and enjoining what is right is a charity, and forbidding what is evil is a charity, and there is charity in the private part of each of you (i.e., lawful marital relations with one's spouse). They said: O Messenger of Allah, can one of us fulfill his desire and have a reward for it?! He said: “Do you not think that if he did it in a forbidden thing, would he be burdened with sin? Likewise, if he did it in a lawful thing, he would have a reward” [Muslim]."
"121","Fifth: On his authority, the Prophet (ﷺ) said to me: “Do not despise any act of kindness, even if it is meeting your brother with an open face” [Muslim]."
"122","Sixth: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A charity is due on every person. Every day the sun rises, it is a charity. To act justly between the two of them is a charity. To help a man with his animal and carry him on it, or lift his belongings onto it is a charity. A kind word is a charity. Every step you take towards prayer is a charity. Removing harmful things from the road is a charity.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. It was also narrated by Muslim from the narration of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “He created every human being from the children of Adam with three hundred and sixty joints. So whoever glorifies Allah, praises Allah, glorifies Allah, glorifies Allah and seeks forgiveness from Allah, removes a stone from the people’s path or a thorn or a bone from the people’s path, or enjoins a good deed or He forbade evil, numbering three hundred and sixty, for that day will come and his soul will be removed from the Fire.”"
"123","Sixteenth: On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever prays Al-Bardain will enter Paradise” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"124","Eighth: On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O Muslim women, do not despise a neighbor to her neighbor, even if it is the hoof of a sheep” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"125","Ninth: On his authority, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Faith is seventy branches, or sixty branches: the best of which is saying there is no god but Allah, and the least of which is removing harm from the way, and modesty is a branch of faith” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"126","The tenth: On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “While a man was walking on a road, he became very thirsty. He found a well, so he went down into it and drank. Then he came out and found a dog panting and eating dirt due to thirst. The man said: This dog was as thirsty as I had been. So he went down to the well and filled his sandals with water, then held it in his mouth until he rose and gave the dog water to drink. So Allah thanked him and forgave him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, do we have a reward for animals? He said: There is a reward for every moist liver” (Agreed upon)."
"127","Eleventh: On his authority, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “I saw a man turning around in Paradise at a tree he cut down on the back of the road that was harming Muslims.” [Muslim]. And in a narration: A man passed by a branch of a tree on the back of a road and said: By Allah, I will move this away from the Muslims so that it does not harm them, so he was admitted to Paradise. And in a narration: To them: While a man was walking on a road, he found a thorn branch on the road, so he removed it, and Allah thanked him for it and forgave him."
"128","Twelfth: On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, then comes to the Friday prayer, and listens and listens, will be forgiven for what comes between that time and the Friday prayer, and an additional three days, and whoever touches a pebble has committed negligence” [Muslim]."
"129","Thirteenth: It is narrated from him that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If a Muslim servant or believer performs ablution and washes his face, every sin that he looked at with his eyes comes out of his face with the water, or the last drop of water, and if he washes his feet, every sin that his feet walked on comes out with the water or with the last drop of water until he comes out clean of sins” [Muslim]."
"130","Fourteenth: On his authority, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “The five daily prayers, Friday to Friday, and Ramadan to Ramadan are expiations for what comes between them if the major sins are avoided” [Muslim]."
"131","Fifteenth: On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Shall I not inform you of what Allah erases sins with and raises ranks?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “Performing ablution in difficult times, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer, for that is the bond” ([Muslim].."
"132","Seventh: On his authority, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “Whoever goes to the mosque in the morning or goes, Allah will prepare for him a place in Paradise whenever he goes in the morning or go.” (Agreed upon)."
"133","Seventeenth: On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If a servant becomes ill or travels, the same as what he used to do as a healthy resident will be recorded for him” [Al-Bukhari]."
"134","Eighteenth: On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Every good deed is charity” [Narrated by Al-Bukhari, and narrated by Muslim from the narration of Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him]."
"135","Nineteenth: On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is no Muslim who plants a tree except that whatever he eats from it is a charity for him, and whatever he steals from it is a charity for him, and no one harms him (or takes from it by force) except it is charity for him” [Narrated by Muslim.] And in his narration: “There is no Muslim who plants a plant except that any human or animal that eats from it is charity for him.” A bird, but it will be a charity for him until the Day of Resurrection.” And in his narration: “There is no Muslim who plants a tree or sows crops except that any person, animal, or thing that eats from it is charity for him.” And it was all narrated from the narration of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him."
"136","Twenty: On his authority, he said: Banu Salamah wanted to move near the mosque, and that was reported to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said to them: “I have heard that you want to move near the mosque?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, we wanted that. He said: “Bani Salamah, your homes are recorded. Your homes are written. Your traces are written.” (Narrated by: Muslim).."
"137","Twenty-one: On the authority of Abu al-Mundhir, Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I know no man farther from the mosque than him, and whose prayer was not missed, so it was said to him, or I said to him: If you bought a donkey, you could ride it in the dark and in the scorching heat (sun), and he said: I would not be happy if my house was next to the mosque, for I want my walk to the mosque and my return to be recorded for me when I return to my family, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said. He said: “Allah has gathered all of that for you” [Muslim]."
"138","Twenty-two: On the authority of Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Forty noble qualities, the highest of which is the generosity of a goat (i.e., giving charity freely as a goat provides milk). Any servant who practices one of them hoping for its reward and believing in its promise will be admitted by Allah into Paradise.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"139","Twenty-third: On the authority of Adi bin Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: “Fear the Fire, even if it is half a date” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in their narration from him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is not one of you except that his Lord will speak to him, with no interpreter between him and him.” He looks to his right and sees nothing but what he has sent forward (of good deeds), and he looks to his left and sees nothing but what he has sent forward. He looks between his hands and sees nothing but the Fire in front of his face, so avoid the Fire even if it is with half a date, and whoever does not find it, then with a kind word.”"
"140","Twenty-fourth: On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah is pleased with a servant if he eats a meal and praises Him for it, or drinks a drink and praises Him for it” [Muslim]."
"141","Twenty-fifth: On the authority of Abu Mus, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Every Muslim must pay charity.” He said: What if he cannot find? He said: What if he cannot? He said: “He helps the needy and anxious.” He said: What if he cannot? He said: “He enjoins what is right or “Goodness.” He said: “What do you think if he does not do it?” He said: “He abstains from evil, for it is charity.” (Agreed upon)"
"142","- On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (ﷺ) entered upon her and a woman was with her. He said: Who is this? She said: This is so-and-so who is known for her prayers. He said: “Do what you are able to do, for by Allah, Allah does not tire until you tire.” And the most beloved religion to him was what its owner persevered in it. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"143","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Three people came to the homes of the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) asking about the worship of the Prophet (ﷺ). When they were informed, it was as if it was said to them, and they said: Where are we with regard to the Prophet (ﷺ) for Allah has forgiven him, both his earlier and later sins? One of them said: As for me, I will pray all night long. The other said: I will fast forever and never break the fast. The other said: I will isolate myself. I will never marry women, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to them and said: “Are you the ones who said such and such?! By Allah, I am the most Allah-fearing and most pious of you, but I fast and break my fast, pray and sleep, and I marry women. Whoever turns away from my Sunnah is not of me” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"144","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Those who go to extremes (in religion) will perish.” He said it three times [Muslim]"
"145","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “Religion is easy, and religion will not be difficult without it being overpowered, so repay, approach, and give good tidings, and seek help in the morning and in the morning, and some of the deep” [Al-Bukhari]. And in his narration: Repay, and approach, and in the morning, and depart, and some of the deep, The intention is to achieve..."
"146","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) entered the mosque and saw a rope stretched between the two poles. He said: “What is this rope?” They said: This is Zainab’s rope, so if she becomes tired, she clings to it. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said, “Untie it, so that one of you may pray with energy, and when he tires, let him rest.” (Agreed upon)"
"147","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If one of you becomes sleepy while praying, let him lie down until sleep goes away, for if one of you prays while he is sleepy and does not know it, perhaps he will go and ask for forgiveness and curse himself” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"148","On the authority of Abu Abdullah Jaber bin Samra, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: “I used to pray the prayers with the Prophet (ﷺ) and his prayer was moderate (in length) and his sermon was moderate (in length)” [Muslim]."
"149","On the authority of Abu Juhaifah Wahb bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) made Salman and Abu Darda’ a brother. So Salman visited Abu Darda’, and he saw Umm Al-Darda’ dressed and said: What is your business? She said: Your brother Abu Darda’ has no need in this world, so Abu Darda’ came and prepared food for him, and said to him: Eat, for I am fasting. He said: I will not even eat. She ate, and he ate, and when the night came, Abu Darda went to get up and said to him: Sleep, so he slept, then he went to get up and said to him: Sleep, and at the end of the night Salman said: Get up now, so they all prayed, and Salman said to him: Your Lord has a right over you, and your soul has a right over you, and your family has a right over you, so give each one who has a right his right, so he came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him, so the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him. “Salman has spoken the truth,” he said [Al-Bukhari]."
"150","On the authority of Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) told me that I say: By Allah, I will fast during the day, and I will pray at night as long as I live. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Are you the one who says that? So I said to him: I said it by my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “You cannot do that, so fast, break your fast, and sleep.” And stand up, and fast for three days of the month, for a good deed is multiplied tenfold, and that is like fasting for a lifetime.” I said: “I am able to do better than that.” He said: “So fast one day and break my fast for two days.” I said: “I am able to do better than that.” He said: “So fast one day and break my fast another day. That is the fasting of David (ﷺ) and it is the most just of fasts.” And in a narration: “And it is the best of fasts.” So I said: “I can do better than that.” Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is nothing better than that.” And for me to have accepted the three days that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, is dearer to me than my family and what I have. And in a narration: “Have I not been told that you fast during the day and pray at night?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “So do not do: fast and break your fast, and sleep and stand up, for your body has a right over you, and your eyes have a right over you, and your husband has a right over you, and your visitor has a right over you, and if it is sufficient for you to fast three days every month, then for every good deed you will get ten times the same, for that is fasting for a lifetime.” So I stressed and he stressed me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am finding strength. He said: “Fast as the Prophet of Allah David did and do not do more.” “I said: What was David’s fast? He said: “Half a lifetime.” Then Abdullah used to say after he grew up: “I wish I had accepted the permission of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).” And in a narration: “Did I not tell you that you fast for a lifetime and recite the Qur’an every night?” So I said: Yes, O. Messenger of Allah, and I did not want anything but good by that. He said: “So fast the fast of the Prophet of Allah, David, for he was the most devout of people, and recite the Qur’an every month.” I said: “O Prophet of Allah, am I able to do better than that?” He said: “So recite it in every twenty.” I said: O Prophet of Allah, can I be able to do better than that? He said: “So recite it in every ten” I said: O Prophet of Allah, can I bear anything better than that? He said: “So recite it every seven days and do not do more than that.” I stressed, and he stressed me, and the Prophet (ﷺ) said to me: “You do not know, perhaps your life will be prolonged.” He said: So I went to what the Prophet (ﷺ) told me. When I grew up, I wished that I had accepted the permission of the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ). And (ﷺ). And in a narration: “And your child has a right over you.” And in a narration: “No one who has fasted forever” fasts three times. And in a narration: “The most beloved of fasting to Allah Almighty is the fasting of David, and the most beloved of prayers to Allah Almighty is the prayer of David: He would sleep half the night, stand up for a third of it, and sleep a sixth of it. He would fast one day and break his fast the next, and would not flee if He met him. And in a narration: My father married a woman of good standing, and he used to meet his daughter-in-law - that is, the wife of his son - and he would ask her about her husband, and she would say to him: What a good man, from a man who has not laid on a bed for us or searched for us since we came to him. When this took a long time with him, he mentioned that to the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said: “Go with him.” So I met him after that. He said: “How do you fast?” I said: “Every day.” He said: “And how do you complete it?” I said: “Every night.” He mentioned something similar to the above. He used to recite to some of his family the seven that he recited, offering it during the day so that it would be easier for him at night. If he wanted to gain piety, he would break his fast for days and count them, and fast as many as they did, out of fear of leaving out anything that the Prophet (ﷺ) had left behind. All of these narrations are authentic, most of them in the two Sahih books. And a little of it in one of them..."
"151","On the authority of Abu Rabi Hanzala bin Al-Rabi’ Al-Asidi, the writer, one of the writers of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, told me, and he said: How are you, Hanzala? I said: Hanzala is a hypocrite? I said: Hanzala is a hypocrite (He said: Glory be to Allah, what do you say? (I said: We will be with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)). And (ﷺ) reminds us of Paradise and Hell as if they are our own eyes. When we leave the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and attend to our wives, children, and estates, we forget a lot. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: By Allah, we will encounter something like this. So Abu Bakr and I set off until we entered upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). I said: Hanzala is a hypocrite, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “And what is that?” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you, you remind us of Hell and Paradise as if it is what we see with our own eyes. If we leave you and attend to our wives, children, and farms, we forget a lot.” So the Messenger of Allah said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you continued as you are with me and in remembrance, the angels would shake hands with you on your beds and on your paths, but, O Hanzala, it is an hour.” And an hour"" three times, [Muslim].."
"152","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: While the Prophet (ﷺ) was giving a sermon, he saw a man standing. He asked about him, and they said: Abu Israel vowed to stand in the sun and not sit, not take shade, not speak, and fast. So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Tell him to speak and let him take shade and sit and complete his fast” [Al-Bukhari]."
"153","On the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever sleeps and misses his portion of Qur'an recital at night, or something from it, and recites it between the dawn prayer and the noon prayer, it will be recorded for him as if he had read it at night” [Muslim]."
"154","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: O Abdullah, do not be like so-and-so. He used to pray the night prayer, but he abandoned the night prayer” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"155","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: If the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) missed prayer at night due to pain or something else, he would pray twelve rak’ahs during the day” [Muslim]."
"156","The first: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Leave me to what I have left you: those who came before you were destroyed by their excessive questioning and their disagreement with their prophets. If I forbid you to do something, avoid it, and if I command you to do something, do as much of it as you can” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"157","The second: On the authority of Abu Najih Al-Irbad bin Sariyah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: “the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) preached to us an eloquent sermon that made hearts tremble and eyes shed tears. We said: O Messenger of Allah, it is as if it were a farewell sermon, so advise us.” He said: “I advise you to fear Allah, and to hear and obey, even if an Ethiopian slave is appointed as a leader over you, and whoever among you lives will see.” There is a lot of disagreement. So you should adhere to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the Rightly Guided Caliphs, biting on it with your molars, and beware of newly invented matters, for every heresy is a misguidance” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"158","Third: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “All of my nation will enter Paradise except those who refuse.” It was said: And whoever refuses, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “Whoever obeys me will enter Paradise, and whoever disobeys me has refused.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"159","Fourth: On the authority of Abu Muslim, and it was said: Abu Iyas Salama bin Amr bin Al-Akwa’, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man ate with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with his left hand, and he said: “Eat with your right hand.” He said: “I cannot.” He said: “I cannot.” The only thing preventing him was pride, so he did not raise it to his mouth. ([Muslim].."
"160","Fifth: On the authority of Abu Abdullah al-Numan bin Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “You will straighten your rows or Allah will discord between your faces” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was straightening our rows to the point that it was as if he was straightening a sword with it, until when he saw that I We learned about him, then he left one day, and he stood until he was about to say the takbir, and he saw a man with his chest exposed, and he said: “Servants of Allah, let your rows be straight or Allah will dissent between your faces.”"
"161","Sixth: On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A house in Medina burned down upon its inhabitants at night, and when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) spoke about them, he said, “This fire is your enemy, so when you sleep, extinguish it from you” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"162","Seventh: On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The likeness of what Allah sent me with of guidance and knowledge is like a rain that struck the land, and a portion of it was good. It accepted water and produced grass and much grass, and among it were low-lying areas that retained water, so Allah benefited the people with them, so they drank from them, watered, and planted. And He struck another portion of it, but they are bottoms that do not hold water and do not grow. That is the example of one who understands the religion of Allah, and benefits him from what Allah has sent me with, so he knows and knows, and the example of one who does not raise his head by that, and does not accept the guidance of Allah with which I was sent” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"163","Eighth: On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The likeness of me and of you is like that of a man who kindled a fire and grasshoppers and moths fall into it while he drove them away from it, and I will take hold of you from the fire, and you will escape from my hand” [Muslim]."
"164","Ninth: On his authority, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded licking the fingers and the dish and said: “You do not know in which of them the blessing is” [Muslim]. And in his narration: “If a bite falls upon one of you, let him take it and remove any dirt that is on it, and let him eat it, and do not leave it for the devil, and let him not wipe his hand with a handkerchief. Until he licks his fingers, he does not know in which food the blessing is.” And in his narration: “The devil is present with one of you at everything that concerns him, until he brings it to his food. If a morsel falls from one of you, let him remove whatever impurity is on it, and let him eat it, and do not leave it for the devil.”"
"165","Tenth: On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood up among us with a sermon and said: “O people, you will be gathered before Allah Almighty, barefooted, naked, and uncircumcised. {Just as We initiated the first creation, We will return it as a promise upon Us. Indeed, We will do it} [Al-Anbiya’: 103] Indeed, the first of creation to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection will be Abraham (ﷺ). Indeed, men from my nation will be brought, and they will be taken to the left. Then I will say: O Lord, my companions. It will be said: You do not know what they did after you. So I will say, as the righteous servant said: {And I was a witness over them as long as I remained among them} until His saying: {The Mighty, the Wise}. [Al-Ma’idah: 117, 118] Then I will be told: ‘They have not ceased to be apostates since I separated from them.’ [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. (46)"
"166","Eleventh: On the authority of Abu Saeed Abdullah bin Mughaffal, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade throwing pebbles and said: “It does not kill the game, nor does it harm the enemy, but it does gouge out an eye and break a tooth” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"167","On the authority of Abis bin Rabi’ah, he said: I saw Omar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, kissing the stone - meaning the black one - and saying: I know that you are a stone that neither benefits nor harms, and had I not seen the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) kissing you, I would not have kissed you. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"168","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When it was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): {To Allah belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth, and whether you reveal what is in yourselves or conceal it, Allah will call you to account for it} (Al-Baqarah: 283) This became more difficult for the companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) so they went to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Then they bowed down on their knees and said: O Messenger of Allah, you have assigned us deeds that are within our power: prayer, jihad, fasting, and charity, and this verse has been revealed to you and we cannot bear it. the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do you want to say as the People of the Book before you said: We heard and disobeyed? Rather, say: We heard and obeyed. Your forgiveness, our Lord. And here is the final destination.” When the people read it and their tongues were moved by it, Allah Almighty revealed after it: {The Messenger believes in what was sent down to him from his Lord, and the believers each believe in Allah and His angels and His books and His messengers. We make no distinction between any of His messengers. And they said, “We hear and we obey. Your forgiveness is our Lord, and to You is the return.”) So when they did that, Allah Almighty abrogated it. Then Allah Almighty revealed: “Allah does not burden a soul except that it is sufficient for it, for it is what it has earned and for it is what it has earned. Our Lord, do not hold us accountable if we forget or make a mistake.” He said: Yes, “Our Lord, and do not place upon us a burden as You placed upon those before us.” He said: “Yes,” “Our Lord, and do not burden us with what we have no strength with.” He said: Yes. On our behalf, and forgive us and have mercy on us, You are our Master, so grant us victory over the disbelieving people.} He said: Yes” [Muslim]."
"169","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever introduces something into this matter of ours that is not part of it will have it rejected” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim: “Whoever does an action that is not in accordance with our matter will have it rejected.”"
"170","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon, his eyes would turn red, his voice would rise, and his anger would become intense, to the point that he was like a warner of an approaching army, saying: “Good morning and good evening,” and saying: “I and this hour have been sent like these,” and he would join his two fingers together. index finger and middle finger, and he says: “As for what follows, the best hadith is the Book of Allah and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad (ﷺ) and the worst of matters are the newly invented matters, and every innovation is a misguidance.” Then he says: “I have more right over every believer than himself. Whoever leaves behind wealth, it goes to its people, and whoever leaves behind a debt or loss, it goes to me and upon me” [Muslim]. On the authority of Al-Irbad bin Sariyah, may Allah be pleased with him, the previous hadith in the chapter on preserving the Sunnah."
"171","On the authority of Abu Amr, Jarir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were at the beginning of the day with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when a naked people came to him, wearing nimars, or cloaks, wearing swords. Most of them were from Mudar, or even all of them were from Mudar. The face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) changed with concern when he saw their destitution. So he entered and then left, and ordered Bilal to give the call to prayer and perform the iqama. He prayed and then delivered a sermon. He said: {O people, fear your Lord, who created you from a single soul} until the end of the verse: {Indeed, Allah is a Watcher over you}, and the other verse at the end of the gathering: {O you who have believed, fear Allah, and let a soul see what it has brought forward for tomorrow} A man gave in charity from his dinar, from a dirham of his garment, from a saa’ of his wheat, from a saa’ of his dates - until he said - Even with a half of a date, a man from the Ansar came with a handful, and his hand almost could not carry it, indeed it could not. Then the people continued until I saw two piles of food and clothes, until I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) beaming as if it were gold-plated, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Whoever establishes a good practice in Islam will have its reward, and the reward of those who act upon it after him without having anything detracted from their rewards. And whoever introduces a bad practice in Islam, he will bear the burden of it and the burden of those who act upon it after him, without diminishing their burden in the least.” [Muslim]"
"172","And on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “There is no soul that is killed unjustly except that the first son of Adam is liable for a measure of its blood because he was the first to institute killing” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"173","On the authority of Abu Masoud Uqba bin Amr Al-Ansari Al-Badi, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever guides to something good will have a reward similar to that of its doer” [Muslim]."
"174","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever calls to guidance will have a reward like the rewards of those who follow him, without that detracting from their rewards in the slightest, and whoever calls for misguidance will bear a sin equal to the sins of those who follow him, without that detracting from their sins in the least.” [Muslim]"
"175","On the authority of Al-Abbas Sahl bin Saad Al-Sa’idi, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said on the day of Khaybar: “Tomorrow I will give the flag to a man at whose hands Allah will give victory, who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love.” So the people spent the night wondering which of them would give it. When the morning came, the people went to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, all of them hoping that he would be given it, so he said: “Where is Ali bin Abi Talib?” It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, he is complaining about his eyes.” He said: “So they sent for him.” He was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) spat in his eyes and prayed for him, and he was healed, as if he had no ailment, so he gave him the standard. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, I will fight them until they are like us? He said: “Proceed on your way until you reach their settlement, then invite them to Islam, and inform them of what is obligatory upon them regarding the right of Allah Almighty. By Allah, for Allah to guide one man through you is better for you than red camels.” (Agreed upon)"
"176","And on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a young man from Aslam said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to fight and I do not have what to prepare with? He said: “Go to so-and-so, for he had prepared (equipment) but fell ill.” So he came to him and said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) greets you and says: Give me what you have prepared. So he said: O so-and-so, give him what you have prepared, and do not withhold anything from him, for Allah, you will not withhold anything from it, and it will be blessed for you. [Muslim]."
"177","On the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman Zaid bin Khalid al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever prepares a fighter for the sake of Allah has fought, and whoever provides for the family of a fighter with goodness has fought” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"178","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent a delegation to the Banu Lahyan from Hudhayl and said: “From every two men, let one of them go forth (on the expedition), and the reward will be between them (both).” [Muslim]."
"179","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) met a group of riders and said: “Who are the people?” They said: “Muslims.” They said: “Who are you?” He said: “Messenger of Allah.” Then a woman raised a young boy to him and said: “Is this a Hajj?” He said: “Yes, and you will be rewarded.” [Muslim]."
"180","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: “The trustworthy Muslim treasurer who does what he is ordered to do, and gives it in full and generously, out of his own goodness, and gives it to the one who ordered it for him, one of the charitable people” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"181","The first: On the authority of Abu Ruqayyah Tamim bin Aws al-Dari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Religion is sincere advice.” We said: To whom? He said: To Allah, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the imams of the Muslims, and to the common people [Muslim]."
"182","Second: On the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to establish prayer, pay zakat, and be sincere to every Muslim. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"183","Third: On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"184","The first: On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Whoever among you sees an evil, let him change it with his hand, and if he is not able to do so, then with his tongue, and if he is not able to do so, then with his heart, and that is the weakest of faith” [Muslim]."
"185","Second: On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is no prophet whom Allah sent to a nation before me but that he had among his nation disciples and companions who follow his Sunnah and follow his command. Then after them there will be successors who say what they do not do and do what they are not commanded. So whoever strives against them with his hand is a believer, and whoever strives against them with his heart is a believer, and whoever strives against them with his tongue is a believer.” And beyond that faith there is not a mustard seed.” [Muslim]."
"186","Third: On the authority of Abu Al-Walid Ubadah bin Al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: “We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on hearing and obeying in hardship and ease, in times of ease and hardship, and that he has the right to prefer some of us over others in shared matters, and that we do not dispute the authority of those appointed to lead us unless you see clear disbelief for which you have clear proof from Allah Almighty, and that we speak the truth wherever we are and do not fear in Allah the blame of a blamer” [Agreed) (on it]."
"187","Fourth: On the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “The example of the one who upholds Allah’s limits and the one who transgresses them is like the example of a people who drew lots for a ship, some of them became at the top of it and some at the bottom of it, and when those at the bottom of it drew from the water, they would pass over those above them and say: ‘If only we had breached our share and did not harm those above us,’ but if they left them and what they wanted, they would perish and be destroyed.” All of them, and if they prevented them from drilling the hole, they would all be saved and they would all be saved.” [Al-Bukhari]"
"188","Fifth: On the authority of the Mother of the Believers, Umm Salamah Hind, daughter of Abi Umayyah Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: “Amirs will be appointed over you, so you recognize and deny. Whoever dislikes is acquitted, and whoever denies is acquitted, but whoever is pleased and follows them” They said: O Messenger of Allah, should we not fight them? He said: “No, the imams have established prayer among you.” [Muslim]."
"189","Sixth: On the authority of the Mother of the Believers, Umm al-Hakam Zainab bint Jahsh, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (ﷺ) entered upon her in fear and said: “There is no god but Allah. Woe to the Arabs because of the evil that has approached. Today there has been an opening from the destruction of Gog and Magog like this.” He circled his thumb and the next. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will the righteous perish while among us? He said: “Yes, if there are many.” Malice"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"190","Seventh: On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “Beware of sitting in the streets.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, we have no choice but to sit (in our usual places). We converse there. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If you refuse except to sit, then give the way its due.” They said: What is the right of the way, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “Lowering the gaze, refraining from harm, returning the greeting, enjoining what is right, and forbidding what is wrong” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"191","Eighth: On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw a gold ring on the hand of a man, so he took it off, threw it away, and said: “One of you goes to an ember of fire and places it in his hand!” So the man was told after the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went: Take your ring; He benefited from it. He said: No, by Allah, I will never take it, for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) threw it. [Muslim]."
"192","Ninth: On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Hasan Al-Basri, that Aidh bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, entered upon Ubayd Allah bin Ziyad and said: My son, I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “The worst of shepherds is the harsh one,” so beware of being one of them. So he said to him: Sit, for you are only one of the bran of the companions of Muhammad (ﷺ). So he said: Did they have bran? It was only bran. After them and others! [Muslim]."
"193","Tenth: On the authority of Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, or Allah will soon send upon you a punishment from Him, and then you will call upon Him and He will not respond to you” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"194","Eleventh: On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “The best jihad is a word of justice before an unjust ruler” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"195","Twelfth: On the authority of Abu Abdullah Tariq bin Shihab Al-Bajli Al-Ahmasi, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man asked the Prophet (ﷺ) while he put his foot in the stirrup: Which jihad is better? He said: “A word of truth before an unjust ruler” [Narrated by Al-Nasa’i with an authentic chain of transmission]."
"196","Thirteenth: On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The first thing that brought deficiency upon the Children of Israel was that a man would meet another man and say, ‘O this one, fear Allah and give up what you are doing, for it is not permissible for you.’ Then he would meet him the next day and he was in his same state, so that did not prevent him from being his companion in eating, drinking, and sitting. So when they did that, Allah struck the hearts of some of them with one another.” Then he said: {Those who disbelieved among the Children of Israel were cursed on the tongue of David and Jesus, son of Mary. That is because they disobeyed and transgressed. They would not refrain from an evil they did. Evil is what they were doing. You will see many of them befriending those who disbelieved, evil is what their souls have presented to them} until His saying: {Disobedient} [Al-Ma’id: 78,81] Then he said: “ No, by Allah, you will enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, and you will seize the hand of the oppressor and you will gently incline him to the truth, and you will strictly restrict him to the truth, or Allah will strike the hearts of some of you against others, and then He will curse you as He cursed them.” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi] This is the wording of Abu Dawud, and the wording of Al-Tirmidhi: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: When the Children of Israel fell into sins, their scholars forbade them, but they did not stop, so they sat with them in their gatherings, and they ate and drank them, so Allah struck the hearts of some of them with one another, and cursed them on the tongue of David and Jesus, son of Mary, because they disobeyed and transgressed. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sat and was reclining and said: No, by the One in whose hand is my soul until Frame them in accordance with the truth. His saying: 'Incline them to the truth' (تأطروهم), meaning to gently guide them to the truth. And 'restrict them to the truth' ("
"197","Fourteenth: On the authority of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: O people, you are reciting this verse: {O you who have believed, you have your own souls. No one who goes astray will harm you if you are guided} [Al-Maeda: 105] And I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “When people see The oppressor, and they did not restrain him, Allah is about to afflict them with a punishment from Him” [Narrated by Abu Dawud, Al-Tirmidhi, and Al-Nasa’i with authentic chains of transmission]."
"198","On the authority of Abu Zaid, Osama bin Zaid bin Haritha, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and thrown into Hell, and the intestines of his stomach will gush out, and he will spin around like a donkey in a millstone. Then the people of Hell will gather around him and say: O so-and-so, what is the matter with you? Didn’t you enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong? And he says: Yes, I used to enjoin what is right and not do it, and forbid what is wrong and do it.” (Agreed upon)"
"199","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The signs of a hypocrite are three: when he speaks, he lies, when he makes a promise, he breaks it, and when he is trusted, he betrays” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"200","On the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) told us two hadiths, one of which I have seen, and I am waiting for the other: He told us that trust was revealed at the root of men’s hearts, and then the Qur’an was revealed and they learned from the Qur’an, and they learned from the Sunnah. Then he told us about removing trustworthiness, and he said: “A man sleeps and trust is taken from his heart, and its effect remains like a wick. So the trust oozes out of his heart, and its trace remains like the trace of a scald, like an embers that you rolled on your foot, and it scalded the foot, and you see the scalded mark but there is nothing (of the coal) left in it. Then he took a pebble and rolled it on his foot. Then the people began to pledge allegiance, and hardly anyone would fulfill the trust until it was said: “Indeed among the children of so-and-so is an honest man, until it is said to the man, ‘How good and pleasant he is, how wise he is!’ and there is not in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith. A time has come and I do not care which of you I have pledged allegiance to. If he is a Muslim, he will return it to his religion, and if he is a Christian or Jew, he will return it to his master, and as for today, I would not give allegiance from you except so-and-so and so-and-so” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"201","On the authority of Hudhayfah and Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with them, they said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah, Blessed and Most High, will gather the people, and the believers will rise until Paradise approaches them. Then they will come to Adam, may Allah’s prayers be upon him, and say: O our father, open Paradise for us. Then he will say: Did I expel you from Paradise except for the sin of your father? I am not the owner of that. Go to my son, Abraham, Allah’s friend. He said: They will come to Abraham, and Abraham will say: I am not the master of that. Go to Moses, to whom Allah spoke verbally. They will come to Moses, and he will say: I am not the master of that. Go to Jesus, the word of Allah and His spirit. Then Jesus will say: I am not the master of that. So they will come to Muhammad (ﷺ) and he will stand up and the permission will be given to him, and trust and mercy will be sent and they will stand up. its sides of the path, right and left, and the first of you passes by like lightning.” I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed. What thing did lightning pass by? He said: “Have you not seen how it passes and returns in the blink of an eye? Then it passes like the wind, then like the birds, and the most powerful of men are their deeds carried out, and your Prophet is standing on the path, saying: ‘O my Lord, grant us peace, peace, until the deeds of the servants are multiplied, until a man comes who cannot walk except by crawling, and on the edges of the path are hanging hooks, commanded to seize whoever they are ordered to. Some are scratched and saved, and some are thrown headfirst into Hell. “By the One in whose hand is Abu Hurairah’s soul, the bottom of Hell will last for seventy years. [Muslim]."
"202","On the authority of Abu Khubayb - with the ḍammah of the ḍā’ al-Mu’jamah - Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: When Al-Zubair stood on the Day of the Camel, he called me and I stood beside him, and he said: O my son, no one will be killed today except an oppressor or an oppressed person, and I do not see myself except that I will be killed today by an oppressor, and one of my greatest concerns is for my religion. Do you think that our religion will leave anything of our money left? Then he said: O my son, sell our money and pay off my debt. He bequeathed one-third of his wealth, and a third of that third to his sons (the sons of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair). He said, “If there is anything left over from our wealth after paying off the debt, then one-third of it is for your children.” Hisham said: Some of Abdullah’s sons had lived with some of the sons of Al-Zubayr, Khabib and Abbad, and he had at that time nine sons and nine daughters. Abdullah said: So he began to advise me of his debt and said: O my son, if you are unable to do anything of it, seek help from him. By my master. He said, by Allah, I did not know what he meant until I said: O father, who is your master? He said: Allah. He said: By Allah, I never fell into distress due to his debt except that I said: O master of Al-Zubayr, pay off his debt, and he repaid it. He said: So Al-Zubayr was killed and he did not leave a dinar or a dirham except two lands, including the forest and eleven houses in the city, and two houses in Basra. and a house in Kufa and a house in Egypt (among his estate). He said: The religion he owed was that a man would bring him money and he would entrust it to him. Then Al-Zubair would say: No, it is a loan; I fear loss for it. He never held any governorship nor was he responsible for collecting jizya, kharaj, or any official duty except participating in campaigns with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) or with Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them. Abdullah said: So I counted what he had. He owed a debt, and I found it to be two thousand and two hundred thousand! Then Hakim bin Hizam met Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr and said: Oh my nephew, how much debt is my brother on? So I silenced him and said: One hundred thousand. Hakim said: By Allah, I don’t see your wealth being sufficient for this! Abdullah said: Did you see if it was one thousand thousand? Two hundred thousand? He said: I don’t see you being able to bear this, if you are unable to do any of it. So seek my help. He said: Al-Zubayr had bought the forest for seventy-one hundred thousand, so Abdullah sold it for one thousand six hundred thousand. Then he stood up and said: Whoever has anything against Al-Zubayr, let him come to us at the forest. Abdullah bin Jaafar came to him, and he had four hundred thousand from Al-Zubayr, and he said to Abdullah: If you wish, I will leave it to you? Abdullah said: No. He said: If you wish, you can make it while you delay. You delay, and Abdullah said: No. He said: So cut a piece for me. Abdullah said: For you from here to here. So Abdullah sold some of it, and paid off his debt, and paid it off, and four and a half shares remained of it. He presented it to Muawiyah, and with him were Amr bin Uthman, Al-Mundhir bin Al-Zubayr, and Ibn Zam’a. Muawiyah said to him: How much was the forest worth? He said: Each share was worth a hundred thousand. He said: How much was left? He said: Four and a half shares. Al-Mundhir Ibn al-Zubayr said: I took a share for a hundred thousand. Amr bin Uthman said: I took a share for a hundred thousand. Ibn Zam’ah said: I took a share for a hundred thousand. Muawiyah said: How much of it is left? He said: A share and a half. He said: I took it for fifty and a hundred thousand. He said: Abdullah bin Jaafar sold his share of it. Muawiyah for six hundred thousand. When Ibn al-Zubayr finished paying off his debt, the sons of al-Zubayr said: Divide our inheritance between us. He said: By Allah, I will not divide it among you until I announce the harvest for four years: Whoever has a debt from al-Zubayr, let him come to us and let us pay it off. So he made a call for the harvest every year, and when four years had passed, he divided it among them and paid a third. Al-Zubayr had four wives, so each wife received 1,200,000, and his total wealth was 50,200,000. [Al-Bukhari]"
"203","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Beware of injustice, for injustice is darkness on the Day of Resurrection, and beware of greed, for greed destroyed those who were before you. It caused them to shed their blood and make lawful their unlawful things” [Muslim]."
"204","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The rights will be given back to their rightful owners on the Day of Resurrection until the hornless sheep is compensated from the horned sheep” [Muslim]."
"205","And on the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: We were talking about the Farewell Pilgrimage, while the Prophet (ﷺ) was among us, and we did not know what the Farewell Pilgrimage was, until Allah praised the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and praised him. Then he mentioned the Antichrist, and he mentioned it frequently, and said: “Allah did not send any prophet but warned his nation: Noah and the prophets after him warned their nations of him, and that if he (the Dajjal) emerges among you, then what is hidden from you.” It is not hidden from you that your Lord is not one-eyed, but he (the Dajjal) is one-eyed, blind in the right eye, as if his eye was a floating grape. Indeed, Allah has forbidden to you your blood and your wealth, as sacred as this day of yours, in this country of yours, in this month of yours. Have I not conveyed the message? They said: Yes. He said: “O Allah, bear witness - three times - and woe to you, or woe to you. See, do not return after me to being infidels who strike the necks of some of you.”” [Narrated by Al-Bukhari, and some of it was narrated by Muslim]."
"206","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever oppresses (anyone) even a span of land, he will be encircled by seven earths on the Day of Resurrection” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"207","On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Indeed, Allah gives respite to the oppressor, and if He seizes him, He does not let him go.” Then he recited: “And likewise is the seizing of your Lord when He seizes the towns while they are unjust. Indeed, His seizing of them is very painful” [Hud: 102] [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"208","On the authority of Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me and said: “You are coming to a people from the People of the Book, so invite them to testify that there is no god but Allah, and that I am the Messenger of Allah. If they obey that, then inform them that Allah has required five prayers for them every day and night. If they obey that, then beware of the value of their money. And fear the call of the oppressed, for there is no veil between it (the call of the oppressed) and Allah.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"209","On the authority of Abu Hamid Abd al-Rahman bin Saad al-Sa’idi, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet appointed a man from Azd, called Ibn al-Latbiyyah, to provide charity. When he came, he said: This is for you, and this was given to me. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood up on the pulpit and thanked Allah and praised him. Then he said: “As for what follows, I am appointing a man from among you to do what Allah has appointed me to do. Then he comes and says: This is for you. And this is a gift that was given to me. Would that he had sat in his father's house until a legitimate gift came to him if he is truthful? By Allah, no one of you takes anything without his right except that he meets Allah Almighty, carrying it on the Day of Resurrection. I do not know of anyone of you who has met Allah carrying a camel that was bellowing, or a cow that was bellowing, or a sheep that was bleating.” Then he raised his hands until the whites of his armpits could be seen and said: “Oh Allah, have I conveyed the message” three times? [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"210","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Whoever has wronged his brother, whether through his honor or anything, let him absolve himself of that (wrong) towards his brother today before there is no dinar or dirham (to compensate with). If he has done a good deed, it will be taken from him in proportion to the amount he wronged, and if he has no good deeds, then some of his companion’s bad deeds will be taken and burdened upon him” [Al-Bukhari]."
"211","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “A Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and an immigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"212","And on his authority, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man called Karkara was on the burden of the Prophet (ﷺ) and he died, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “He is in Hell.” So they went to look at him and found a cloak that had been tied up. [Al-Bukhari]."
"213","On the authority of Abu Bakra Nafi` ibn al-Harith, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Indeed, time has turned around as it was on the day Allah created the heavens and the earth: the year is twelve months, of which four are sacred: three successive: Dhul-Qa’dah, Dhul-Hijjah, Muharram, and Rajab Mudar which is between Jumada and Sha’ban. Which month is this?” We said: Allah and His Messenger know best, so he remained silent. So much so that we thought he would call it by something other than its name. He said: Isn’t it Dhul-Hijja? We said, “Yes.” He said: “What kind of town is this?” We said: “Allah and His Messenger know best,” so we remained silent until we thought he would call it by something other than its name. He said: “Isn’t it the city (Mecca)?” We said: Yes. He said: “So what day is this?” We said: Allah and His Messenger know best, so we remained silent until we thought he would call it by something other than its name. He said: “Isn’t it the Day of Sacrifice?” We said, “Yes.” He said: “Your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you, just as this day of yours in this country of yours is sacred in this month of yours. Whoever conveys it will be more aware of it than some of those who heard it.” Then he said: “Have you conveyed it? Have you not conveyed it?” We said: Yes. He said: “O Allah, bear witness” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"214","On the authority of Abu Umamah Iyas bin Tha’labah Al-Harithi, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever takes away the right of a Muslim man by his oath, Allah has made Hell obligatory for him and has forbidden Paradise for him.” A man said: And if it is a small thing, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “Even a small twig of the araak tree” [Muslim]."
"215","On the authority of Adi Ibn Amira, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Whoever of you we employ for a job, then he conceals a needle or anything above it or anything above it, is embezzlement (ghulul) that will be brought on the Day of Resurrection.” Then a black man from the Ansar stood up to him, as if I was looking at him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, accept your work for me. He said: “And what’s the matter with you?” He said: “I heard you saying such and such.” He said: “And I I say it now: Whoever we use to do something, let him bring a little or a lot, for whatever he is given, he will take, and whatever he is forbidden from, he refrains from it. [Muslim]."
"216","On the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When it was the Day of Khaybar, a group of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) came and said that so-and-so is a martyr, and so-and-so is a martyr, until they passed by a man and said: So-and-so is a martyr. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: No, I saw him in the Fire in his cloak - or cloak -” [Muslim]."
"217","On the authority of Abu Qatada Al-Harith bin Rabi’, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he stood up among them and mentioned to them that jihad in the path of Allah and belief in Allah is the best of deeds. Then a man stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think that if I kill in the name of Allah, my sins will be expiated for me? So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: “Yes, if you are killed in the path of Allah and you are patient and seeking reward, approaching and not retreating.” Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “How did you say?” He said: “What do you think if I were killed in the name of Allah, will my sins be expiated from me?” The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Yes, and you are patient and seeking reward, coming forward without turning away, except for debt, for Gabriel told me that” [Muslim]."
"218","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do you know who the bankrupt is?” They said: The bankrupt among us is the one who has no dirham or property. So he said: “The bankrupt from my nation will come on the Day of Resurrection with prayer, fasting, and zakat, and he will come cursing this, slandering this, eating this’s money, shedding this’s blood, beating this, and he will be given this.” Of his good deeds, and this is one of his good deeds. If his good deeds were exhausted before he fulfilled what he owed, he would take some of their sins and cast them upon him, then he would be cast into the Fire.” [Muslim]."
"219","On the authority of Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I am only human, and you dispute with me, and perhaps some of you will be more eloquent in his argument than others, so I will judge for him according to what I hear. For whomever I judge for the right of his brother, I will cut off a piece of Hell for him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"220","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The believer continues to be in a state of spaciousness and ease in his religion as long as he does not shed innocent blood” [Al-Bukhari]."
"221","On the authority of Khawla bint Amer Al-Ansari, the wife of Hamzah, may Allah be pleased with him and her, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Men who unlawfully consume the wealth of Allah will have the Fire (Hell) on the Day of Resurrection” [Al-Bukhari]."
"222","On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “A believer to a believer is like a building that supports one another,” and he interlaced his fingers. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"223","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever passes by any of our mosques or our markets, and has arrows, let him hold them, or hold their arrowheads with his palm, lest he harm any of the Muslims with anything from them” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"224","On the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The example of the believers in their love, compassion, and sympathy is like the body, if one organ complains of it, the rest of the body responds to it with sleepless nights and fever” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"225","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet kissed Al-Hasan bin Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, and Al-Aqra’ bin Habis was with him. Al-Aqra’ said: I have ten children and I have not kissed any of them. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) looked at him and said: “He who does not have mercy will not have mercy” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"226","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Some Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: Do you accept your boys? He said: “Yes.” They said: But by Allah, we will not accept! Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do you have any power if Allah has removed mercy from your hearts?” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"227","On the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “He who does not have mercy on people, Allah will not have mercy on him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"228","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If one of you prays for people, let him shorten it, for among them are the weak, the sick, and the old. And if he prays alone, let him prolong it as much as he wishes” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. (10)"
"229","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would abandon work, and he loved to do it, for fear that people would do it and it would be imposed on them” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"230","And on her authority, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade them from fasting continuously (without breaking the fast at night) out of mercy for them, so they said: Are you communicating? He said: “I am not like you; I remain (fasting) and my Lord feeds me and gives me drink” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. Its meaning is that it makes one who eats and drinks strong."
"231","On the authority of Abu Qatada Al-Harith bin Rabi’, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I am standing up for prayer, and I want to prolong it, but I hear the boy crying, so I shorten my prayer out of dislike of causing hardship to his mother” [Al-Bukhari]."
"232","On the authority of Jundub bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah, so Allah will not ask you for anything from His protection, for whoever asks Him for something from His protection, He will grant it to him, then cast him on his face into the Fire of Hell” [Muslim]."
"233","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A Muslim is a Muslim’s brother. He does not oppress him, nor does he betray him. Whoever is in need of his brother, Allah will meet his need, and whoever relieves a Muslim’s distress, Allah will relieve him of his distress on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever covers a Muslim, Allah will cover him on the Day of Resurrection” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"234","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim. He does not betray him, lie to him, or let him down. Everything that a Muslim has is sacred to another Muslim: his honor, his wealth, and his blood. Piety here. It is enough evil for a person to despise his Muslim brother” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"235","On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Do not envy one another, do not bear mutual hatred, do not outbid one another in sales, do not turn away from one another, and do not bid against one another in a sale, and be servants of Allah as brothers. A Muslim is a Muslim’s brother: he does not oppress him, he does not despise him, and he does not let him down. Piety here - and he points to his chest three times - is enough evil for a person to despise his Muslim brother. It is forbidden for a Muslim to violate the blood, wealth, and honor of another Muslim” [Muslim]."
"236","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him (ﷺ) he said: “None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"237","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Support your brother, whether he is an oppressor or an oppressed person.” A man said: O Messenger of Allah, support him if he is oppressed. Do you think that if he is an oppressor, how can I support him? He said: “You restrain him - or prevent him - from injustice, for that is his victory” [Al-Bukhari]."
"238","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The rights of a Muslim over another Muslim are five: returning greetings, visiting the sick, following funerals, answering invitations, and to say the Prayer of Mercy to the one who sneezes” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim: “The rights of a Muslim over another Muslim are six: If you meet him, greet him, and if he calls you, answer him, and if he seeks advice from you, give him advice, and when he sneezes and praises Allah, then say the Prayer of Mercy to him, and if he is sick, visit him, and if he dies, follow his funeral procession.”"
"239","On the authority of Abu Amara Al-Baraa bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded us to do seven things, and forbade us from seven things: He commanded us to visit the sick, to follow the funeral procession, to say the Prayer of Mercy to the one who sneezes, to fulfill one's oath, to support the oppressed, to respond to the one who invites (to a meal), and to spread greetings. He forbade us from wearing rings or seals with gold, from drinking with silver, from red cushions, from bows, and from wearing silk, istabraq, and dibaj [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"240","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “A servant does not cover a servant in this world but Allah will cover him on the Day of Resurrection” [Muslim]."
"241","And on his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “All of my nation is safe except those who speak out openly, and part of openness is when a man does something at night, then in the morning and Allah has covered it for him, he says: ‘Oh so-and-so, yesterday I did such-and-such,’ and his Lord has covered him for the night, and he spends the morning uncovering the veil that Allah had placed over him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"242","On the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “If a female slave commits adultery and her adultery becomes clear, then the punishment should flog her and do not rebuke her. Then if she commits the second adultery, let the punishment flog her and do not rebuke her. Then if she commits adultery a third time, let him sell her, even if it is with a rope of hair.” (Agreed upon) (15)"
"243","On his authority, he said: A man who had drunk alcohol was brought to the Prophet and he said: “Strike him.” Abu Hurairah said: Among us is the one who strikes with his hand, the one who strikes with his shoe, and the one who strikes with his garment. When he left, some of the people said: May Allah disgrace you. He said: “Do not say like that, lest you help Satan against him.” [Al-Bukhari].."
"244","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim. He does not oppress him or betray him. Whoever is in need of his brother, Allah will meet his need, and whoever relieves a Muslim’s distress, Allah will relieve him of his distress on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever covers a Muslim, Allah will cover him on the Day of Resurrection” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"245","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Whoever relieves a believer of the distress of this world, Allah will relieve him of the distress of the Day of Resurrection, and whoever eases the hardship of a person in financial difficulty, Allah will make things easy for him in this world and the hereafter, and whoever covers a Muslim, Allah will cover him in this world and the hereafter. No people gathered in one of the houses of Allah Almighty, reciting the Book of Allah, and studying it among themselves except that tranquility descended upon them, mercy enveloped them, the angels surrounded them, and Allah reminded them of those with Him. And whoever has little good deeds, his lineage will not avail him anything” [Muslim]."
"246","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Whenever a person seeking a need came to the Prophet (ﷺ), he would go to those sitting with him and say: “Intercede, and you will be rewarded, and Allah will decide through the tongue of His Prophet what He likes” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. (16)"
"247","And on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, in the story of Barirah and her husband. He said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said to her: “Will you take him back?” She said: O Messenger of Allah, do you command me? He said: “I only intercede.” She said: I have no need for him. [Al-Bukhari]."
"248","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Every bone of a person has a charity due upon it. Every day the sun rises, to act justly between two people is a charity. To help a man on his animal and carry him on it, or to lift his belongings onto it is a charity. A kind word is a charity, every step you take towards prayer is a charity, and removing harmful things from the road is a charity.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. (17)"
"249","On the authority of Umm Kulthum bint Uqba bin Abi Muait, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “The one who makes peace between people and then promotes good, or says good is not a liar” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in Muslim’s narration, Ziadah said: “And I did not hear him give him a concession in anything that people say except in three, meaning: war, reconciliation between people, and the man’s speech to his wife, and the woman’s speech to her husband.”"
"250","And on the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) heard the voice of two opponents at the door, their voices raising, and one of them humbled the other and begged him for something, and he said: By Allah, I will not do it. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out to them and said: “Where is the one who seeks Allah who does not do good deeds?” So he said: “I do, O Messenger of Allah, to him, whichever one I like.” (Agreed upon) (on him).."
"251","On the authority of Abu Abbas Sahl bin Saad Al-Saadi, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was informed that there was evil among the Banu Amr ibn Awf, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out to reconcile them with some people with him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was detained and the time had come for prayer. So can you lead the people? He said: Yes, if you wish. So Bilal established the prayer, and Abu Bakr came forward and said “Allahu Akbar,” and the people said “Allahu Akbar,” and the Messenger of Allah came. the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) walked in the rows until he stood up in the row, so the people began to applaud, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, did not turn around during his prayer. When the people applauded the most, he turned around and saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) pointed to him, so Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, raised his hand and thanked Allah, and retreated behind him until he stood in the row, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came forward and prayed for the people. When he finished, he turned to the people and said: “O people, what is the matter with you that when something disturbs you during prayer, you begin to clap? The applause is for women. Whoever is disturbed by something in his prayer, let him say, Glory be to Allah, for no one hears him when he says Glory be to Allah except he turns around and says: O Abu Bakr: What prevented you from leading the people in prayer when I pointed to you?” So Abu Bakr said: Ibn Ibn Al-Khattab should not have heard him say, Glory be to Allah. Abu Quhafa instructed the people to lead the people in prayer in front of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. (20)"
"252","On the authority of Haritha bin Wahb, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise? Every humble, meek weak person. If he swore an oath to Allah, he would fulfill it. Shall I not tell you about the people of Hell? Every harsh, miserly, arrogant person.” (Agreed upon) (21)"
"253","On the authority of Abu Abbas Sahl bin Saad Al-Sa’idi, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man passed by the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said to a man sitting with him: “What do you think about this?” He said: A man from the noblest of people. This man, by Allah, has the right that if he proposes marriage he will be accepted, and if he intercedes his intercession will be accepted. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) remained silent, then another man passed by, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him. He said: “What do you think about this?” He said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a man from among the poor Muslims. If he proposes, he should not be married, if he intercedes, he should not intercede, and if he says, his words should not be listened to. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “This is better than filling the earth like this.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. (22)"
"254","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Heaven and Hell argued, and Hell said: In the tyrannical and the arrogant, and Paradise said: In the weak and needy of people, so Allah decided between them: You are Paradise, my mercy, and I have mercy with you whom I wish, and you are Hell, I punish through you whom I wish, and it is up to both of you to fill it.” [Al-Bukhari] Muslim).."
"255","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “On the Day of Resurrection, there will come a great, fat man who will not be worth as much weight to the wing of a mosquito” (Agreed upon)."
"256","On his authority, a black woman was maintaining the mosque, or a young man, and she was missing, so he inquired about her. They informed him that she had died. He said: “Did you not inform me?” It was as if they belittled her matter, or his matter, so he said: “Show me to his grave.” So they showed him her grave and he prayed over her, then he said: “These graves are full.” It is darkness upon its people, and Allah Almighty will illuminate these graves for them by my prayers over them.” (Agreed upon) (23)"
"257","And on his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A disheveled, dusty, man pushed away from doors, if he swore an oath to Allah, he would fulfill it” [Muslim]."
"258","On the authority of Osama, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “I stood at the gate of Paradise, and found that most of those who had entered it were the poor, while the wealthy were held back. They were imprisoned, but the companions of Hell had been ordered to go to Hell. And I stood at the gate of Hell, and found that most of those who had entered it were women” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. (24)"
"259","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Only three spoke in the cradle: Jesus, son of Mary, and the companion of Jurayj, and Jurayj was a man of worship, so he took a hermitage and was in it, and his mother came to him while he was praying and said: O Jurayj, and his mother came to him while he was praying and said: Oh Jurayj, and he said: Oh Lord, my mother and my prayer, so he went to his prayer and she left. When It was the next day that she came to him while he was praying, and said: O Jurayj, and he said: 'O my Lord, my mother and my prayer,' so he resumed his prayer and she left. When she returned the next day while he was praying, she called him again, and he repeated the same response, so she left and prayed: 'O Allah, do not let him die until he sees the faces of prostitutes.' So the children of Israel remembered Jurayj and his worship, and she was a prostitute who was imitating her beauty, so she said: If you wish, I will tempt him, so she exposed herself to him, but he did not pay attention to her, so she came to a shepherd who was sheltering in his hermitage. So she made herself available to him and he had relations with her. So she became pregnant, and they started beating him. He said: What is the matter with you? They said: I committed adultery with this prostitute and gave birth to you. He said: Where is the boy? So they brought him and he said: Leave me so I can pray, so he prayed. When he finished praying, he went to the boy and poked his stomach and said: O boy, who is your father? He said: So-and-so shepherd, so they went to Jurayj, kissing him and wiping him. And they said: We will build your hermitage of gold. He said: No, restore it from clay as it was, so they did. We saw a boy being breastfed by his mother, and a man passed by riding on a luxurious animal with a handsome appearance. She said: “Oh Allah, make my son like this.” He left the breast and came to him and looked at him and said: “Oh Allah, do not make me like him.” Then he approached his breast and he began to suckle. It was as if I was looking at the Messenger of Allah. May the (ﷺ) (ﷺ) while he was narrating his breastfeeding with his index finger in his mouth, so he began to suck it. He said: “They passed by a slave girl and they were beating her, and they were saying: You committed adultery and stole, and she was saying: Allah is sufficient for me, and He is the best disposer of affairs.” His mother said: Oh Allah, do not make my son like her. So he left the breastfeeding and looked at her and said: Oh Allah, make me like her. There, they retracted the conversation and she said: A man of good appearance passed by. So I said: Oh Allah, make my son like him. So I said: Oh Allah, do not make me like him. They passed by this nation and they were beating her and saying: She committed adultery and stole. I said: Oh Allah, do not make my son like her. So I said: Oh Allah, make me like her?! He said: That man was a tyrant, so I said: Oh Allah, do not make me like him. And to this woman they say: She committed adultery, and she did not commit adultery, and she stole, and she did not steal. So I said: Oh Allah, make me like her.” (Agreed upon) (25)"
"260","On the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) six people, and the polytheists said to the Prophet (ﷺ): Expel these people, they do not dare against us. It was me, Ibn Masoud, and two men whom I cannot name, and what Allah wished for it to happen occurred to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) so he spoke to himself, so Allah Almighty revealed: {And do not expel those who call upon their Lord in the morning and the evening. They want his face} [Al-An’am: 52: Narrated by Muslim]."
"261","On the authority of Abu Hubayra Aidh bin Amr Al-Muzani, who was one of the people of the pledge of allegiance to Al-Ridwan, may Allah be pleased with him, that Abu Sufyan came to Salman, Suhaib, and Bilal with a group, and they said: The swords of Allah have not yet taken their due effect against the enemy of Allah. Then Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Are you saying this to the sheikh of Quraysh and their master? So he came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and told him, and he said: “O Abu Bakr, perhaps you have angered them? If you have angered them, you have angered your Lord. So he came to them and said: O brothers, did I make you angry? They said: No, may Allah forgive you, my brother. [Muslim]."
"262","On the authority of Sahl bin Saeed, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger (ﷺ) said: “I and the one who takes care of an orphan will be in Paradise like this,” and he pointed with his index and middle fingers, separating them. [Al-Bukhari]."
"263","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The one who takes care of an orphan, for him or for someone else, I and he are like these two in Paradise.” The narrator, who is Malik Ibn Anas, pointed with his index and middle fingers. [Muslim]."
"264","On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “It is not the poor person who is turned away with only one or two dates, or one morsel and two morsels, but rather the poor person who is chaste” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"265","On the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ): “The one who takes care of the widow and the poor is like the one who fights in the cause of Allah,” and I think he said: “And like the one who stands up and does not let up, and like the fasting person who does not break his fast” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"266","On the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “The worst food is the food of a feast. It prevents him who comes to it, and he who refuses it is invited to it, and whoever does not respond to the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger” [Muslim]. And in a narration in “Al-Sahihayn” on the authority of Abu Hurairah, from his saying: “Evil food is the food of a feast to which the rich are invited and left out.” The poor” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"267","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Whoever supports two female slaves until they reach puberty, on the Day of Resurrection, he and I will come like these two,” and he joined his fingers. [Muslim]. (29)"
"268","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: “A woman came to me with two of her daughters asking, but she did not find anything with me except one date, so I gave it to her, so she divided it between her two daughters, but she did not eat from it. Then she got up and went out, so the Prophet (ﷺ) entered upon us, so I told him, and he said: “Whoever is tested by one of these daughters with something and does good to them, they will be a shield for him from Hell” ((Agreed upon). On him).."
"269","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: A poor woman came to me carrying her two daughters, so I fed her three dates. She gave each of them a date and raised a date to her mouth to eat. So her daughters fed her, so she split the date she wanted to eat between them. I liked her condition, so I mentioned what she had done to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: “Allah has made it obligatory for her to enter Paradise, or free her from sin because of it.” Fire” [Muslim]."
"270","On the authority of Abu Shuraih Khuwaylid bin Amr Al-Khuza’i, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “O Allah, I deprive the rights of the weak, the orphan and the woman” [A good hadith narrated by Al-Nasa’i with a good chain of transmission]."
"271","On the authority of Musab bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Saad saw that he had superiority over those below him, so the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Are you going to be supported and given sustenance except by your weak ones?” [Al-Bukhari] This is a mursal hadith, for Musab bin Sa'd is a Tabi'i (follower of the Companions), ((And it was narrated by Al-Hafiz Abu Bakr Al-Barqani in his Sahih, connected on the authority of Musab on the authority of His father, may Allah be pleased with him)."
"272","On the authority of Abu Al-Darda’ Uwaimer, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Seek me among the weak, for you will only be helped, and you will be provided for by the weak of yours” [Abu Dawud]."
"273","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Treat women well, for the woman was created from a rib, and the crooked part of the rib is at the top, so if you try to straighten it, you will break it, and if you leave it, it will remain crooked, so treat women well” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration in [The two Sahih books]: “A woman is like a rib. If you straighten her, you will break her, and if you enjoy her, you will enjoy her while there is crookedness in her.” And in a narration by Muslim: “The woman was created from a rib. She will not be straight for you in a way. If you straighten her, you will break her, and if you go to straighten her, you will break her, and her divorce is her breaking (i.e., the result of trying to straighten her)”"
"274","On the authority of Abdullah bin Zam’ah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) giving a sermon, and he mentioned the she-camel and the one who hamstrung her, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: (When the most wretched of hers was resurrected) a mighty, powerful and invincible man among his clan. Then he mentioned women, and he preached to them, and said: “One of you may beat his wife with the severity of a slave, so perhaps he He will have sex with her since the end of his day.” Then he admonished them about their laughter at farting and said: “Is there any one of you who laughs at what he does?” (Agreed upon)."
"275","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A believing man should not hate a believing woman if he dislikes one of her traits, he will be pleased with another of her traits.” Or he said: “other than it (i.e., another trait)” [Muslim]."
"276","On the authority of Amr ibn al-Ahwad al-Jashmi, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) during the Farewell Pilgrimage, saying after he had thanked Allah Almighty, praised Him, mentioned, and preached, then he said: “And treat women well, for they are your helpers, and you do not have the right to do anything other than that unless they commit a clear indecency. If they do, then deprive them of their beds, and beat them not severely. If they obey you, then do not seek a way against them. Indeed, you have a right over your women, and your women have a right over you, so your right over them is that they should not let those whom you dislike enter your beds, and that they should not let those whom you dislike enter your homes. Indeed, their right over you is that you should be kind to them in their clothing and food.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"277","On the authority of Muawiyah bin Haidah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said, O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) what is the right of the wife of one of us over him? He said: “That you feed her when you eat, and that you clothe her when you clothe yourself, and that you do not strike her face, and that you do not abuse her, and that you do not forsake her except in the house.” A good hadith narrated by Abu Dawud, who said: The meaning of “do not become ugly,” meaning: Do not say that Allah makes you ugly."
"278","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The most perfect of believers in faith is the one with the best character, and the best of you are the best to their wives” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"279","On the authority of Iyas bin Abi Dhubab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not beat Allah’s female slaves.” Then Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: Women rebuke their husbands, so he granted permission to beat them, so many women went around the family of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) complaining about their husbands, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Many women have gone around Muhammad’s family complaining about their husbands. They are not your best.” [Abu Dawud]."
"280","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The world is enjoyment, and the best enjoyment is a righteous woman” [Muslim]."
"281","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If a man invites his wife to his bed and she does not come to him, and he spends the night angry with her, the angels curse her until morning” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in her narration, “If a woman spends the night avoiding her husband’s bed, the angels curse her until morning.” And in a narration, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, there is no man who invites his wife to his bed and she refuses to do so, except that He who is in heaven is displeased with her until he is satisfied with her.”"
"282","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, also that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “It is not permissible for a woman to fast while her husband is present without his permission, and she is not permitted to allow anyone into his house except with his permission” (Agreed upon, and this is the wording of Al-Bukhari)."
"283","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “All of you are shepherds, and all of you are responsible for his flock. The prince is a shepherd, and the man is a shepherd over his household;"
"284","On the authority of Abu Ali Talq bin Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If a man calls his wife for his need, let her come to him, even if she is on the stove.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"285","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “If I were to command someone to prostrate to anyone else, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"286","On the authority of Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Any woman who dies and her husband is satisfied with her will enter Paradise” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"287","On the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “A woman does not harm her husband in this world unless a wife from among the beautiful houris says, ‘Do not harm him. May Allah kill you!’ For he is with you but an intruder who is about to leave you to us.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"288","On the authority of Osama bin Zaid, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “I have not left behind me any temptation that is more harmful to men than women” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"289","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A dinar you spent in the path of Allah, a dinar you spent on a slave, a dinar you gave in charity to a poor person, and a dinar you spent on your family, the greatest reward is the one you spent on your family” [Muslim]."
"290","On the authority of Abu Abdullah - and he is called: Abu Abdul Rahman - Thawban bin Bajadid, a client of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The best dinar a man can spend is a dinar he spends on his family, a dinar he spends on his animal for the sake of Allah, and a dinar he spends on his companions for the sake of Allah” ([Muslim].."
"291","And on the authority of Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, do I have a reward for the children of Abu Salamah if I spend on them, and I am not leaving them like this and so, but they are my sons? He said: “Yes, you will have a reward for what you spent on them” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"292","On the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, in his long hadith that we presented at the beginning of the book in the chapter on intention, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: “And you will not spend seeking the pleasure of Allah with it except that you will be rewarded with it up to what you put in your wife’s mouth” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"293","On the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Badri, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “If a man spends on his family an expenditure he intends for Allah's sake, then it is charity for him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"294","And on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): “It is enough sin for a person to waste what he provides for.” An authentic hadith [narrated by Abu Dawud and others]. It was narrated by Muslim in his Sahih with the same meaning that he said: “It is enough sin for a person to withhold from someone who has his livelihood.”"
"295","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “There is not a day when the servants wake up except that two angels descend, and one of them says: Oh Allah, give a successor to the spender, and the other says: Oh Allah, give the withholder loss” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"296","And on the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and start with those you support, and the best charity is that which is done on the back of wealth, and whoever abstains from asking others, Allah will suffice him, and whoever is self-sufficient, Allah will enrich him” [Al-Bukhari]."
"297","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Abu Talha, may Allah be pleased with him, was the most wealthy of the Ansar in Medina in terms of palm trees, and the most beloved of his wealth was Birhaa, which was facing the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would enter it and drink from the good water in it. Anas said: When this verse was revealed: “You will not attain righteousness until you spend of what you love,” Abu Talha went to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: O Messenger, Allah Almighty has revealed to you: {You will not attain righteousness until you spend of what you love} And if my wealth is dearest to me, Barhaa, and it is charity for Allah Almighty, I hope for its righteousness and its reserve with Allah Almighty, so put it, O Messenger of Allah, where Allah shows you. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Well done! That is profitable wealth, that is profitable wealth, and I have heard what you said, “I think you should give it to your closest relatives.” Abu Talha said: “I will, O Messenger of Allah.” So Abu Talha divided it among his relatives and his cousins. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"298","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, took the date of charity and put it in his mouth, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Kh-k-k-k-h, throw it away. Didn’t you know that we do not eat charity!? [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration: “It is not permissible for us to give charity” and his saying: “KKHKKH” is said by placing the Kha’ in its place, and it is said by kasra it with the tanween, and it is a word that rebukes the boy from dirty things. Al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, was a boy."
"299","On the authority of Abu Hafs Omar bin Abi Salamah Abdullah bin Abdul Asad, stepson of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: I was a boy in the lap of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and my hand was straying over the dish, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: “O boy, name the name of Allah Almighty, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what follows you,” and that is still my taste. ((Agreed) On him).."
"300","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: Each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is responsible for his flock, and the woman is a shepherd in her husband’s house and responsible for her flock, and the servant is a shepherd of his master’s property and responsible for his flock, so all of you are a shepherd and responsible for his flock” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"301","On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Command your children to pray when they are seven years old, and beat them for it when they are ten years old, and separate them in their beds” [A good hadith narrated by Abu Dawud with a good chain of transmission]."
"302","On the authority of Abu Tharayya Sabra bin Ma’bad al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Teach a boy to pray at the age of seven” and beat him for it when he is ten years old. A good hadith narrated by Abu Dawud, and al-Tirmidhi said it was a good hadith. Abu Dawud’s wording was: “Teach a boy to pray when he reaches seven years of age.”"
"303","On the authority of Ibn Omar and Aisha, may Allah be pleased with them, they said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Gabriel kept advising me to take care of my neighbor until I thought he would inherit from him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"304","On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O Abu Dharr, if you cook broth, add more water to it, and treat your neighbors.” [Muslim]. And in his narration on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: My friend (ﷺ) advised me: “If you cook broth, add more water to it, then see the people of house of your neighbors, so treat them kindly.”"
"305","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “By Allah, he does not believe, by Allah, he does not believe, by Allah, he does not believe!” It was said: Who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “The one whose neighbor is not safe from his calamities!” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim: He who does not make his neighbor safe from his own harms will not enter Paradise.”"
"306","On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O Muslim women, do not despise a female neighbor for her female neighbor, even if it is a small portion of sheep” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"307","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A neighbor should not prevent a neighbor from planting a piece of wood in his wall.” Then Abu Hurairah says: Why should I see you turning away from it! By Allah, I will throw it between your shoulders. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"308","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or remain silent” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"309","On the authority of Abu Shurayh Al-Khuza’i, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or remain silent” [Narrated by Muslim with this wording, and Al-Bukhari narrated some of it]."
"310","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbours, so which of them should I give a gift to? He said: “To the one closest to you in terms of doors” [Al-Bukhari]."
"311","On the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The best companions in the sight of Allah Almighty are the best to their companion, and the best neighbors in the sight of Allah Almighty are the best to their neighbor” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"312","On the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I asked the Prophet (ﷺ): Which work is most beloved to Allah Almighty? He said: “Praying on time.” I said: Then what? He said: “Being righteous to one’s parents.” I said: Then what? He said: “Jihad for the sake of Allah” (Agreed upon). On him).."
"313","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “No son repays his father unless he finds him owned, buys him, and frees him.” [Muslim]."
"314","It is also reported from him that the Messenger of Allah said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him maintain his ties of kinship. He believes in Allah and the Last Day, so let him speak good or remain silent.” Agreed upon."
"315","And on his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah Almighty created creation so that when He had finished with them, the womb would stand up.” She said: “This is the place of the one seeking refuge with you from estrangement.” He said: “Yes. Are you not satisfied that I should maintain ties with those who have joined you, and cut off ties with those who have separated from you?” She said: “Yes.” He said: “That is for you.” Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Read if you wish: (Is it possible that if you turn away [from Allah’s command], you would spread corruption on earth and sever your ties of kinship? These are the ones whom Allah has cursed, so He deafened them and blinded their sight.) [Muhammad: 22,32] [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Al-Bukhari: And Allah Almighty said: ““Whoever maintains ties with you [the womb], I will maintain ties with him; and whoever cuts you off, I will cut him off.”"
"316","On his authority, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the most deserving of my good companionship? He said: “Your mother.” He said: “Then who?” He said: “Your mother” He said: “Then who?” He said: “Your mother” He said: “Then who?” He said: “Then who?” “Your father” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration: O Messenger of Allah, who is more deserving of good company? He said: “Your mother, then your mother, then your mother, then your father, then your nearest relatives, then your nearest relatives.”"
"317","And on his authority, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “May his nose be rubbed in dust, then may his nose be rubbed in dust, then may his nose be rubbed in dust - whoever has his parents alive in old age, one or both of them, will not enter Paradise” [Muslim]"
"318","On his authority, a man said: O Messenger of Allah! I have relatives, I maintain ties with them, but they cut me off, and I do good to them, but they abuse me, and I am patient with them, and they treat me with abuse/ignorance. So he said: “If you were as you said, It is as if you have made them miserable, and Allah will remain a helper/supporter for you against them as long as you continue in this good conduct.” [Muslim]."
"319","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever wants his livelihood to be expanded and his lifespan to be extended, let him maintain his ties of kinship” (Agreed upon)."
"320","On his authority, he said: Abu Talha had the most wealth among the Ansar in Medina in terms of palm trees, and the most beloved of his wealth was Birhaa, which was facing the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would enter it and drink from the good water in it. When this verse was revealed: “You will not attain righteousness until you spend of what you love” [Al Imran: 92] Abu Talha went to the Messenger of Allah. he said: O Messenger of Allah, indeed Allah, Blessed and Most High, says: {You will not attain righteousness until you spend of what you love.} And if I love my wealth to me, Barha’, and it is a charity for Allah Almighty, and I hope for its righteousness and its treasure with Allah Almighty, then put it, O Messenger of Allah, where Allah has shown you. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Well done! That is most profitable wealth, and that is most profitable wealth! I heard what you said, and I think you should give it to your relatives.” Abu Talha said: “I will do it, O Messenger of Allah.” So Abu Talha divided it among his relatives and his cousins. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. His words have previously been explained in: the chapter on spending from what he likes."
"321","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them, he said: A man came to the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) and said: I pledge allegiance to you for migration and jihad, seeking reward from Allah Almighty. He said: “Do you have any of your parents alive?” He said: Yes, rather both of them are alive. He said: “So you seek reward from Allah Almighty?” He said: Yes. He said, “Then go back to your parents and treat them well.” (Agreed upon. This is a Muslim wording.) And in their narration: A man came and asked him for permission to engage in jihad. He said, “Are your parents alive?” He said: Yes. He said: “So strive through them (by serving your parents, which is the jihad of serving one's parents).”"
"322","On the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “The one who is connected is not the one who reciprocates (only maintains ties of kinship when others do so), but the one who is connected if his ties of kinship are severed, he connects them” [Al-Bukhari]."
"323","On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The womb is hanging from the throne, saying: Whoever joins me, Allah will join him, and whoever separates me, Allah will separate him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"324","And on the authority of the Mother of the Believers, Maimunah bint Al-Harith, may Allah be pleased with her, that she freed a child and did not ask the permission of the Prophet (ﷺ) so when the day came that he would visit her, she said: Did you feel, O Messenger of Allah, that I had freed my slave girl? He said: “Or did you?” She said: Yes. He said: “But if you had given her to your maternal uncles, your reward would have been greater.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"325","On the authority of Asma’ bint Abi Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with them both, she said: I came to my mother while she was a polytheist during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) so I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to ask the Messenger of Allah. I said: I came to my mother and she was willing. Should I uphold ties with my mother? He said: “Yes, uphold ties with your mother.” (Agreed upon)."
"326","On the authority of Zainab Al-Thaqafiyya, the wife of Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him and her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Give charity, O women, even if it is from your adornments.” She said: So I returned to Abdullah bin Masoud and said to him: You are a generous man, quick to give, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has commanded us to give charity, so give it to him, so ask him, and if that is sufficient for me, otherwise I will transfer it to Other than you, Abdullah said: Rather, come to him, so I set off, and saw a woman from the Ansar at the door of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) needing her need. the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was surrounded by awe, making it intimidating to approach him, so Bilal came out to us, so we said to him: Come to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and tell him that two women at the door are asking you: Should I give the charity on their behalf to their husbands and to orphans in Their chambers? And do not tell him who we are, so he entered their wives and orphans in their chambers? And do not tell him who we are. So Bilal entered the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and asked him. the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him, “Who are they?” He said: A woman from the Ansar and Zainab. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Which Zayanib are they?” He said: Abdullah’s wife, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “They have two rewards: the reward of kinship and the reward of charity” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"327","On the authority of Abu Sufyan Sakhr bin Harb, may Allah be pleased with him, in his long hadith on the story of Heraclius, that Heraclius said to Abu Sufyan: What does he command you to do? I mean, the Prophet (ﷺ) said: I said: He says: “Worship Allah alone, and do not associate anything with Him, and abandon what your fathers say. He commands us to pray, to be truthful, to be chaste, and to be connected.” (Agreed upon)"
"328","On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “You will conquer a land in which the qirat is mentioned.” And in a narration: “You will conquer Egypt, a land in which the qirat is called, so be kind to its people, for they have a covenant of protection and kinship ties.” And in a narration: “So if you conquer it, be good to its people, for it is theirs.” “Dhimma and kinship” or he said: “Dhimma and kinship” [Muslim]."
"329","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When this verse was revealed: (And warn your closest clan) [Al-Shu’ara’: 214] the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called Quraysh, and they gathered together, and he generalized, and said: “O Banu Abd Shams, O Banu Ka’b bin Luay, save yourselves from the Fire, O Banu Murrah bin Ka'b, save yourselves from the Fire, O Banu Abd Manaf, save yourselves from the Fire, O Banu Hashim, save yourselves from the Fire, O Banu Abdul Muttalib, save yourselves from the Fire, O Fatima, save yourself from the Fire, for I do not possess anything for you from Allah, except that you have a bond of kinship that I will uphold with its due rights.” [Muslim]."
"330","On the authority of Abu Abdullah Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying openly and not secretly: “The family of the Banu So-and-so are not my guardians. Rather, my guardian is Allah and the righteous of the believers, but they have a bond of kinship that I will uphold with its due rights.” [Agreed upon. Bukhari’s wording]."
"331","On the authority of Abu Ayoub Khaled bin Zaid Al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about a deed that will bring me into Paradise and keep me away from Hell. So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Worship Allah, and do not associate anything with Him, and establish prayer, and pay zakat, and maintain family ties” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"332","On the authority of Salman bin Amer, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “If one of you breaks his fast, let him break his fast with dates, for it is a blessing. If he does not find dates, then with water, for it is purification.” And he said: “Giving charity to the poor is charity, and giving charity to a relative is twofold: charity and upholding ties.” ([Al-Tirmidhi]."
"333","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I had a woman under my care, and I loved her, and Omar hated her, so he said to me: Divorce her, but I refused. So Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him, and the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Divorce her.” [Narrated by Abu Dawud and al-Tirmidhi and said: a good and authentic hadith]."
"334","On the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man came to him and said: I have a wife and my mother is ordering me to divorce her? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “The father is the middle of the gates of Paradise. If you wish, then destroy that door, or protect it.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"335","On the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “A maternal aunt is in the same position as a mother” [Al-Tirmidhi]. There are many well-known hadiths in the Sahih on this topic; Among them is the hadith of the Companions of the Cave, and the hadith of Jurayj, which we have previously mentioned, and well-known hadiths in the Sahih that I have omitted briefly. Among the most important of them is the long hadith of Amr ibn Absa, may Allah be pleased with him, which includes many sentences of the rules and etiquette of Islam, and I will mention it in its entirety, Allah Almighty willing, in the chapter on hope. In it he said: I entered upon the Prophet (ﷺ) in Mecca, meaning at the beginning of the prophethood, and I said to him: What are you? He said: “A prophet,” so I said: “What is a prophet?” He said: “Allah Almighty sent me.” So I said: With what did He send you? He said: “He sent me to connect family ties, break idols, and to affirm the oneness of Allah and not associate anything with Him” [And he mentioned the entire hadith. And Allah knows best]."
"336","On the authority of Abu Bakra Nafi’ bin Al-Harith, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Shall I not inform you of the greatest of the major sins?” Three times we said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah: He said: “Associating partners with Allah and being disobedient to one’s parents.” He was reclining and sat down, so he said: “And false speech and false witness.” He continued repeating it until we said: 'Would that he remained silent' [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"337","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, he said: “The major sins: associating partners with Allah, disobeying one’s parents, murder, and swearing a false oath.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"338","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Among the major sins is a man cursing his parents!” They said: O Messenger of Allah, does a man curse his parents?! He said: “Yes; he curses a man’s father, so he curses his father, and he curses a man’s mother, so he curses his mother.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration: “The One of the greatest sins is for a man to curse his parents! It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how can a man curse his parents? He said: “He curses a man’s father, so he curses his father, and he curses his mother, so he curses his mother.”"
"339","On the authority of Abu Muhammad Jubair from Mut’im, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “No one who severs ties will enter Paradise.” Sufyan said in his narration: This means: one who severs ties with ties of kinship. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"340","On the authority of Abu Issa Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Allah Almighty has forbidden to you disobedience to mothers, and withholding [what is due to others] and demanding [what is not one’s right], and infanticide of daughters, and He detests gossip, asking too much, and wasting money” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"341","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “The most righteous act is for a man to maintain affection for his father.”"
"342","And on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a Bedouin man met him on the road to Mecca, so Abdullah bin Omar greeted him, and carried him on a donkey that he was riding, and gave him a turban that was on his head. Ibn Dinar said: So we said to him: May Allah bless you. They are Bedouins and they are pleased with what is easy. Abdullah bin Omar said: This father was friendly to Omar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Allah, upon him be peace, says: “The most righteous of righteousness is a man’s maintaining ties with his father’s friends.” And in a narration on the authority of Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when he went out to Mecca, he had a donkey on which he would rest when he got tired of riding the mount, and a turban with which he would cover his head. One day he was on that donkey when a Bedouin passed by him, and he said: Aren’t you the son of so-and-so, the son of so-and-so? He said: Yes. So he gave him the donkey, and he said: Ride. This, and he gave him the turban and said: Tie your head with it, and some of his companions said to him: May Allah forgive you. You gave this Bedouin the donkey that you used to ride on, and the turban with which you used to tie your head? So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “One of the most righteous acts of righteousness is for a man to maintain ties with his father’s friends after he has moved away.” And his father was a friend of Omar, may Allah be pleased with him."
"343","On the authority of Abu Usayd - with Damm al-Hamza and Fath al-Sin - Malik bin Rabi’ah al-Sa’idi, may Allah be pleased with him, said: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) a man from Banu Salamah came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there anything left of honoring my parents that I would honor them with after their death? He said: “Yes, praying for them, asking forgiveness for them, enforcing their covenant after them, and the ties of kinship that cannot be connected except through them.” And honoring their friend” [Abu Dawud]."
"344","And on the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I have never been more jealous of one of the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) than I have been jealous of Khadija, may Allah be pleased with her, and I never saw her, but he would often mention her, and perhaps he would slaughter a sheep, then cut off its limbs, then send them to Khadija’s friends. Perhaps I would say to him: It is as if there was no one in this world except Khadija! Then he would say: “She was and was, and I had a son from her.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in one narration, if it was to slaughter a sheep, then he would give as much of it as a gift to her female friends. And in a narration, when he slaughtered a sheep, he would say: “Send it to Khadija’s friends.” And in a narration, she said: Hala bint Khuwaylid, Khadija’s sister, asked permission to go to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he knew that Khadija’s permission had been asked, so he was satisfied with that. He said: Oh Allah, Hala bint Khuwaylid"
"345","On the authority of Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I went out with Jarir bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, may Allah be pleased with him, on a journey, and he was serving me, so I said to him: Do not do that, and he said: I have seen the Ansar doing a service for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and I vowed to myself that I would not accompany any of them except to serve him. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"346","On the authority of Yazid bin Hayyan, he said: Husayn bin Sabrah, Amr bin Muslim, and I set out for Zaid bin Arqam, may Allah be pleased with them. When we sat with him, Husayn said to him: O Zaid, you have met with much goodness. I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and heard his conversation. I fought with him and prayed behind him: O Zaid, you have met with much goodness. Tell us, O Zaid, what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: Oh my nephew, by Allah, I have grown in age, my age has grown old, and I have forgotten some of what I was aware of from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) so I told you, so accept it, and what not, do not bother me. Then he said: One day the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood up and preached among us at a water called Khama between Mecca and Medina. He thanked Allah, praised Him, preached, and mentioned, then he said: “As for what follows, O people, For I am only a human being and the Messenger of my Lord is about to come and I will respond, and I am leaving behind you two heavy burdens. The first of them is the Book of Allah, in which is guidance and light, so take the Book of Allah and hold fast to it. So he urged the Book of Allah, desired it, then said: “And my family, I remind you of Allah among my family, I remind you of Allah among my family.” Husayn said to him: And from his family, O Zaid, are his wives not from his family? He said: His wives are from his family, but my family are those for whom charity is forbidden for others to give after me. He said: And who are they? He said: They are the family of Ali, the family of Aqeel, the family of Jaafar, and the family of Abbas. He said: All of these forbid charity? He said: Yes. [Muslim]. And in a narration: “But I am leaving behind you two heavy things: one of them is the Book of Allah and the rope of Allah, and whoever follows them is upon guidance, and whoever abandons them is upon misguidance.”"
"347","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of a chain of narrators that he said: Watch for Muhammad (ﷺ) among his family, [Al-Bukhari]."
"348","On the authority of Abu Masoud Uqba bin Amr al-Badri al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The people who are most literate in the Book of Allah will lead the people in prayer, and if they are equal in reading, then the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah, and if they are equal in the Sunnah, then the oldest of them to emigrate, and if they were equal in immigration, then the oldest of them. A man does not believe another man in his authority, and he does not sit in his house honorably without his permission.” [Muslim]. And in his narration: “The oldest among them in peace” instead of “in age”: or Islam. And in a narration: The people are led by the most literate of the Book of Allah and the oldest among them in reading, and if their reading is the one who emigrated, then the oldest among them to immigrate will lead them. If they were equal in migration, then the oldest of them should lead the people in prayer."
"349","On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to wipe our shoulders during prayer and say: “Stay equal and do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Those of you who possess sound judgment and forbid [wrong] will be closer to me, then those who come after them.” [Muslim]."
"350","On the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Those among you who possess sound judgment and forbid [wrong], then those who follow them, said three times, “And beware of the whims of markets” [Muslim]."
"351","On the authority of Abu Yahya, and it was said: Abu Muhammad Sahl bin Abi Hathmah - with the opening of the neglected haa and the saccade of the triangular thaa - Al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Abdullah bin Sahl and Muhayyah bin Masoud set out for Khaybar, which was under a peace treaty, and they separated. Muhaiysa came to Abdullah bin Sahl while he was dead, dripping in his own blood, and buried him. Then he came to Medina, and Abdul Rahman bin Sahl, Muhayyah and Huwaysa bin Masoud set off to the Prophet (ﷺ), then Abdul Rahman went to speak and said: “You are older, you are older.” He was the youngest of the people, so he remained silent, so they spoke and he said: “Will you swear oaths and claim the blood of your murdered one? And he mentioned the entirety of the hadith. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"352","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to bury the two Uhud martyrs in the same grave, and then say: Which of them has recited the Qur’an more? So if one of them was pointed out to him, he would place him first in the grave niche (al-lahd). [Al-Bukhari]."
"353","And on the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “I saw myself in a dream using a siwak, and two men came to me, one of them older than the other, so I handed the smaller siwak, and it was said to me: ‘Grow up,’ so I gave it to the older of them” [Narrated by Muslim and Al-Bukhari in commentary]."
"354","On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Part of the reverence of Allah Almighty is to honor the gray-haired Muslim, the bearer of the Qur’an who does not exaggerate in it, and who is neglectful of it, and honoring the one with just authority” [A good hadith narrated by Abu Dawud]."
"355","On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with them, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “He is not one of us who does not have mercy on our young and recognize the honor of our elders” [An authentic hadith narrated by Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi, and Al-Tirmidhi said: A good and authentic hadith]."
"356","And on the authority of Maimoon bin Abi Shabib, may Allah have mercy on him, that Aisha, may Allah be pleased with him, the imam, passed by a beggar, and she gave him a piece of bread, and a man with clothes and appearance passed by her, so she made him sit, and he ate, and she was told about that: ? She said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Assign people their proper ranks according to their status” [Abu Dawud]. But Maimoon said: He did not meet Aisha (i.e., he did not hear this narration from her directly)"
"357","And on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Uyaynah bin Hisn came and came to visit his nephew, Al-Hurr bin Qays, and he was one of the people whom Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, was close to. The readers were companions of Omar’s council and consultation, whether they were old or young. Uyaynah said to his nephew: O son of my brother, you have a position with this prince, so ask permission for me to meet him. So he (the nephew) asked permission for him, so Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, gave him permission, and when he entered, he said: “O son of al-Khattab, by Allah By Allah, you do not give us our full due, and you do not judge us with justice. So Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, became so angry that he was about to attack him, so Al-Hurr said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, Allah Almighty said to his Prophet (ﷺ) {Take pardon, command what is right, and turn away from the ignorant} and this is one of the ignorant. By Allah, Omar did not go beyond it when he recited it to him, and he abided strictly by the Book of Allah Almighty. [Al-Bukhari]."
"358","On the authority of Abu Saeed Samra bin Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was a boy during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and I used to memorize things from him, so what prevents me from saying this is that there are men here who are older than me. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"359","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A young man does not honor an old man due to his age until Allah decrees for him someone who will honor him at his age” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"360","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Abu Bakr said to Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, after the death of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): Take us to Umm Ayman (ﷺ) and we will visit her as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to visit them. When they reached her, she cried, and they said to her: What makes you cry? Do you not know that what Allah has is better for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)? She said: I am not crying, I do not know that What Allah Almighty has is better for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) but I cry because the revelation from heaven has stopped, so she incites them to cry, so they start crying with her. [Muslim]."
"361","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ): A man visited a brother of his in another village, and Allah Almighty stationed an angel along his path. When he came to him, he said: Where do you want? He said: I want a brother of mine in this village. He said: Do you have any favor from him that you can recompense? He said: No, except that I loved for the sake of Allah Almighty. He said: I am the Messenger of Allah to you, for Allah has loved you as you loved him for His sake” [Muslim]."
"362","On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever visits a sick person or visits a brother of his in Allah, a caller will call him, ‘May you be blessed, may your walk be blessed, and may you attain a station in Paradise.’” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"363","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “The example of a good companion and a bad companion is like the one who carries musk and the one who blows the furnace. The carrier of musk will either give you a shoe, or you will buy from him, or you will find a pleasant scent from him. And the one who blows the furnace will either burn your clothes, or you will find a foul odor from him.” (Agreed upon) (on him).."
"364","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “A woman is married for four reasons: for her money, for her lineage, for her beauty, and for her religion, so choose the one who is religious and may your hands be rubbed with water” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"365","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said to Gabriel: “What prevents you from visiting us more often than you visit us?” So it was revealed: “And we do not come down except by the command of your Lord. To Him belongs what is before us and what is behind us and what is between that” [Al-Bukhari]."
"366","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “Do not keep company with anyone but a believer, and only a pious person should eat your food.” [Narrated by Abu Dawud, and Al-Tirmidhi with an okay chain of transmission]."
"367","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “A man follows the religion of his friend, so let each of you look at who he befriends.” [Narrated by Abu Dawud, and Al-Tirmidhi with an authentic chain of transmission, and Al-Tirmidhi said: A good hadith]."
"368","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “A man is with those he loves” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. In a narration, he said: It was said to the Prophet (ﷺ): A man loves a people but has not yet joined them? He said: “A man is with those he loves.”"
"369","And on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a Bedouin said to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): When is the Hour? The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: What have you prepared for it? No prayer, no charity, but I love Allah and His Messenger.” The Prophet (ﷺ) then said: “You are with those you love..” The Prophet (ﷺ) then said: “You are with those you love."
"370","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about a man who loved a people but did not join them? So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A man is with those he loves” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"371","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “People are minerals like the minerals of gold and silver. The best of them in pre-Islamic times are the best in Islam if they understand it. Souls are conscripted soldiers, so what is familiar among them gets together, and what is dissimilar among them differs.” [Narrated by Muslim?]. [And he narrated) Al-Bukhari] His saying: “souls” from the narration of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her."
"372","On the authority of Usir bin Amr, who is said to be “Ibn Jabir,” and he said: “When the contingents of the people of Yemen came to him, Omar bin Al-Khattab would ask them: Is Uwais bin Aamir among you?” Until he came to Uwais, may Allah be pleased with him, and said to him: Are you Uwais bin Aamir? He said: Yes, he said: From Murad, then from Qarn? He said: Yes. He said: So you had leprosy, and you recovered from it except for a place of a dirham? He said: Yes. He said: You have a mother? He said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Uwais bin Amir comes to you with supplies from the people of Yemen from Murad. Then from a century ago he had leprosy, and he was cured of it except for a place of a dirham. He has a mother, and he is dutiful to her. If he swears by Allah, He (Allah) will fulfill his oath for him. I was able to ask forgiveness for you, so do it.” So he asked forgiveness for me, so I asked forgiveness for him. Omar said to him: Where do you want? He said: Kufa. He said: Shall I not write for you to its handler? He said: Being among the common people is more beloved to me. Then, the next year, a man of their nobles made Hajj, so Omar agreed, so he asked him about Uwais. He said: I left him shabby in the house with few possessions. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah say: Uwais bin Amr will come to you. with supplies from the people of Yemen from Murad, then from Qarn. He had leprosy, but he recovered from it except for the place of a dirham. He has a mother with whom he is righteous. If he swears by Allah, He (Allah) will fulfill his oath for him. If you are able to ask forgiveness for you, do so. Then he came to Uwais and said, “Ask forgiveness for me.” He said: “You have made a promise to travel righteously, so ask forgiveness for me.” He said: “Have you met Omar?” He said: “Yes,” so ask forgiveness for him, and the people understood him. So he set off on his face. [Muslim]. And also in a narration by Muslim on the authority of Usir ibn Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the people of Kufa came to see Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, and among them was a man who used to mock Uwais. Omar said: Is there anyone from the Qarnayn here? Then that man came, and Omar said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A man.” He comes to you from Yemen, and he is called: Uwais. He does not leave anyone behind in Yemen except his mother. He had whiteness in him, so he called upon Allah Almighty, so He removed it except to the place of a dinar or a dirham. Whoever of you meets him, let him ask forgiveness for you. And in a narration of his on the authority of Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “The best of the followers is a man called: Uwais: He had a mother and had white spots on him, so treat him and let him ask forgiveness for you"
"373","On the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I asked the Prophet (ﷺ) permission to perform Umrah, and he gave me permission, and said: “Do not forget us, my brother, in your supplication.” He said a word that I would give up the entire world to possess. In a narration, he said: “Include us, my brother, in your supplication.” An authentic hadith ([Abu Dawud] True).."
"374","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) would visit Quba’, riding and walking, and pray two rak’ahs there, [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration: The Prophet (ﷺ) would come to the Quba Mosque every Saturday, riding and walking, and Ibn Umar used to do that."
"375","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “There are three things whoever is in him will find in them the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger are dearer to him than anything else, that he loves a person and loves him only for Allah, and that he hates to return to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it, just as he hates being thrown into the Fire” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"376","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “There are seven whom Allah will shade in His shade on the Day when there is no shade but His shade: a just ruler, a young man who grew up worshiping Allah Almighty, a man whose heart is attached to the mosques, two men who loved each other for Allah’s sake, met for His sake, and parted for His sake, a man who was invited by a beautiful and attractive woman but said, ‘I fear Allah,’ a man who gave charity and hid it so that his left hand does not know what his right hand spends, and a man who remembered Allah alone in privacy and his eyes filled with tears.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"377","And on his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Allah Almighty will say on the Day of Resurrection, ‘Where are those who love one another for the sake of My Majesty? Today I will shade them in My shade on a day when there will be no shade but My shade.’” [Muslim]."
"378","On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Should I direct you to something that if you do it, you will love one another: spread peace among yourselves [Muslim]."
"379","On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A man visited a brother of his in another village, and Allah provided for him a property along his path.” He mentioned the hadith to his saying: “Allah has loved you as you have loved Him” [Narrated by Muslim, and we have already mentioned the chapter before it]."
"380","On the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said about the Ansar: “No one loves them except a believer, and no one hates them except a hypocrite. Whoever loves them, Allah loves him, and whoever hates them, Allah hates him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"381","On the authority of Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Allah Almighty said: Those who love one another for the sake of My majesty will have platforms of light, and the prophets and martyrs will envy them.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"382","And on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, may Allah have mercy on him, he said: I entered the Damascus Mosque, and I saw a bright young man, and people were with him. If they disagreed about something, they attributed it to him and followed his opinion. So I asked about him, and it was said: This is Muadh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him. So when it was the next day, I left, and I found that he had preceded me in arriving at the mosque, and I found him praying, so I waited for him until he finished his prayer, then I came to him before his face, so I greeted him. Then I said: By Allah, I love you. He said: By Allah? He said: Allah. He said: By Allah? He said: Allah. So he took me by the handle of my robe and pulled me to him. He said: Good news, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Allah Almighty said: My love is obligatory for those who love one another for Me, those who sit together for Me, and those who visit one another, and those who exchange favors for Me.” An authentic hadith [Narrated by Malik in Fi al-Muwatta with its authentic chain of transmission]."
"383","On the authority of Abu Karima Al-Miqdad bin Ma’d Yakrib, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “If a man loves his brother, let him tell him that he loves him” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"384","On the authority of Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took his hand and said: “O Muadh, by Allah, I love you. Then I advise you, O Muadh, not to stop saying at the end of every prayer: O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well.” An authentic hadith, [Narrated by Abu Dawud and Al-Nasa’i with an authentic chain of transmission]."
"385","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man was with the Prophet (ﷺ) and a man passed by him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I love this. The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: “Did you inform him (of your love)?” He said: “No.” He said: “Inform him.” So he followed him and said: I love you for the sake of Allah, so he said: Allah loves you, for Whom you have loved me. His. [Abu Dawud]."
"386","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah Almighty said: ‘Whoever harms a friend of Mine, I have declared war upon him, and my servant does not approach me with anything more beloved to me than what I have made obligatory upon him. And he continues to draw near to Me with voluntary acts until I love him. Then when I love him, I am his hearing with which he hears, his sight with which he sees, his hand with which he strikes, and his foot with which he walks, and if he asks Me, I will give him, and if he seeks My refuge, I will seek refuge with him.” [Al-Bukhari]"
"387","And on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “If Allah loves a servant, he calls out to Gabriel: Allah Almighty loves so-and-so, so love him, and Gabriel loves him, and he calls out to the people of heaven: Allah loves so-and-so, so love him, so the people of heaven love him, then acceptance is granted to him on earth” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “When Allah Almighty loves a servant, he calls Gabriel and says: I love so-and-so, so I love him, and Gabriel loves him. Then he calls in heaven and says: Allah loves so-and-so, so love him, and the people of heaven love him. Then acceptance is given to him on earth. And if he hates a servant, he calls Gabriel and says: I hate so-and-so, so hate him. Then Gabriel hates him, then he calls out to the people of heaven, “Allah hates so-and-so, so hate him, and then hatred will be created for him on earth.”"
"388","And on the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent a man on a mission, and he would recite to his companions during their prayer, and he would conclude with {Say, He is Allah One.} So when they returned, they mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: “Ask him for what he was doing that for?” So they asked him, and he said: Because it is an attribute of the Most Merciful, so I like to recite it, so he said. the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): “Tell him that Allah Almighty loves him” (Agreed upon)."
"389","On the authority of Jundub bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah, so Allah will not ask you for anything of His protection, for whoever asks of him for something of His protection, He will grant it to him, then throw him on his face into the fire of Hell. [Muslim]."
"390","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I have been commanded to fight people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and perform prayer and pay zakat. If they do that, their blood and their wealth will be protected from me except for the right of Islam, and their reckoning will be with Allah Almighty” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"391","On the authority of Abu Abdullah Tariq bin Ashim, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Whoever says there is no god but Allah, and disbelieves in what is worshiped other than Allah, his wealth and blood will be forbidden, and his reckoning will be with Allah Almighty” [Muslim]."
"392","On the authority of Abu Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): What do you think if I meet a man from the infidels, and we fight, and he strikes one of my hands with a sword, cutting it off, then takes refuge from me in a tree, and says, “I have submitted to Allah. Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he said it?” He said: “Do not kill him. If you kill him, and you are in the position he was before he said the word that he said” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. ((And the meaning is that he is in your position, i.e.: innocent of blood, ruled by his conversion to Islam, and the meaning is that you are in his position, i.e.: blood is permissible by retaliation for his heirs, not that it is in his position in disbelief. And Allah knows best)."
"393","On the authority of Osama bin Zaid, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent us to Al-Harqa of Juhayna, so we led the people in the morning at their waters, and I and a man from the Ansar followed a man from among them, and when we overshadowed him, he said: There is no god but Allah, so the Ansari stopped him, and I stabbed him with my spear until I killed him. When we came to Medina, that news reached the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said to me: ""O Osama, did you kill him after he said there is no god but Allah?! I said, O Messenger of Allah, he was only seeking refuge, so he said, 'You killed him after he said there is no god but Allah?!'"" He kept repeating it until I wished I had not converted to Islam before that day. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration: Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said “He said: There is no god but Allah and you killed him?! I said: O Messenger of Allah, he only said it out of fear of weapons. He said: “Did you not open his heart so that you would know whether he said it or not?!” He continued repeating it until I wished I had converted to Islam that day."
"394","On the authority of Jundub bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent a delegation of Muslims to a people of the polytheists, and they met, so if a man of the polytheists wanted to go to a man of the Muslims, he would go to him and kill him, and that a man from the Muslims took advantage of his negligence, and we were talking that it was Osama bin Zaid, so when he raised the sword against him, he said: There is no god but Allah, and he killed him, so the good news came to the Messenger of Allah, May Allah’s (ﷺ) so he asked him and told him, until he told him what the man had done, so he called him and asked him, and he said: “Why did you kill him?” He said: O Messenger of Allah, he was the most harmful to the Muslims. He killed so-and-so and so-and-so - and he named a group for him - and I attacked him. When he saw the sword, he said: There is no god but Allah. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “You killed him?” He said, “Yes.” He said: “So how will you do with There is no god but Allah, when the Day of Resurrection comes?” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness for me.” He said: “How will you do with There is no god but Allah when the Day of Resurrection comes?” So he did nothing more than say: “How will you do with There is no god but Allah when the Day of Resurrection comes?” [Muslim]."
"395","On the authority of Abdullah bin Utbah bin Masoud, he said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: “People used to take revelation during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) even though the revelation had stopped, but we take them now according to what has appeared to us of your deeds. Whoever shows us good, we trust him and bring him closer, and we have nothing of his secret. He said: “His inner disposition is good” [Al-Bukhari]."
"396","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he is the truthful and trustworthy, told us: “The creation of one of you is gathered in his mother’s womb for forty days as a sperm, then he becomes a clot like that, then he becomes an embryo like that, then the angel is sent, and the spirit is breathed into him, and he is commanded with four words: write down his livelihood, his term, his work, and wretched or blessed. By the One besides whom there is no god. One of you may do the work of the people of Paradise until there is only an arm's length between him and it, then what is written overtakes him, so he does the work of the people of Hell and enters it. And one of you may act with the deeds of the people of Hell until there is only an arm's length between him and it, then what is written overtakes him and he does the work of the people of Paradise and enters it. (Agreed upon)"
"397","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Hell will be brought that day with seventy thousand reins, with seventy thousand angels pulling it on each rein” [Muslim]."
"398","On the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “The easiest torment for the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection will be a man who will have two coals placed in the soles of his feet, from which his brain will boil. He will not see that anyone is more tormented than him, and indeed he will be the least tormented by them” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"399","On the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Among them is some whom the Fire will take to his ankles, and some it will take to his knees, and some it will take it to his waist, and some it will take it to his collarbone” [Muslim]. The clavicle, with fatha ta’ and dhammah al-qaf, is the bone at the opening of the throat, and humans have two clavicles on either side of the throat.’)"
"400","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The people stand up to the Lord of the Worlds until one of them disappears in his sweat to the middle of his ears” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. [And al-rashah: sweat]."
"401","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave us a sermon the likes of which I had never heard. He said: “If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and cry a lot.” Then the companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) covered their faces, and they were sobbing. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration: News reached the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) concerning his companions, so he delivered a sermon, and said: “I was presented with Paradise and Hell, but I have not seen good and evil like today. If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and cry a lot.” When the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not come upon a day more severe than this, they covered their heads and were sobbing."
"402","On the authority of Al-Miqdad, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “The sun will draw near to the creation on the Day of Resurrection until it will be as close as a mile away from them.” Salim bin Aamir, the narrator, said on the authority of Al-Miqdad: By Allah, I do not know what a mile means, the distance of the earth or the mile with which the eye is kohl-lined. The people will be [in sweat] according to their deeds: some of them up to their ankles, some up to their knees, some up to their waists, and some will be bridled by sweat.” the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) pointed to his mouth with his hand [Muslim]."
"403","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The people will sweat on the Day of Resurrection until their sweat sinks into the earth seventy cubits, and the sweat will bridle them until it reaches their ears.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. )"
"404","On his authority, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he heard a loud noise and he said: “Do you know what this is?” We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is a stone that was thrown into the fire seventy years ago, and it is now falling in the fire until it has reached its bottom, so you heard its sound. [Muslim]"
"405","On the authority of Adi bin Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is not one of you except that his Lord will speak to him, with no interpreter between him and him. So he looks to his right and sees nothing but what he has presented, and he looks to his left and sees nothing but what he has presented, and he looks in front of him and sees nothing but the Fire in front of his face, so avoid the Fire, even if it is with a half of a date.” (Agreed upon) (on him).."
"406","On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I see what you do not see; the sky creaked, and it was right that it creaked, and there is not room for four fingers in it except for an angel placing his forehead in prostration to Allah Almighty. By Allah, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and cry a lot, and you would not enjoy women on beds, and you would go out to the ascents, seeking Allah Almighty. Almighty” [Al-Tirmidhi]. And it is folded with the opening of the hamza and the tightening of the ta’, and it is folded with the opening of the ta’ and after it is a broken hamza, and the folding is the sound of saddlebags and qutab and their like, and its meaning is: that the large number of worshiping angels in the sky has burdened it to the point that it creaked."
"407","On the authority of Abu Barzah - Baraa then Zay - Nadlah bin Ubaid Al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about his life and how he spent it, about his knowledge and what he did with it, about his money from where he earned it and on what he spent it, and about his body and how he used it up” ([Al-Tirmidhi]"
"408","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited {On that day she will narrate her news} and then said: “Do you know what her news is?” They said, Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: “For her news is that every male or female slave will bear witness to what was done on her back, saying: She did such-and-such on such-and-such a day, so this is her news.” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"409","On the authority of Abu Saadi Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “How can he be blessed when the owner of the horn has placed the horn in his mouth, and he listens to the permission when he is commanded to blow and blow?” So it was as if that was a burden on the companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said to them: “Say: Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs.” ([Al-Tirmidhi] Hassan)."
"410","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever fears Allah will travel at night, and whoever travels at night will reach the destination. Indeed, Allah’s commodity is expensive, but Allah’s commodity is Paradise” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"411","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “The people will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection, barefoot and naked.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, are all men and women looking at each other? He said: “O Aisha, the matter is too severe for them to care about that.” And in a narration: “The matter is more momentous than [the issue of] some of them looking at one another.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"412","On the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that Jesus is Allah’s servant and Messenger, and His word which He bestowed on Mary and a spirit from Him, and that Paradise is true and Hell is true, Allah will admit him to Paradise regardless of his deeds” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] In a narration by Muslim: “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, Hell will be forbidden to him.”"
"413","On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Allah Almighty says: Whoever does a good deed will receive ten times it or more, and whoever does a bad deed, the reward for a bad deed will be an evil like it or I will be forgiven. And whoever draws near to Me by a span, I will draw near to him by a cubit, and whoever draws near to Me by a cubit, I will draw near to him by a length, and whoever comes to Me walking, I will come to him running., and whoever meets me with a sin nearly as great as the earth, not associating anything with Him, I will meet him with forgiveness equal to it.” [Muslim]"
"414","On the authority of Jabir, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet and said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the two decisive matters [that determine one's eternal fate]? He said: “Whoever dies associating nothing with Allah will enter Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Him will enter Hell.” [Muslim]"
"415","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) and Mu’adh, his companion on the journey, said: “O Mu’adh.” He said: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and I am pleased with you.” Three times, he said: “There is no servant who bears witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, truthfully from his heart, except that Allah has forbidden him to Hell.” He said: O Messenger of Allah, should I not tell the people about it so that they will be rejoiced? He said: “then they will rely [solely on this testimony and abandon good deeds],” so he informed Mu'adh of it when he was dying, out of fear of sin [for not having conveyed it to him earlier]. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"416","On the authority of Abu Hurairah - or Abu Saeed Al-Khudri - may Allah be pleased with them both: The narrator doubted, and doubt does not harm the eyes of the Companions: Because they are all just. He said: When the Battle of Tabuk took place, a famine struck the people, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, if you would give us permission, we would slaughter our watering camels and consume their meat and milk? So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do it.” So he came. Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, if you do, shorten the noon prayer, but ask them for their leftover provisions, then pray to Allah for blessings on them, perhaps Allah will put a blessing in that. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Yes,” so he called for a portion of food and spread it out, then he called for the portion of their provisions, so each man came with a handful of millet, another with a handful of dates, and another with a crumb of bread, until a small amount of food was gathered on the tray. then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) invoked blessings upon the food, then said: “Take your containers.” They took their containers until they did not leave a container in the soldiers without filling it, and they ate until they were full and there was leftover. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that I am the Messenger of Allah. No servant of Allah will meet them without doubting.” He will be blocked from Paradise” [Muslim]."
"417","On the authority of Itban bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who was one of those who witnessed Badr, he said: I was praying for my people, Banu Salem, and there was a valley between me and them when the rain came, and it was difficult for me to cross it before their mosque. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said to him: I denied my sight, and the valley between me and my people would flow when the rain came, so it would be difficult for me to cross it, so I wanted you to You come and pray in my house in a place that I use as a prayer place. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I will do that.” So they went to the Messenger of Allah and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, after the day had become intense. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked permission, so I gave him permission. He did not sit down until he said: “Where would you like me to pray in your house?” So I pointed to him the place I would like to pray. He prayed in it, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood up, and we lined up behind him, so he prayed two rak’ahs, then he greeted us and greeted us when he said his salutation, so I kept him as a guest to eat the khazeera (meat and grain dish) that was prepared for him, so the people of the house heard that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was in my house, and some of them jumped up until there were many men in the house, and a man said: What is the matter with Malik? I do not see him here! Another man said: That is a hypocrite who does not love Allah and His Messenger, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not say that. Have you not seen him say: There is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the face of Allah Almighty?” He said: “Allah and His Messenger know best. As for us, by Allah, we do not see his love, nor his speech except the hypocrites.” Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “For Allah has forbidden to Hell whoever says: There is no god but Allah.” In doing so, he seeks the face of Allah” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. (‘Itban with a kasra on the neglected eye, and placing the double ta’ over it and after them a unified b. And the khazeera with the lexicalized kha, and the za: it is flour cooked with lard. And his saying: Tha’ab rijal with the tha’. The triangle, meaning: they came and gathered.')"
"418","On the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came with captives, and suddenly a woman from among the captives was running. When she found a boy in the captivity, she took him, pressed him to her bosom, and breastfed him. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do you see this woman throwing her child into the fire?” We said, “No, by Allah.” He said: “Allah is more merciful to His servants than This mother with her child” (Agreed upon)."
"419","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “When Allah created creation, He wrote it down in a book, which is with Him above the throne: My mercy prevails over my wrath.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"420","And on his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Allah made mercy into one hundred parts, and with Him He kept ninety-nine, and sent down one part to the earth. From that part, He shows mercy to creatures until an animal raises its hoof from its calf for fear that it will harm it.” And in a narration: “Allah Almighty has one hundred mercies, of which He has sent down one mercy, between jinn, mankind, and beasts.” And vermin, through it they sympathize, and through it they show compassion, and through it the beast shows compassion for its child, and Allah Almighty has delayed ninety-nine mercies with which He will have mercy on His servants on the Day of Resurrection” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. It was also narrated by Muslim from the narration of Salman Al-Farsi, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah Almighty has a hundred mercies, and of them is one mercy.” Through it, creation shows compassion to one another, and the remaining ninety-nine mercies are for the Day of Resurrection. “And in a narration: “On the day He created the heavens and the earth, Allah Almighty created a hundred mercies, each mercy equal to what is between the heavens and the earth. Then He made of them a mercy on the earth, in which a mother has compassion for her child, and animals and birds have compassion for one another. So when the Day of Resurrection comes, He will complete it with this mercy.”"
"421","And on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) in what is narrated about his Lord, Blessed and Most High, he said: “My servant committed a sin, and he said: O Allah, forgive me my sin. Then Allah, Blessed and Most High, said: My servant committed a sin, so he knew that he had a Lord who forgives sins and punishes for the sin. Then he sinned again and said: O Lord, forgive me my sin. Then Allah Blessed and Most High said: My servant sinned. He committed a sin, so he knew that he had a Lord who forgives sins and punishes for the sin. Then he sinned again and said: “O Lord, forgive me my sin.” He said, Blessed and Most High: My servant committed a sin, so he knew that he had a Lord who forgives sins and punishes for the sin. I have forgiven my servant, so let him do what he wants. And the Almighty says: “Let him do what he wants.” He willed, meaning: As long as he does this, he sins and repents, forgive him, for repentance destroys what came before it."
"422","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you had not sinned, Allah would have taken you away and brought a people who would sin and seek forgiveness from Allah Almighty, and He would forgive them” [Muslim]."
"423","On the authority of Abu Ayoub Khalid bin Zaid, may Allah be pleased with him, he said I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “If you had not sinned, Allah would have created a creation to sin, and they would ask forgiveness, and He would forgive them” [Muslim]."
"424","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with us Abu Bakr and Omar, may Allah be pleased with them, with a group. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) rose from among us, and slowed down for us, so we feared that he would cut us off, so we were terrified, so we got up, and I was the first to be terrified, so I went out in search of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) until I came to a wall. To the Ansar - and he mentioned the hadith in its length up to his saying: Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Go, and whoever you meet behind this wall bears witness that there is no god but Allah, being certain in his heart, so give him good tidings of Paradise” [Muslim]."
"425","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (ﷺ) recited the words of Allah Almighty regarding Abraham (ﷺ): {My Lord, they have misled many people. Whoever follows me is of me} [Ibrahim: 36], and the saying of Jesus (ﷺ): {If You punish them, then they are Your servants. And if You forgive them, You are the Mighty, the Wise.} [Al-Ma’idah: 118] Then he raised his hands and said: “O Allah, my nation,” and wept, and Allah Almighty said: “O Gabriel, go to Muhammad, and your Lord knows best, and ask him why he is crying?” So Gabriel came to him, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) informed him [Gabriel] of what he had said. And Allah is the Most Knowing, so Allah Almighty said: “O Gabriel, go to Muhammad and say: We will please you regarding your nation and will not treat you wrong.” [Muslim]."
"426","On the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a donkey, and he said: “O Muadh, do you know what the right of Allah is upon His servants, and what the right of the servants is upon Allah?” I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: “The right of Allah upon the servants is that they worship Him, and not associate anything with Him, and the right of the servants upon Allah is that He does not punish those who do not associate anything with Him, so I said, O Messenger of Allah, should I not give good tidings to the people? He said, “Do not give them good tidings lest they rely” (Agreed upon)."
"427","On the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “When a Muslim is asked in the grave, he bears witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. That is the Almighty’s saying: {Allah establishes those who believe with the firm word in this life and in the hereafter} [Ibrahim: 27] (Agreed upon). (on him).."
"428","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “When an infidel does a good deed, he is given a portion of this world with it, but as for the believer, Allah Almighty stores up for him his good deeds in the hereafter, and gives him sustenance in this world for his obedience.” And in a narration: “Allah does not wrong a believer for a good deed with which he is given in this world and rewarded with it in the hereafter.” As for the disbeliever, he is fed with the good deeds of what he did for Allah Almighty in this world, until when it leads to the Hereafter, he has no good deed to be rewarded with.” [Muslim]"
"429","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The example of the five daily prayers is like a flowing, abundant river at the door of one of you from which he washes five times every day” [Muslim]. (‘Al-Ghamr: abundant.’)"
"430","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “There is no Muslim man who dies and forty men who do not associate anything with Allah stand up for his funeral except that Allah intercedes for them for the sake of the deceased.” [Muslim]."
"431","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in a dome of about forty people, and he said: “Would you be satisfied to be a quarter of the people of Paradise?” We said: Yes. He said: Would you be satisfied to be a third of the people of Paradise? We said: Yes. He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, Muhammad, I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise, and that is Only a Muslim soul will enter Paradise, and you are not among the people of polytheism except as a white hair in the skin of a black bull, or as a black hair in the skin of a red bull.” (Agreed upon)"
"432","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If on the Day of Resurrection Allah will hand over to every Muslim a Jew or a Christian, he will say: ‘This is your redemption from Hell.’” And in a narration from him on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “On the Day of Resurrection, some Muslims will come with sins as great as mountains, and Allah will forgive them.” (Narrated by him) Muslim).."
"433","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: On the Day of Resurrection, the believer will approach his Lord until He places His shroud over him, and He will make him confess his sins. He will say: Do you know the sin of such-and-such? Do you know the sin of such-and-such? Then he will say: My Lord, I know. He said: For I have covered it for you in this world, and I will forgive it for you today, and he will be given a record of his good deeds. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. [His shroud: His covering and mercy]."
"434","And on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man received a kiss from a woman, so he came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and told him, so Allah Almighty revealed: {And establish prayer during the two ends of the day and part of the night. Indeed, good deeds remove bad deeds} [Hud: 114] Then the man said: What is this for, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “For all my nation.” All of them” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"435","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a punishment, so perform it on me, and I attended the prayer. He prayed with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and when he finished the prayer, he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a punishment, so fulfill the Book of Allah. He said: “Did you attend the prayer with us?” He said: Yes. He said: “You have been forgiven.” (Agreed upon)"
"436","On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah is pleased with a servant when he eats a meal, and praises Him for it, or drinks a drink, and praises Him for it.” [Muslim]."
"437","On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said, “Indeed, Allah Almighty extends His Hand at night so that the sinner of the day may repent, and He extends His Hand during the day so that the sinner of the night may repent, until the sun rises from the west” [Muslim]."
"438","On the authority of Abu Najih Amr bin Absa - with the opening of the eye and the letter - Al-Salami, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When I was in pre-Islamic times, I used to think that people were misguided, that they were not upon anything, and that they were worshiping idols, so I heard of a man in Mecca telling news, so I sat on my mount, and came to him, and behold, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was hiding, and his people dared him, so he was kind until I entered upon him in Mecca. So I said to him: What are you? He said: “I am a prophet.” I said: “And what is a prophet?” He said: “Allah sent me.” I said: “With what will I appoint you?” He said: “He sent me to connect family ties, break idols, and to affirm the oneness of Allah, not associating anything with Him.” I said: “Who is with you on this?” He said: “A free man and a slave.” And with him on that day was Abu Bakr and Bilal, may Allah be pleased with them. I said: I am following you. He said: “You will not be able to do that this day of yours. Do you not see my condition and the condition of the people? But go back to your family, and if you hear of me appearing, come to me.” He said: So I went to my family and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to Medina, and I was with my family, so I began to learn the news and ask the people when he came to Medina until he arrived. so I said: What did this man who came to Medina do? They said: People were rushing towards him, and his people wanted to kill him, but they were unable to do so, so I came to Medina and entered upon him, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you recognize me? He said: “Yes, you are the one who met me in Mecca.” He said: So I said, O Messenger of Allah, tell me about what Allah has taught you that I do not know. Tell me about prayer? He said: “Pray the morning prayer, then stop praying until the sun rises the length of a spear, for it rises when it rises between the horns of Satan, and at that time the infidels prostrate to it. Then pray, for the prayer is witnessed and attended until the shadow is equal to the length of a spear, then stop praying, for then Hell will burn; then when the shade (after noon) comes, pray; Prayer is witnessed and attended until you pray the afternoon prayer, then refrain from prayer until the sun sets, for it sets between the horns of Satan, and at that time the disbelievers prostrate to it.” He said: So I said: O Prophet of Allah, tell me about ablution? He said: “There is not a man among you who approaches his ablution, then rinses his mouth and inhales it, but the sins fall out on his face, in his mouth, and in his nostrils, and then when he washes His face is as Allah commanded him, unless the sins of his face fall down from the ends of his beard with the water, then he washes his hands to the elbows, unless the sins of his hands fall down from his fingertips with water and then he wipes his head, unless the sins of his hands fall down from his fingertips with water, then he washes his hands up to the elbows, unless the sins of his hands fall down from his fingertips with the water then he wipes his head, unless the sins of his head fall down from the ends of his hair with water, then he washes his forefoot to the ankles unless sins fall out. His feet from his fingertips to the water, and if he stood up and prayed, then he praised Allah Almighty, and praised and glorified him for the one to whom he is worthy, and his heart was emptied for Allah Almighty, unless he departed from his sin as he looked on the day his mother gave birth to him.” So Amr ibn Absa narrated this hadith to Abu Umamah, a companion of the Messenger of Allah, and Abu Umamah said to him: O Amr ibn Absa, see what you say! In one position will this man be given? So he said. Amr: O Abu Umamah, my age has grown, my bones have thinned, and my end is approaching, and I have no need to lie to Allah Almighty, nor to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). If I had not heard it from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) except once, twice, or three times, until he counted seven times, I would never have spoken to him, but I heard him more than that [Muslim]."
"439","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “If Allah Almighty wanted mercy for a nation, He took its prophet before it, and made it a privilege and advance for it in its hands, and if He wanted to destroy a nation, He tortured it while its prophet was alive, and destroyed it while it was alive and watching, so He approved of its destruction when they lied to him and disobeyed His command.” [Muslim]."
"440","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he said: “Allah, the Almighty, said: I am as my servant thinks of me and I am with him wherever he remembers me. By Allah, I rejoice more at the repentance of My servant than any of you rejoices at finding his lost camel in the desert. And whoever draws near to Me by a span, I draw near to him by a cubit, and whoever draws near to Me by a cubit, I draw near to him by a length, and if he comes to me walking, I come to him running.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. This is the wording of one of Muslim’s narrations. Its explanation was presented in the chapter before it. It was narrated in the two Sahih books: “And I am with him when he reminds me” with the letter “nun,” and in this narration “where” with the tha’, and both are authentic."
"441","On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) three days before his death, saying: “None of you will die except with a good opinion of Allah Almighty” [Muslim]."
"442","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Allah Almighty said: O son of Adam, as long as you call on Me and hope in Me, I will forgive you for what you did, and I do not care. O son of Adam, if your sins reached the clouds of the sky, and then you asked for My forgiveness, I would forgive you. O son of Adam, if you brought to Me sins nearly as great as the earth, and then met Me, associating nothing with Him, I would come to you. With forgiveness nearly as great as it.” [Al-Tirmidhi] He said it was a good hadith.)"
"443","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If the believer knew what Allah has of punishment, no one would covet His Paradise, and if the disbeliever knew what Allah has of mercy, no one would despair of His Paradise” [Muslim]."
"444","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If the funeral takes place and the people or men carry it on their necks, if it is righteous, it says: Hasten me, bring me forward, and if it is not righteous, it says: Oh, woe to her! Where are you taking it? Everything hears his voice except man, and if he hears it, he will be shocked” [Al-Bukhari]."
"445","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Paradise is closer to one of you than the straps of his sandals, and Hell is like that” [Al-Bukhari]."
"446","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said to me, “Recite the Qur’an to me.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, I recite to you, and it was revealed to you?! He said: “I would love to hear it from someone else.” So I recited Surah An-Nisa to him, until I came to this verse (So how if We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you as a witness over these) [An-Nisa: 41] He said: “It is enough for you now.” He turned to him, and saw his eyes streaming with tears. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"447","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon the likes of which I had never heard. He said: “If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and cry a lot.” He said: Then the companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) covered their faces, and they were whimpering softly, [Al-Bukhari and Muslim], and a statement has already been made in the section on fear."
"448","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “A man who wept out of fear of Allah will not enter Hell until the milk returns to the udder, and the dust of Allah’s cause and the smoke of Hell are not combined” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"449","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There are seven whom Allah will shade in His shade on the Day when there will be no shade except His shade: a just imam, a young man who grew up in the worship of Allah, a man whose heart was attached to the mosques, two men who loved one another for the sake of Allah, who gathered for His sake and parted for His sake, and a man who was invited by a woman of position and beauty, and said: I fear Allah, and a man who gave charity and hid it so that his left [hand] does not know what his right [hand] spends.” What his right hand spends, and a man who mentioned Allah alone and his eyes filled with tears” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"450","On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was praying and his chest was emitting a sound like the bubbling of a cauldron from crying. [An authentic hadith narrated by Abu Dawud, and Al-Tirmidhi with an authentic chain of transmission]."
"451","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Ubayy bin Ka’b, may Allah be pleased with him: “Allah Almighty commanded me to recite to you: ‘It was not those who disbelieved.’ Ubayy said: ‘Did he name me?’ He said: ‘Yes’, and my father cried. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. [And in a narration: My father kept crying]."
"452","On his authority, he said: Abu Bakr said to Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, after the death of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): We went to Umm Ayman (ﷺ) and we would visit her as he used to visit her. When we reached her, she cried, and they said: What makes you cry? Don’t you know that what Allah Almighty has is better for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)? She said: I do not cry, [claiming] that I do not know that what is with Allah is better for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), but I cry because the revelation from heaven has stopped, so it provoked them to cry, so they started crying with her. [Narrated by Muslim, and it was previously mentioned in the chapter on visiting good people]."
"453","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: When the pain of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) became severe, he was told during prayer, and he said: “Tell Abu Bakr so that he may pray with the people.” Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: Indeed, Abu Bakr is a gentle man. When he recites the Qur’an, he is overcome with tears, so he said: “Tell him so that he may pray.” And in a narration on the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, She said: I said: If Abu Bakr stood in your place, people would not hear [him] cry. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"454","On the authority of Ibrahim bin Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, that Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought food while he was fasting, and he said: Mus`ab bin Umair, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed, and he was better than me. There was nothing for him to shroud himself with except a cloak. If he covered his head with it, his legs would appear, and if he covered his feet with it, his head would be exposed. Then he extended for us what he extended from the world - or he said: We were given from the world what we were given - we feared that our good deeds would be hastened for us. Then he started crying until he stopped eating. [Al-Bukhari]."
"455","On the authority of Abu Umamah Siddi bin Ajlan Al-Bahili, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “There is nothing more beloved to Allah Almighty than two drops and two traces: a drop of tears out of fear of Allah, and a drop of blood shed for the sake of Allah, and as for the two traces: a trace [left from striving] in the way of Allah Almighty, and a trace [left from performing] one of the obligations of Allah Almighty” ([Al-Tirmidhi] He said the hadith was Hasan). The hadith of Al-Irbad bin Sariyah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) preached to us a sermon that made hearts tremble and eyes shed tears."
"456","On the authority of Amr bin Awf Al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, may Allah be pleased with him, to Bahrain to collect its tribute. He came with money from Bahrain, so the Ansar heard of Abu Ubaidah’s arrival, so they attended the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed, he left and they faced him, and he smiled. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw them, then he said: “I think you heard that Abu Ubaidah came with something from Bahrain?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, and he said: “Give good tidings and hope for what pleases you, for by Allah, I do not fear poverty for you, but I fear that the world will be extended to you as it was extended to those who were before you, and you will compete with it as they competed for it, and it will destroy you as it destroyed them.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"457","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sat on the pulpit, and we sat around him, and he said: “Indeed, what I fear for you after me is that the flower and adornment of the world will be opened to you” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"458","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The world is beautiful and green, and Allah Almighty has appointed you as successors in it. He will see how you do, so fear the world and fear women” [Muslim]."
"459","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Oh Allah, there is no life except the life of the Hereafter” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"460","On his authority, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “Three things follow the dead: his family, his money, and his work: two come back and one remains: his family and money come back and his work remains.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"461","On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The most affluent of the people of this world, of the people of Hell, will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and dipped once in Hell, and then it will be said: O son of Adam, have you ever seen anything good? Have you ever experienced bliss? And he will say: No, by Allah, O Lord. And the most miserable of the people in this world of the people of Paradise will be brought, and he will be dipped once in Paradise, and it will be said: To him: O son of Adam, have you ever seen misery? Has hardship ever troubled you? Then he says: No, by Allah, I have never experienced misery, nor have I ever seen hardship.” [Muslim]."
"462","On the authority of Al-Mustarad bin Shaddad, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “What is this world in the afterlife, except something like when one of you dips his finger into the sea and sees what it comes back with?” [Muslim]."
"463","And on the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by the market while the people were on his sides. He passed by a dead goat, so he took it and took it by the ears. Then he said: “Which of you would like this to be his for a dirham?” They said: “We would not like it to be ours for anything and what to do with it?” Then he said: “Would you like it to be yours?” They said: By Allah, if it were alive it would be. It is a disgrace that he is small-eared. So how could he be dead? He said: “By Allah, this world is easier for Allah than this is for you” [Muslim]. (‘His saying: His palms, meaning: on his sides. And the silence is the small ear.’)"
"464","On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was walking with the Prophet (ﷺ) in a neighborhood in Medina, when one of them called out: “O Abu Dharr.” I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “I am not pleased that I have gold like this of Uhud. Three days have passed and I have a dinar of it, except something I reserve for a debt, unless I say to him about it among the servants of Allah like this, and so and so.” To his right, to his left, and behind him, then he walked and said: “The majority will be the few on the Day of Resurrection, except for those who say, ‘With money like this, so, so, and so on.’ To his right, to his left, and behind him, ‘and they are few.’ Then he said to me, ‘Do not leave where you are until I come to you.’ Then he set off in the darkness of the night until he disappeared. I heard a voice rising, so I feared that someone might have attacked the Prophet (ﷺ) so I wanted to go.” So I mentioned his saying: “Do not leave until I come to you.” I did not leave until he came to me, so I said: I heard a voice that I feared, so I mentioned it to him, and he said: “Did you hear it?” I said: Yes, he said: “That Gabriel came to me and said: Whoever of your nation dies not associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise,” I said: “And if He committed adultery, even if he stole? He said: Even if he committed adultery, even if he stole. (Agreed upon, and this is the wording of Al-Bukhari.)"
"465","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “If I had the equivalent of Uhud in gold, I would be pleased that three nights would not pass by and I had nothing of it except something I would reserve for a debt” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"466","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Look at the one who is below you and do not look at the one who is above you, for he is more worthy that you should not disdain the blessings of Allah upon you” [Agreed upon, and this is a Muslim wording]. And in the narration of Al-Bukhari: “If one of you looks at the one who has superiority over him in money and character, let him look at the one who is lower than him.” Al-Bukhari: “If one of you looks at someone who is superior to him in money and character, let him look at someone who is inferior to him.”"
"467","And on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “A miserable servant of the dinar, the dirham, the velvet, and the khameesa; if he gives, he is satisfied; if he does not give, he is not satisfied” [Al-Bukhari]."
"468","And on his authority, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw seventy of the people of Suffah, and not one of them was a man wearing a robe, either a garment or a cloak, tied around their necks. Some of them reached half the length of the legs, and some reached the length of the ankles, so he gathered them together with his hand for fear that his private parts would be seen” [Al-Bukhari]."
"469","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the infidel” [Muslim]."
"470","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took me by the shoulders and said: “Be in this world as if you were a stranger, or a passerby.” And Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to say: If you arrive in the evening, do not wait for the morning, and when morning comes, do not wait for the evening, and take from your health for your illness and from your life for your death. [Al-Bukhari]."
"471","On the authority of Abu Abbas Sahl bin Saad Al-Saadi, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed that if I do, Allah will love me and the people will love me. So he said: “Avoid the world and Allah will love you, and renounce what the people have and the people will love you” [A good hadith narrated by Ibn Majah and others with good chains of transmission]."
"472","On the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, mentioned what befell people in this world, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) continuing today to squirm with what he could find of daqal to fill his stomach with. [Muslim]. Daqal with the opening of the neglected daal and the qaf: bad dates."
"473","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) died, and there is nothing in my house that a person with a liver would eat except a piece of barley on a shelf of mine, so I ate some of it until it became too long for me, so I ate it and it was gone."
"474","On the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, brother of Al-Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith, Mother of the Believers, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not leave behind a dinar or a dirham, nor a male slave, nor a female slave, or anything except his white mule that he used to ride, his weapon, and land that he gave to the wayfarer as charity” [Al-Bukhari]."
"475","On the authority of Khabbab bin Al-Art, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to seek the face of Allah Almighty. So our reward fell on Allah, and among us were those who died and did not eat any of their reward. Among them was Mus’ab bin Umair, may Allah be pleased with him. He was killed on the day of Uhud and left behind a nimar, so when we covered his head with it, his legs would be visible, and if we covered his legs with it, his head would be visible. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered us to cover his head and place some of the Idhkhir on his feet. And among us was he who had fruit ripened, so he would give it away. ((Agreed) (on him). Nimrah: a striped woolen garment. And his saying: “Ina’at” means: it has matured and matured. And his saying “he guides her” which is with the opening of the yā’ and the ḍamma of the ḍāl and its kasra are two languages; That is, he picks it and reaps it, and this is a metaphor for what Allah Almighty has opened up to them in this world and they have mastered it."
"476","On the authority of Sahl bin Saad Al-Saadi, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If the world were equivalent to Allah as the wing of a mosquito, He would not give an unbeliever a drink of water from it” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"477","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, “The world is cursed, and cursed is what is in it, except for the remembrance of Allah Almighty, and what follows Him, and the knowledgeable and the learner.” [Al-Tirmidhi]. ((Narrated by Al-Tirmidhi said: It is a good hadith"
"478","On the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not take the estate lest you desire this world.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"479","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by us while we were repairing our small tent. He said: “What is this?” So we said: “It has worn out, so we are repairing it.” He said: “I do not see the matter being anything more urgent than that.” Narrated by Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi with the chain of transmission of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, and he said: Al-Tirmidhi: [Hasan Sahih Hadith]."
"480","On the authority of Kaab bin Iyad, may Allah be pleased with him, who said I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Every nation has a temptation, and the temptation of my nation is money” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"481","On the authority of Abu Amr, and it is said: Abu Abdullah: and it is said: Abu Laila, Uthman Ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “The son of Adam has no right to anything other than these qualities: a house in which he lives, a garment to cover his private parts, and julf al-khubz (plain/coarse bread, or bread without condiment) and water” [Al-Tirmidhi]. [Al-Tirmidhi said: I heard Abu Dawud Sulaiman bin Salim Al-Balkhi say: I heard Al-Nadr bin Shumail say: Julf: bread that has no condiment (idam) with it. Someone else said: It is thick bread. Al-Harawi said: What is meant here is a bread container, like the julaq and the kharj, and Allah knows best]."
"482","And on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, “Biskar Al-Shain and Al-Kha’ Al-Mushada with the two emphasized (shadda) letters,” may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was reciting: {Increase has distracted you}. He said: “The son of Adam says: My money, and do you, son of Adam, have any of your money except what I ate and used up, or I wore and wore out, or I gave in charity and spent it?” [Muslim]."
"483","On the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man said to the Prophet (ﷺ) O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I love you. He said: “Look, what are you saying?” He said: “By Allah, I love you,” three times. Then he said: “If you love me, prepare for poverty by donning steadfastness like a protective covering (tajfaf), for poverty reaches those who love me faster than a flood reaches its end.” [Al-Tirmidhi] 'The dryness is made by breaking the double ta' above and isskaning the jem and with the repeated fa', and it is something that the horse wears, to protect himself from harm, and it may be worn by humans.'"
"484","On the authority of Ka’b bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Two hungry wolves sent to kill sheep do not spoil them more than a person’s desire for money and honor corrupts his religion” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"485","And on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slept on a mat, and he said, and it affected his side. We said: O Messenger of Allah, if we had made a bedding for you! He said: “What about this world? I am in this world only like a rider who took shade under a tree and then departed and left it.” ([Al-Tirmidhi] True).."
"486","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The poor will enter Paradise five hundred years before the rich” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"487","On the authority of Ibn Abbas and Imran bin Al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) “He said: “I looked into Paradise and saw most of its people being poor, and I looked into Hell and saw most of its people were women” [Agreed upon from the narration of Ibn Abbas]. ((It was also narrated by Al-Bukhari from the narration of Imran bin Al-Husayn).."
"488","On the authority of Osama bin Zaid, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “I stood at the gate of Paradise, and most of those who entered it were the poor. And the people of wealth and fortune are imprisoned, but the companions of Hell have been commanded to go to hell” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And ((Al-jadd: luck and wealth. This hadith has previously been explained in the chapter The virtue of weakness)."
"489","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “The truest word ever said by a poet is the word of Labid: Everything except Allah is false.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"490","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The family of Muhammad (ﷺ) had never had enough of barley bread for two consecutive days until he died. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration: The family of Muhammad (ﷺ) had never had enough of wheat food for three nights in a row until he died."
"491","And on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that she used to say: By Allah, my sister’s son, if we were to look at the crescent, then the crescent: three crescents in two months, and and no fire was ever lit in the houses of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) I said: O aunt, what was your livelihood? She said: The two black ones: dates and water, except that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had neighbors from the Ansar, and they had They used to send some of their milk to the Messenger of Allah, so he would give us drink. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"492","On the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he passed by a people with a roasted sheep before them, and they invited him, but he refused to eat, and he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) left the world and was not satisfied with barley bread. [Al-Bukhari]."
"493","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) did not eat on a plate until he died, and he did not eat thin, puffed bread until he died. [Al-Bukhari]. [And in his narration: He never saw a greasy sheep with his own eyes]."
"494","On the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I saw your Prophet (ﷺ) and he could never find enough bad dates to fill his stomach, [Muslim]. [Dhal: bad dates]."
"495","On the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not eat thin, baked bread (نقي) from the time Allah Almighty sent him until Allah Almighty took him, He was asked: Did you have sieves during the reign of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)? He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not see a sieve from the time Allah Almighty sent him until Allah Almighty took him. So he was told: How? Did you eat barley that was not sifted? He said: We used to grind it and blow it, and what flew away, and what remained, we moistened and kneaded [Al-Bukhari]. It is a triangular ba'a, then a stressed ra', then a double ya' from under it, then a nun, meaning: We made it wet and kneaded it.'))"
"496","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out one day or night, and he found Abu Bakr and Omar, may Allah be pleased with them, and he said: “What has brought you out of your homes at this hour?” They said: Hunger, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “And I, by the One in whose hand is my soul, the one who brought you out will have brought me out. Arise.” So they stood up with him, and went to a man from the Ansar, but he was not in his house. When the woman saw him, she said: Hello and welcome, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to her, “Where is so-and-so?” She said, “He went to fetch water for us, when the Ansari came and looked at the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and his two companions. Then he said: Praise be to Allah, no one today has more generous guests than me.” So he set off and brought them a stalk of dates in it. And he said: Eat, and he took the knife, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Beware of milk.” So he slaughtered for them, and they ate from the sheep and from that stalk and drank. When they were full and drank, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Abu Bakr and Omar, may Allah be pleased with them: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will ask about this bliss on the Day of Resurrection. Hunger drove you out of your homes, and then you did not return until This bliss has befallen you.” [Muslim]. And its kasra means the knife. And the milkmaids are full of milk. The question about the Ansari who came to him is Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayhan, may Allah be pleased with him. This was stated clearly in the narration of al-Tirmidhi and others.)"
"497","On the authority of Khaled bin Omar Al-Adawi, he said: Utbah bin Ghazwan, who was the Emir of Basra, addressed us, so he praised and praised Allah, then said: As for what follows; For the world has indicated its end and is passing by quickly, and nothing remains of it except a slurry like the slurry of a vessel that its owner catches, and you are moving from it to an abode that will never disappear, so move with the best that you have, for it has been mentioned to us that a stone is thrown from the edge of Hellfire and falls therein for seventy years, not reaching a bottom for it, and by Allah it will be filled... so are you amazed!? And it has been mentioned to us that the space between two shutters is From the gates of Paradise, it is a journey of forty years, and a day will come when it will be like heavy crowds, and I saw that I was the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and we had no food except the leaves of trees, until our throats were sore, so I picked up a cloak and split it between me and Saad bin Malik, so I girded with half of it, and Saad girded with half of it. Today, not one of us has become the ruler of Egypt from the regions, and I seek refuge in Allah from being in myself. Great, but in the sight of Allah, small. [Muslim]. His saying: I have given notice is the extension of the alif, meaning: I have informed. And his saying: bisram: it is with the ḍamma of the ṣad, meaning with its cessation and annihilation. And his saying, “Walāt a shoe” is a neglected, open baha, then dhaal. A stressed dictionary, then an extended alif, i.e. fast. And the sababa with the ḍamma of the neglected ṣad: it is the easy remainder. And his saying: he suffices with it is by tightening the ba before the ha, i.e. he brings it together. It is with the opening of the qāf and the kasra of the rā’, meaning: it has sores on it."
"498","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, brought out for us a garment and a thick garment. She said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed away in these two [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"499","On the authority of Saeed bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I am the first of the Arabs to shoot an arrow for the sake of Allah, and we used to fight with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and we had no food except fenugreek leaves, this samr. So much so that if one of us ate it as a sheep eats, he would have no waste (stool) from it. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. Two well-known types of desert trees..."
"500","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O Allah, make the sustenance of Muhammad’s (ﷺ) family sufficient to meet their basic needs” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. Linguists explain that the meaning of “qoot (sufficiency)” is: that which staves off hunger and meets essential needs."
"501","On the authority of Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""By Allah, besides Whom there is no god, I used to press my liver against the ground from hunger, and I would tie a stone over my stomach from hunger. One day I sat on the path from which they used to emerge. The Prophet (ﷺ) passed by me, and when he saw me he smiled, recognizing what was on my face and in my heart. Then he said: ""O Abu Hirr!"" I replied: ""At your service, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Come along!"" and walked on. I followed him until he entered (a house). He asked permission and I was allowed, so I entered and found a bowl of milk. He asked: ""Where did this milk come from?"" They replied: ""So-and-so sent it as a gift to you."" He said: ""O Abu Hirr!"" I said: ""At your service, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Go to the people of As-Suffah and summon them to me."" (The people of As-Suffah were the guests of Islam who had no families or wealth. Whenever a gift came to the Prophet (ﷺ) he would send for them and share it with them.) This displeased me, and I thought: ""What is this milk to the people of As-Suffah? I deserve to drink from this milk to strengthen myself. When they come and he orders me to serve them, what will be left for me?"" But there was no alternative but to obey Allah and His Messenger. So I went to them and summoned them, and they came and sought permission, which was granted. They took their places in the house and he said: ""O Abu Hirr!"" I said: ""At your service, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Take the bowl and give it to them."" I took the bowl and began giving it to one man after another. Each drank until satisfied and returned the bowl. I continued until I reached the Prophet (ﷺ) after all the people had drunk and were satisfied. He took the bowl, placed it on his hand, looked at me and smiled, then said: ""O Abu Hirr!"" I said: ""At your service, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""You and I remain."" I said: ""That is true, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Sit down and drink."" So I sat down and drank. He said: ""Drink!"" and I kept drinking until I said: ""No, by Him Who sent you with the truth, I can find no room for it!"" He said: ""Show me."" I gave him the bowl, and he praised Allah, said the basmalah, and drank the remainder."" [Al-Bukhari]"
"502","On the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: You saw me lying prostrate between the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and the room of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, unconscious. Then the comer comes and places his foot on my neck, and sees that I am mad and there is no madness in me. There is nothing wrong with me but hunger. [Al-Bukhari]."
"503","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) died while his armor was mortgaged to a Jew for thirty saa’s of barley. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"504","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) mortgaged his armor for barley, and I walked to the Prophet (ﷺ) with barley bread and melted fat, and I heard him say: “The family of Muhammad had no food (not even a saa’ of barley) in the morning nor in the evening,” and they were nine households. [Al-Bukhari]. ((الإهالة: with kasra on the hamza: melted fat. And"
"505","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw seventy of the people of Suffah, and not one of them had a cloak; they had only a lower garment (izar) or a wraparound (kisaa'). They had tied around their necks some of them that reached half the length of the legs, and some of them that reached the ankles, and gathered the clothing with his hand for fear that his private parts would be seen. [Al-Bukhari]."
"506","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The bed of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was made of tanned leather stuffed with palm fiber. [Al-Bukhari]."
"507","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when a man from the Ansar came and greeted him, then the Ansari turned away, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O brother of the Ansar, how is my brother Saad bin Ubadah?” He said: Salih, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Who will visit him?” “Who among you?” So he stood up and we stood with him, and we were about thirteen. We had no sandals, no slippers, no caps, and no shirt. We walked in that marshes, until we came to him, and his people remained behind around him until the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and his companions who were with him approached. [Muslim]."
"508","On the authority of Imran bin Al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: “The best of you are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them.” Imran said: I do not know. He said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said twice or three times: “Then after them there will be people who bear false witness but whose testimony is not accepted, who betray and are not trusted, who vow but do not fulfill, and fatness appears among them.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"509","On the authority of Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O son of Adam: to give abundance is good for you, and to withhold it is evil for you. Do not be blamed for subsistence, and start with those you support.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"510","On the authority of Ubaidullah bin Muhsin Al-Ansari Al-Khatmi, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever among you wakes up safe in his household, healthy in his body, and has sustenance for his day, it is as if the world had been completely occupied for him” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"511","-On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “He who converted to Islam has succeeded, his livelihood is sufficient, and Allah has satisfied him with what He has given him” [Muslim]."
"512","On the authority of Abu Muhammad Fadalah bin Ubaid Al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Blessed is he who is guided to Islam, whose livelihood is sufficient, and he is content.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"513","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) spent consecutive nights fasting, and his family could not find dinner, and most of their bread was barley bread. [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"514","And on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led the people, men of his stature would fall down during the prayer from extreme hunger - and they are the people of the Suffah - until the Bedouins would say: These are crazy people. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed, he would turn to them and say: “If you knew what you have with Allah Almighty, you would love to increase in want and need.” [Al-Tirmidhi] “Al-Khasasa”: poverty and extreme hunger."
"515","On the authority of Abu Karima Al-Miqdam bin Maadikarb, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, “No human being fills a vessel worse than his stomach. The son of Adam suffices for food that will strengthen his core. If it is inevitable, then a third for his food, a third for his drink, and a third for himself.” [Al-Tirmidhi]. “Eats” That is: a bite."
"516","On the authority of Abu Umamah Iyas bin Tha’labah Al-Ansari Al-Harithi, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned the world one day in his presence, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Don’t you listen? Don’t you listen? Indeed, simplicity (in appearance) is part of faith, and immorality is part of faith.” Meaning: aridity. [Abu Dawud]. “Badha” is pronounced with the unified “ba” and the two syllables, which is a shabby appearance and abandonment of luxurious clothing. As for “barrenness” it is pronounced with the “qaf” and the “ha”."
"517","On the authority of Abu Abdullah Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent us and Abu Ubaidah, may Allah be pleased with him, ordered us to receive a caravan of Quraysh, and he provided us with a sack of dates for which he did not find any other for us. So Abu Ubaidah used to give us a date, and it was said: How did you make it with it? He said: We suck it as a child sucks, then we drink from it of water, and it is enough for our day for the rest of the day. At night, we used to beat with our sticks, then we drenched them with water and ate them. He said: We set out on the seashore, and it rose for us on the seashore like a huge dune. We came to it and found it was an animal called anmber. Abu Ubaidah said: Dead, then he said: No, rather we are messengers of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and in the path of Allah. You were forced to eat, so we remained on it for a month, and we were three hundred, until we became fat, and you saw us. We scoop up a little of the fat from the person who is in his eyehole and cut off the lump of fat from him like a bull or the size of an ox. Abu Ubaidah took thirteen men from us and seated them in his eyehole, and he took one of his ribs and made it stand up. Then the greatest camel departed with us, so he passed under it and we took provision from its meat and dried meat. When we came to Medina, we came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him, so he said: “It is a provision that Allah has provided for you, so are you with you? “Some of its meat, so you feed us?” So we sent some of it to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he ate it. [Muslim]. “Al-Jarrab”: a well-known leather container, and it is with a kasra and an opening of the jim, and the kasra is more eloquent. His saying: “we suck it” with an opening for a mi. It is eaten by camels. “And the dune”: a hill made of sand. “And the waqb” with the opening of the waw and the suffix of the qaf, and after it a unified ba, which is the click of the eye. “By lightening the ha”: that is, he made a mount upon it. “Al-Shaiq” with the dictionary shin and the qaf: the meat that was cut to be cooked from it, and Allah knows best."
"518","On the authority of Asmaa bint Yazid, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The sleeve of the shirt of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was up to the wrist, [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"519","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: On the day of the ditch, we were digging, and a heavy dune appeared. They came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: This is a dune that appeared in the ditch. He said: “I am descending.” Then he got up, and his stomach was tied with a stone. We stayed for three days without tasting anything, so the Prophet (ﷺ) took the pickaxe, hit it, and it came back as a pile of stones. Am I weak, or am I weak? So I said: O Messenger of Allah, allow me to go home. So I said to my wife: I saw something in the Prophet (ﷺ) and something about that. Patience, so do you have something? She said: I have barley and a bunch. So I slaughtered the bunches and ground the barley until we put the meat in the cooking pot. Then I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and the dough had broken, and the cooking pot on the heating stones was almost cooked. So I said: It is good for me, so stand up, O Messenger of Allah, and one or two men. He said: “How much is it?” So I mentioned it to him and he said: “It is very good. Tell her not to remove the twine or the bread from the oven until I come.” So he said: “Stand up.” So the emigrants and the Ansar stood up, so I entered upon her and said: Woe to you. The Prophet (ﷺ) and the emigrants and the Ansar and those who With them! She said: Did he ask you? I said: Yes. He said: “Come in and do not strain. So he began to break the bread, and put meat on it, and to ferment the burma and oven if he took from it, and bring it to his companions and then take it away. He continued breaking and scooping until they were satisfied, and some of it remained, so he said: Eat this and be sacrificed, for the people have been afflicted with famine” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. Narration: Jabir said: When he dug the ditch, I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) standing alone, so I turned to my wife and said: Do you have anything? I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) suffering a severe loss, so she brought out to me a sack containing a saa’ of barley, and we had a domesticated animal, so I slaughtered it and ground the barley, so I went to my empty place and cut it completely. Then I turned to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: Do not disgrace me with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and those with him. So I came to him and walked with him and said: O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: Do not expose me to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and those with him. We slaughtered an animal for ourselves, and ground a saa of barley, so come and go with you. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) shouted and said: “O people of the ditch, Jabir has made a sausage, so welcome.” Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Do not come down with your whole body and do not bake your dough until I come.” So I came, and the Prophet (ﷺ) came, leading the people until I came to my wife and she said: By you and by you! I said: I have done what you said. So she brought out dough, so he spat on it and blessed it, then he went to our whole place and spat and blessed it, then he said: “Call a baker and let her bake with you, and take some of the whole cup of yours and do not put it down.” And they were a thousand, so I swear to Allah that they would eat until they left it and deviated, and if our whole batch would be covered as it is. And our dough should be baked as it is. His saying: “I presented a kaddiyah”: with the addition of the kaf and the sakān of the dal and the double yā’ under it, which is a thick, solid piece of earth on which an ax does not work. “The dune” is originally a sand hill, and what is meant here is: it became soft dirt, which is the meaning of “ahīl.” “Athāfī”: stones. Which is subject to fate. And “ḍaḍaḥuma”: they crowded together. “Famine”: hunger, which is with the opening of the meem. And “Al-Khams” is with the opening of the lexicalized kha and the meem: hunger. And “reversed”: turned around and came back. The diminutive of “Bimma”, which is the embrace - with the opening of the eye -. And “the domesticated”: she is the one who brought the house together. And “Al-Su’ur”: the food to which people are invited, and it is in Persian. And “Hayla” means: come. And her saying: “By you and by you” means: she quarreled with him and cursed him, because she thought that the one who Then it was not enough for them, so she became ashamed and it was hidden from her what Allah Almighty had honored his Prophet (ﷺ) in this apparent miracle and the amazing verse The ladle. And “it covers” meaning: its boiling makes a sound, and Allah knows best."
"520","And on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Abu Talha said to Umm Sulaym: I heard the voice of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) weak and I could tell he (the Prophet) was hungry. Do you have anything? She said: Yes, so she took out discs of barley, then took a veil for her, wrapped some of the bread around, then put it under my dress and brought some back to me. Then she sent me to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and I went with it, and found the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He was sitting in the mosque, and people were with him, so I stood among them, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me, “Abu Talha sent you?” I said: Yes, and he said: “Food.” So I said: Yes, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Stand up.” So they set out until I came to Abu Talha and informed him, so Abu said. Talha: O Umm Sulaym: The Messenger of Allah has brought the people and we do not have anything to feed them? She said: Allah and His Messenger know best. So Abu Talha set off until he met the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came with him until they entered. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Come, give me what you have, O Umm Sulaym.” So she brought that bread, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered it. Then he said: “Give permission to ten,” so he gave them permission, and they ate until they were satisfied and then left. Then he said: “Give permission to ten,” so he gave them permission, and they ate until they were satisfied, then they left. Then he said: “Give permission.” ""So he gave them permission until all the people had eaten and were satisfied, and the people were seventy or eighty men. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration: He kept entering ten and leaving ten, until not one of them remained but entered, and ate until he was satisfied. Then he prepared it, and it was like it when they ate from it. And in a narration: So they ate ten, until he did that with eighty men, then the Prophet (ﷺ) ate. After that, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) one day, and I found him sitting with his companions, and he had bandaged his stomach with a band. So I said to some of his companions: Why did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) bandage his stomach? They said: From hunger, so I went to my father. Talha, who is the husband of Umm Sulaym bint Milhan, so I said: Father, I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) bandaging his stomach with a band. So I asked some of his companions, and they said: From hunger. So Abu Talha entered my mother and said: Is there anything? She said: Yes, I have a piece of bread and dates. If the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to us alone, we would satisfy him, and if another came with him, talk about them, and he mentioned All the talk."
"521","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Wealth is not from abundance of possessions, but wealth is the contentment of the soul” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. “"
"522","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “He who converts to Islam, was granted a sufficient livelihood, and is content with what Allah has given him has succeeded” [Muslim]."
"523","On the authority of Hakim bin Hizam, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then he said: “O Wise, this money is green and sweet, so whoever takes it with a generous soul will be blessed with it, and whoever takes it with a greedy soul will not be blessed in it, and he is like one who eats and is not satisfied, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand.” Hakim said: So I said, O Messenger. By Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will not take anything from anyone after you until I leave this world. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, used to invite Hakim to give him something to give, but he refused to accept anything from him. Then Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, called him to give it, but he refused to accept it. So he said: O community of Muslims, I bear witness to Hakim that I am offering him his right that Allah has divided for him in this spoil, but he refuses to take it. Hakim did not take anything from anyone after the Prophet until he died. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. “Yrzā” is Bara’, then Zay, then Hamza, meaning: He did not take anything from anyone. The origin of razi’ is: decrease, meaning: He did not decrease anyone in anything by taking from him. And “nafsharf”: its aspiration and greed for something. “Sakhawah.” “Self”: It is the lack of supervision of something, greed for it, indifference to it, and gluttony"
"524","And on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a campaign, and we were six men, and we had a camel which we took turns riding, so our feet became blistered, and my feet became blistered, and my nails fell, so we used to wrap rags around our feet, so it was called the Battle of Dhat al-Riqa’ because we used to wrap rags around our feet. Abu Burdah said: Abu Musa narrated this hadith, then he disliked it. That, and he said: I would not do to mention it! He said: It is as if he hated that he divulged any of his work. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"525","And on the authority of Amr bin Taghlib - by opening the ta’ with the double ta’ above, with the suffix of the ghān with the vocabulary, and the kasra of the lam - may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was brought with money or taken captives, so he divided it up, so he gave to men, and left men, and he heard that those he had left had blamed him. So he thanked Allah, then praised him, then said, As for what follows, by Allah, I give to a man and leave a man, and what I leave is more beloved to me than what I give, but I only give to people. Because I see in their hearts the anxiety and panic, and the deprivation of people to what Allah has placed in their hearts of wealth and goodness, among them is Amr ibn Taghlib.” Amr ibn Taghlib said: By Allah, I do not like that with the word of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) I should have red camels [Al-Bukhari]. “Panic”: it is the most intense anxiety, and it was said: boredom."
"526","On the authority of Hakim bin Hizam, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and start with those you support, and the best charity is from the back of a rich person, and whoever is chaste, Allah will pardon him, and whoever is self-sufficient, Allah will enrich him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. [And this is the wording of Al-Bukhari, and the wording of Muslim is shorter]."
"527","On the authority of Abu Sufyan Sakhr bin Harb, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not persist in begging, for by Allah, none of you will ask me for anything, and his asking will elicit something from me, and I will hate him, so I will bless him for what I have given him” [Muslim]."
"528","On the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman Awf bin Malik al-Ashja’i, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) nine or eight or seven, and he said: “Will you not pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?” And the five daily prayers and obey.” He concealed a hidden word: “And do not ask the people for anything.” I saw some of those people drop the whip of one of them and would not ask anyone to hand it to him. [Muslim]."
"529","And on the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “The question will continue with one of you until he meets Allah Almighty and there is no piece of flesh left on his face” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"530","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said while he was on the pulpit, and mentioned charity and abstinence from begging: “The upper hand is better than the lower hand. The upper hand is the one who spends, and the lower hand is the beggar” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"531","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever asks people for a lot of food is only asking for hot coals; let him ask little or refrain (from asking)” [Muslim]."
"532","On the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Begging is a hardship that causes a man to suffer, unless the man asks a ruler or something that is necessary.” ([Al-Tirmidhi]. “Toil”: scratching and the like."
"533","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever is afflicted with poverty and inflicts it on people, it does not fill his poverty, and whoever directs his need to Allah (i.e., relies solely on Him), Allah will soon provide him with provision, sooner or later.” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi] “It is about to” with a kasra on the shin: i.e. He speeds up."
"534","On the authority of Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Who will guarantee for me that people will not ask anything, and I will guarantee Paradise for him?” So I said: I; He did not ask anyone anything. [Abu Dawud]."
"535","On the authority of Abu Bishr Qabisah bin Al-Mukhariq, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I had taken on a debt (to reconcile between two groups) related to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), so I went to ask him about it. He said: “Stay until the charity comes to us and we will order it for you.” Then he said: “O Qabisah, Begging is not permissible except for three cases: A man who has taken on a debt (to reconcile between two groups), so it is permissible for him to beg until he pays off the debt, then he must stop. A man afflicted with a disaster that destroys his wealth, so it is permissible for him to beg until he has enough for a livelihood or sufficient provision, until three people of sound judgment from his community testify: 'So-and-so has been afflicted with poverty', so it is permissible for him to beg until he has enough for a livelihood or sufficient provision. Whatever is beyond these three cases of begging, O Qabisah, is unlawful, and whoever consumes it consumes unlawfully.” [Muslim]. “Al-hamal” with fatha-ha: when a fight and the like takes place between two groups, and a person makes peace between them over money that he can bear and commits to himself. And “pandemic”: a blight that befalls a person’s money. The need and sufficiency of the needy, and “want”: poverty. And “al-hajja”: reason."
"536","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “It is not the poor person who goes around among the people who is denied a bite and two bites, and a date and two dates, but the poor person who does not find any wealth to enrich him, and no one notices him, so charity is given to him, and does not get up and ask the people” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"537","On the authority of Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Omar, may Allah be pleased with them, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to give me a gift, and I would say: Give it to someone who is poorer than me, so he said: “Take it; if any of this money comes to you, and you are neither in need nor a beggar, then take it and finance it if you wish, all of it, and if you wish, give it in charity, and what not, do not follow it yourself.” Salem said: Abdullah did not ask anyone for anything, nor did he return anything I gave him. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"538","On the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Zubair bin Al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “For one of you to take his rope and then go to the mountain and bring a bundle of firewood on his back and sell it, and Allah will protect his face with it, it is better for him than to ask the people, give him something or withhold him.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"539","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “For one of you to carry a bundle of firewood on his back, it is better for him than to ask someone and give him something or withhold from him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"540","And on the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Dawud (peace be upon him) would not eat except from what he worked with his hands.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"541","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Zechariah (peace be upon him) was a carpenter” [Muslim]."
"542","On the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Ma’di Yakrib, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “No one has ever eaten food better than eating what he made with his own hands, and the Prophet of Allah, Dawud (peace be upon him) used to eat what he made with his own hands.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"543","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “There is no envy except in two things: a man to whom Allah has given wealth, and he spends it in the path of righteousness, and a man to whom Allah has given wisdom, and he judges it and teaches it” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"544","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Which of you is the wealth of his heir more beloved to him than his own wealth?” They said: O Messenger of Allah, there is none of us whose wealth is dearer to him. He said: “For his wealth is what he puts forward, and the wealth of his heir is what he leaves behind.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"545","On the authority of Uday bin Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Beware of Hell, even if it is half a date” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"546","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: It never occurred that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked for anything and he said no. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"547","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is not a day on which the servants wake up except that two angels descend, and one of them says: O Allah, give a successor to the spender, and the other says: O Allah, give loss to the one who withholds (wealth)” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"548","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah Almighty said: Spend, O son of Adam, and He will spend on you” (Agreed upon)."
"549","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): Which Islam is best? He said: “You give food, and you greet those you know and those you do not know.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"550","On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Forty qualities, the highest of which is giving a goat as a gift. There is no worker who acts upon one of them, hoping for its reward and believing in the fulfillment of its promise, except that Allah Almighty will admit him into Paradise by it.” [Narrated by Al-Bukhari. This hadith has previously been explained in the chapter explaining the abundance of good paths]."
"551","On the authority of Abu Umamah Sada bin Ajlan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O son of Adam, to give your surplus (of wealth) is good for you, and to withhold it is evil for you, and do not be blamed for subsistence, and start with what you support, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand” [Muslim]."
"552","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was not asked for anything about Islam except that he gave it to the asker. A man came to him, so he gave him sheep between two mountains. Then he returned to his people and said: O my people, embrace Islam, for Muhammad gives to the one who does not fear poverty, even if a man embraces Islam seeking nothing but the world, he does not remain in that state but a short while until Islam becomes dearer to him than the world and all that is in it. ((Narrated by) Muslim).."
"553","On the authority of Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) distributed a portion, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, who is more deserving of it than these people? He said: “They have left me no choice but to give them even if they ask me rudely, or they will call me stingy, and I am not stingy.” [Muslim]."
"554","And on the authority of Jubair bin Mutim, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: While he was walking with the Prophet (ﷺ) locked in Hunain, the Bedouins stopped him asking him, until they forced him to Samra, so I snatched his robe, and the Prophet (ﷺ) stood up and said: “Give me my robe. If I had as many blessings as these small branches of the tree, I would divide it among you, and then you will not find me stingy, liar, or cowardly.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"555","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “No charity decreases wealth, and Allah does not increase a servant (in honor) except when he pardons (others), and no one humbles himself before Allah except that Allah Almighty exalts him” [Muslim]."
"556","And on the authority of Abu Kabsha Amr bin Saad Al-Anmari, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “There are three things that I swear by, and I tell you a hadith, so memorize it: A servant’s wealth is not diminished by charity, nor is a servant’s wrong done to him by patience except that Allah increases his glory, and no servant opens the door of a question except that Allah opens for him the door of poverty, or a word similar to it, and he tells you a hadith, so memorize it. He said: The world is only for four people: A servant to whom Allah has given wealth and knowledge, in which he fears his Lord, maintains his ties of kinship, and knows the rights of Allah over it (fulfilling its obligations to Allah), this is the best of stations. And a servant to whom Allah has provided knowledge, but not money, is sincere in intention, saying: If I had money, I would do the work of so-and-so, for it is his intention, and their reward is the same. And a servant whom Allah has provided with money, but has not provided him with knowledge, so he blunders in his money without knowledge, neither fears his Lord nor maintains ties of kinship with it (the wealth). He does not know the rights of Allah over it, for this is the most vile of statuses. And a servant whom Allah did not provide with wealth or knowledge, he says: If I had money, I would do the work of so-and-so on it, for it is his intention, so it is the same for both of them.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"557","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, they slaughtered a sheep, and the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “What is left of it?” She said: “All of it is left except its shoulder.” He said: “All of it is left except its shoulder.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"558","On the authority of Asma’ bint Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with them both, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: “Do not practice sorcery, and you will not be afflicted with it.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"559","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “The parable of the miserly person and the spender is like the example of two men with two iron coats of mail (armor) on them from their breasts to their collarbones. As for the one who spends, whenever he spends, it (the armor) expands and becomes spacious on his skin until his knuckles are hidden and his traces are erased. As for the miserly person, he does not want to spend anything except that every ring sticks to its place, so he expands it, but it does not expand.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And 'Paradise' refers to the coat of mail (armor), and its meaning is: the more the spender spends, the more it expands and becomes longer until it drags behind him, and his feet and the traces of his walk and steps are hidden."
"560","On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever gives in charity the equivalent of a date from good earnings, and Allah accepts only good (charity), Allah will accept it with His right hand, then nurture it for its owner as one of you nurtures his foal until it becomes like a mountain.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] “Falu” with the opening of the fa, the lam being joined, and the waw being stressed, and it is also said: with a kasra. The fa’, the lam’s housing, and the waw’s lightening: it is the dowry."
"561","And on his authority, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “While a man was walking through a desert of land, he heard a voice in a cloud: Water so-and-so’s garden. Then that cloud moved away and emptied its water into a desert. Suddenly, a channel from those water channels had absorbed all that water. He followed the water, and then a man was standing in his garden, diverting the water with his tools, and he said to him: O Abdullah, what is your name? He said: So-and-so is for the name that he heard in the cloud, so he said. To him: O Abdullah, why did you ask me my name? He said: I heard a voice in the clouds from which this is the water saying: Water so-and-so’s garden in your name, so what do you do with it? He said: But if you say this, then I look at what comes out of it, and I give a third of it in charity, and I and my family eat a third, and I put a third of it back in it [Muslim]. “Al-Hurra” is the clothed land. Black stones. “And the anus” with the opening of the syllable shin and the rā’ and the jim in the syllable: it is the flow of water."
"562","And on the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Beware of injustice, for injustice is darkness on the Day of Resurrection, and beware of miserliness, for miserliness destroyed those before you, causing them to shed their blood and make lawful what they had prohibited.” [Muslim]."
"563","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: I am exhausted, so he sent for some of his wives, and she said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I have nothing but water. Then he sent to another, and she said the same, until they all said the same: No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have nothing but water. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said, “Who will host him tonight?” Then a man from the Ansar said, 'I will, O Messenger of Allah.' So he set off with him on his journey, and said to his wife: Honor the guest of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). In one narration, he said to his wife: Do you have anything? She said: No, except food for my children. He said: So give them something, and if they want dinner, put them to sleep. And if our guest enters, I turn off the lamp and show him we are eating. So they sat down, and the guest ate and stayed for the night, and when morning came, he went to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: “Allah has marveled at what you have done to your guest tonight” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"564","And on his authority he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The food of two is sufficient for three, and the food of three is sufficient for four” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim on the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: The food of one is sufficient for two, the food of two is sufficient for four, and the food for four is sufficient for eight."
"565","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: While we were traveling with the Prophet (ﷺ) a man came on his camel, and he began to look right and left. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever has some surplus, let him give it to the one who has no riding animal, and whoever has some surplus, let him give it to the one who has no food.” He mentioned types of wealth, as previously mentioned, until we saw that none of us had any right to the surplus. [Muslim]."
"566","On the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with a woven cloak and said: I wove it to clothe you, so the Prophet (ﷺ) took it and needed it, so he came out to us and it was his garment, Then so-and-so said, 'Clothe me with it, how fine it is!' The Prophet said: 'Yes.' So the Prophet (ﷺ) sat in the gathering, then came back, folded it, and then sent it to him: The people said to him: 'You have done well!' The Prophet (ﷺ) wore it when he was in need of it, then I asked him and learned that he does not refuse a questioner, she said: By Allah, I did not ask him to wear it, but I asked him so that it would be my shroud. Sahl said: So it was his shroud. [Al-Bukhari]"
"567","On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: If the Ash’aris ran out of provisions during the battle, or if their family’s food in Medina became scarce, they would gather what they had in one garment and divide it among them in one vessel equally, so they are of me and I of them” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"568","On the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, that a drink was brought to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he drank from it. A boy was on his right, and the elders were on his left. He said to the boy: “Do you give me permission to give these?” The boy said, “No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not prefer anyone over you.” So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) returned it to the boy's hand. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. The verb """
"569","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “While Job, (ﷺ) was bathing naked, golden locusts fell on him, and Job began to dig through his garment, so his Lord, the Almighty and Majestic, called out to him, O Job, was I not your song of what you see?! He said: Yes, by your glory, but I am indispensable to your blessing, ([Al-Bukhari].."
"570","On the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is no envy except in two things: a man to whom Allah has given money, and who has given it the right to destroy it in truth, and a man to whom Allah has given wisdom, so he judges by it and knows it” [Agreed upon, and his explanation will be presented shortly]."
"571","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both: On the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “There is no envy except in two things: a man to whom Allah has given the Qur’an, and he recites it throughout the night and during the day, and a man to whom Allah has given wealth, so he spends it throughout the night and during the day” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] “the time”: the hours."
"572","And on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the poor immigrants came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: “The wealthy people have taken the highest ranks and the lasting bliss.” So he said: “And what is that?” They said: “They pray as we pray, and they fast as we fast, and they give in charity, but we do not give in charity, and they emancipate and we do not emancipate.” Then he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Should I not inform you? “Something by which you will surpass those who came before you, and with which you will precede those after you, and no one will be better than you except he who has done the same as what you have done?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “You glorify, glorify, and praise, after every prayer thirty-three times.” So the poor immigrants returned to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: “Our brothers who have wealth heard about what we did, so they did the same?” So the Messenger of Allah said. May Allah’s (ﷺ): “That is the grace of Allah. He gives it to whomever He wills” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim], and this is the wording of a Muslim narration."
"573","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took me by the shoulders and said: “Be in this world as if you were a stranger or a passerby.” And Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to say: If it is evening, do not wait for the morning, and if it is morning, do not wait for the evening, and take from your health for your illness, and from your life for your death” [Al-Bukhari]."
"574","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “What is the right of a Muslim man, who has something to bequeath, to spend two nights without having his will written with him?” (Agreed upon) This is the wording of Al-Bukhari. And in a narration by Muslim, “to spend three nights: Ibn Umar said: Not a night has passed since I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say that unless I have my will.”"
"575","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) drew lines and said: “This is the human being, and this is his term, so while he was like that, the closest line came” [Al-Bukhari]."
"576","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) wrote a square line, and he wrote a line in the middle coming out of it, and he wrote small lines to the one in the middle from his side which is in the middle, and he said: “This is the human being, and this is his time surrounding him - or it has surrounded him - and this is the one outside his hope, and these small lines are the afflictions (that befall him). If this one misses him, this one will bite him, and if this one misses him, this one will bite him.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"577","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Hasten to do good deeds. Are you waiting for anything except forgotten poverty, or oppressive wealth, or a corrupting illness, or ruined old age, or imminent death, or the Antichrist, an absent evil awaiting, or the Hour, for the Hour is more severe and more grievous?!” ([Al-Tirmidhi] He said: It is a good hadith"
"578","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Make frequent mention of the destroyer of pleasures” [meaning death] [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"579","On the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may Allah be pleased with him: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: When a third of the night had passed, he would get up and say: “O people, remember Allah.” The first blast (of the resurrection trumpet) has come, followed by the second blast. Death came with what is in it. Death came with what is in it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I send the most blessings upon you, so how many of my prayers should I devote to you? He said: “Whatever you want.” I said: A quarter? He said: “Whatever you want, and if you increase, it is yours.” I said: Half? He said: Whatever you want, if you increase, it is yours. I said: Two-thirds? He said: Whatever you want, if you increase, it is better for you. I said: May I make all my prayers for you? He said: “If your concern is sufficient, and your sin is forgiven” ([Al-Tirmidhi]."
"580","On the authority of Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “I forbade you from visiting graves, so visit them” [Muslim]. And in a narration, “So whoever wants to visit the graves, let him visit them, for they remind us of the Hereafter.”"
"581","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would go out at the end of the night to Al-Baqi’, he would say: “Peace be upon you, the home of a believing people, and what you were promised has come to you. Tomorrow you will be raised from your graves, and we, Allah willing, will follow you. O Allah, forgive the people of Baqi’ Al-Gharqad” [Muslim]."
"582","On the authority of Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) used to teach them, when they went out to the cemeteries, to say: “Peace be upon you, the people of the abodes (graves), among the believers and Muslims, and we, Allah willing, will follow you. I ask Allah for safety for us and you” [Muslim]."
"583","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by graves in Medina, so he turned to them with his face and said: “Peace be upon you, people of the graves. May Allah forgive us and you. You are our predecessors and we are the ones who follow your track” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"584","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “None of you should wish for death. He is either doing good, and perhaps he will increase, or doing wrong, and perhaps he will be granted repentance.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. This is the wording of Al-Bukhari, and in a narration by Muslim on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who said: “None of you should wish for death, nor should he pray for it before it comes to him, that if he dies, his work will cease, and that it will only increase the life of the believer in goodness.”"
"585","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “None of you should wish for death because of harm that has befallen him. If he must do so, let him say: O Allah, grant me life as long as life is good for me, and cause me to die if death is good for me” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"586","And on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said: We entered upon Khabbab bin Al-Art, may Allah be pleased with him, to visit him (during his illness), and he had been cauterized seven times, and he said: Our companions of the predecessors have passed away, and the world has not diminished them, and we have been struck with something for which we cannot find a place except dirt, and had the Prophet (ﷺ) not forbidden us from praying for death, I would have prayed for it. Then we came to him again while he was building a wall for himself, and he said: The Muslim will be rewarded for everything. He spends it except on something that will put it in this dirt. [Agreed upon, and this is the wording of Al-Bukhari’s narration]."
"587","On the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “What is permissible is clear, and what is forbidden is clear, and between them are doubtful matters that many people do not know. So whoever fears the doubtful, protects his religion and honor, and whoever falls into the doubtful, falls into the forbidden, like a shepherd grazing around a restricted pasture (Hima) about to graze therein. And every ruler has a restricted pasture (Hima), and Allah's restricted pasture is His prohibitions. In the body there is a piece of flesh that, if it is good, the whole body is good, and if it is spoiled, the whole body is spoilt: namely, the heart” [Agreed upon. It was narrated through several paths with similar wording]"
"588","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) found a date on the road and said: “If I had not feared that it would be charity, I would have eaten it.” (Agreed upon)"
"589","On the authority of Al-Nawwas bin Samaan, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: Righteousness is good character, and wrongdoing is what wavers in your soul, and you hate for people to find out about it [Muslim]."
"590","On the authority of Wabisa bin Ma’bad, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: “You have come to ask about righteousness?” I said yes, and he said: “Search your heart. Righteousness is what the soul is at ease with and the heart is at ease with, and sin is what troubles the soul and hesitates in the chest, even if the people give you fatwas and give you fatwas.” ((A good hadith, narrated by Ahmad and al-Darimi in Their support).."
"591","And on the authority of Abu Saru’ah - Kasr Al-Sin Al-Najmalah and its accusative case - Uqba bin Al-Harith, may Allah be pleased with him, that he married a daughter of Abu Ihab bin Aziz, and a woman came to him and said: I have breastfed Uqba, whom he had married, and Uqba said to her: I do not know that you breastfed me, nor did you tell me. So he rode to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in Medina, and asked him, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “How, when it was said?” Then Uqba left her and she married another husband.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"592","On the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): “Leave what doubts you for what does not doubt you” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"593","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, had a boy who paid him the tax, and Abu Bakr used to eat from his tax. One day he brought something, and Abu Bakr ate from it. The boy said to him: Do you know what this is? Then Abu Bakr said: What is it? He said: I used to guess for a man in pre-Islamic times, and the fortune-telling was excellent, except that I deceived him and he met me, so he gave me this. Which I ate from, so Abu Bakr inserted his hand and vomited everything in his stomach” [Al-Bukhari]."
"594","And on the authority of Nafi’, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, assigned a stipend of four thousand for the first emigrants and a stipend of three thousand five hundred for his son, and he was told: He is one of the emigrants, so why did you reduce it? He said: Only his father immigrated with him. He said: He is not like someone who immigrated himself. [Al-Bukhari]"
"595","On the authority of Attiya bin Urwah al-Saadi, the companion, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A servant does not attain the level of being one of the pious until he abandons what is permissible, out of caution for what is harmful.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"596","On the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Allah loves the pious, rich and hidden servant” [Muslim]. What is meant by “the rich” is the rich in soul, as previously mentioned in the authentic hadith."
"597","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man said: Which of the people is better, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “A believer who strives with his life and his wealth in the cause of Allah.” He said: Then who? He said: “A man who secludes himself in a mountainous region and worships his Lord.” And in a narration: “He fears Allah and shuns people from his evil.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"598","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A Muslim’s best wealth will soon be sheep with which he can trace the tops of the mountains and the countryside, fleeing with his religion from temptations” [Al-Bukhari]. And the tops of the mountains: the highest ones."
"599","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Allah did not send a prophet except that he tended sheep.” His companions said: “You?” He said: “I used to herd them on qirats for the people of Mecca.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"600","On the authority of him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he said: “Among the people’s best livelihood is a man holding the reins of his horse for the sake of Allah, flying on board, and whenever he hears a howl or a startle, he flies at him, seeking to be killed, or death awaits him, or a man with spoils at the top of one of these branches, or the depth of one of these valleys, who establishes prayer, pays zakat, and worships his Lord until certainty comes to him. There are none of the people except In goodness” [Muslim]."
"601","On the authority of Iyad bin Himar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah has revealed to me that you should be humble so that no one will be proud of anyone else, and no one will oppress anyone else” [Muslim]."
"602","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “No charity decreases wealth, and Allah does not increase a servant in honor except by forgiveness, and no one humbles himself before Allah except that Allah exalts him” [Muslim]."
"603","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that he passed by boys and greeted them and said: The Prophet (ﷺ) used to do that. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"604","On his authority, he said: If the female slave was one of the slave girls of Medina, she could take the hand of the Prophet (ﷺ) and take him wherever she wanted. [Al-Bukhari]."
"605","On the authority of Al-Aswad bin Yazid, he said: Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, was asked: What did the Prophet (ﷺ) do in his house? She said: He used to do his family’s job - meaning: serving his family - and when the time for prayer came, he would go out to pray” [Al-Bukhari]."
"606","On the authority of Abu Rifa’ah Tamim bin Asid, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I approached the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was delivering the sermon, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, a strange man came to ask about his religion. He does not know what his religion is? So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) turned to me and left his sermon until he came to me. He brought a chair, so he sat on it and began to teach me what Allah had taught him. Then he came to his sermon and completed the last of it. [Muslim]."
"607","And on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ate food, he would lick his three fingers. He said: “And he said: ‘If a morsel of one of you falls, let him remove the harmful substance from it, and eat it, and not leave it to the devil.’ And he commanded that the bowl be wiped clean. He said: ‘For you do not know in which of your food the blessing lies.’” [Muslim]."
"608","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Allah has not sent a prophet except that he herded sheep.” His companions said: And you? He said: Yes, I used to herd them on carats for the people of Mecca. [Al-Bukhari]."
"609","And on the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: If I am invited to a sheep's foreleg or shoulder, I will accept, and if I am given a sheep's foreleg or shoulder as a gift, I will accept it.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"610","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) named Al-Adhaba would not be outrun in a race, or could hardly be outrun. A Bedouin rode his camel and overtook her in the race. This made it difficult for the Muslims until he recognized it. the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “It is a decree of Allah that nothing in the world is raised [in status] except that He lowers it.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"611","On the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “No one will enter Paradise who has an atom’s weight of arrogance in his heart.” Then a man said, “A man likes his clothes to be good and his shoes to be good?” He said: “Indeed, Allah is beautiful. Indeed, Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty. Arrogance is disdain for the truth and looking down upon people.” [Muslim]."
"612","On the authority of Salama bin Al-Akwa’, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man ate with his left hand at the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: “Eat with your right hand.” He said: “I cannot!” He said: “Can you not [eat with your right hand]?” Nothing prevented him except pride. So he did not raise it to his mouth. [Muslim]."
"613","On the authority of Haritha bin Wahb, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: Shall I not tell you about the people of Hell? “Every harsh, stingy, and arrogant person” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. His explanation was presented in the chapter on the weakness of Muslims."
"614","On the authority of Abu Saeed, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Heaven and Hell protested, and Hell said: In the tyrannical and the arrogant, and Paradise said: In the weak and the poor of people. So Allah decided between them: You are Paradise my mercy, I have mercy on whomever I wish with you, and you are my torment, I punish you with whomever I wish, and it is up to each of you to fill it” ([Muslim].."
"615","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will not look at the one who pulled his garment out of arrogance.” (Agreed upon)"
"616","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There are three to whom Allah will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them, nor will He look at them, and they will have a painful punishment: an adulterous old man, a lying king, and an arrogant breadwinner” [Muslim]"
"617","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah Almighty said: Glory is My cloak and pride is My robe. Whoever disputes with Me in either of them, I will punish him” [Muslim]."
"618","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “While a man was walking in an outfit that pleased his soul, with his head upturned, strutting in his walk, Allah caused him to sink into the earth, and he was rolling on the ground until the Day of Resurrection” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"619","On the authority of Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A man will continue to go by himself until he is written among the tyrants, and what befalls them will happen to him” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"620","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was the best of people in character [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"621","On his authority, he said: I have never touched a brocade or a silk softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and I have never smelled a scent better than the smell of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). I served the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for ten years, and he never said to me: “Ugh,” nor did he say to something I did, “Why did you do it?” Nor did he say to something I did not do, “Didn’t I do such-and-such?” (Agreed upon)"
"622","On the authority of Al-Saab bin Jathama, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I gave the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) a wild donkey, and he returned it to me, and when he saw what was on my face, he said: “We did not return it to you except because I was in a state of ihram.” (Agreed upon)"
"623","On the authority of Al-Nawas bin Samaan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about righteousness and sin, and he said: “Righteousness is good character, and sin is what wavers in your soul and you hate for people to find out about it” [Muslim]."
"624","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was not obscene or foul-mouthed. He used to say: “The best of you are the ones with the best morals” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"625","On the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “There is nothing heavier in the scale of a believer on the Day of Resurrection than good character, and Allah hates the obscene and indecent” ([Al-Tirmidhi]"
"626","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about what most brings people into Paradise? He said: “Fearing Allah and good character.” And he was asked about what most brings people into Hell. He said: “The mouth and the private parts.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"627","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The most perfect of believers in faith is the one with the best character, and the best of you are the best of you with respect to their wives.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"628","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “The believer, by his good character, attains the status of the one who is fasting and standing” [Abu Dawud]."
"629","On the authority of Abu Imamah Al-Bahili, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I guarantee a house in the outskirts of Paradise for whoever abandons quarreling, even if he is in the right, and for a house in the middle of Paradise for whoever abandons lying, even if he is joking, and for a house at the top of Paradise for whoever has good character” [An authentic hadith narrated by Abu Dawud with an authentic chain of transmission]."
"630","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Those who are dearest to me and closest to me in assembly on the Day of Resurrection are those who have the best morals, and those who are most hateful to me and farthest from me on the Day of Resurrection are the chatterers, the rants, and the arrogant ones.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, we have learned “the chatterers and the boastful ones.” So what are the al-mutafahhiqun? He said: “The arrogant ones.” [Al-Tirmidhi] “The talkative”: he is one who talks a lot out of affectation. “The one who rants”: he is one who overreaches people with his speech, and speaks with a full mouth, boastfully and glorifying his words; “Al-Mutafihiq”: Its origin is from Al-Fahq, which means fullness, and it is the one who fills his mouth with words, expanding with it and becoming arrogant with it, and displaying virtue over others. Al-Tirmidhi narrated on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, may Allah have mercy on him, in the interpretation of good manners. He said: It is a cheerful face, giving good, and restraining from harm."
"631","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Ashaj Abdul Qais: “You have two qualities that Allah loves: forbearance and gentleness.” [Muslim]."
"632","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah is gentle and loves gentleness in all matters” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"633","On her authority, the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Allah is kind and loves gentleness, and He gives for kindness what He does not give for violence, and He does not give for anything else” [Muslim]."
"634","On her authority, the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Kindness is not in anything except that it beautifies it, and is not removed from anything except that it disgraces it” [Muslim]."
"635","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A Bedouin urinated in the mosque, so the people stood up to attack him, so the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Leave him and throw on his urine a bucket of water, or a large quantity of water, for you were sent to facilitate and were not sent to make it difficult” [Al-Bukhari]."
"636","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Make things easy and do not make things difficult, give good tidings and do not alienate (Agreed upon)."
"637","On the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Whoever deprives kindness deprives all goodness” [Muslim]."
"638","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said to the Prophet (ﷺ): Advise me. He said: “Do not get angry.” He repeated it several times and said: “Do not get angry.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"639","On the authority of Abu Ya’la Shaddad bin Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “Allah has decreed goodness upon everything, so if you kill, kill well, and if you slaughter, slaughter well, and let one of you sharpen his blade and have mercy on his sacrifice” [Muslim]."
"640","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was never given a choice between two matters except that he took the easier of the two, unless it was a sin. If it was a sin, he was the furthest from it. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never took revenge for himself in anything, unless the sanctity of Allah was violated, in which case he avenged Allah Almighty. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"641","And on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Shall I not tell you to whom the Fire is forbidden - or to whom the Fire is forbidden? - It is forbidden to every relative who is easy, gentle and easy.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"642","And on the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said to the Prophet (ﷺ): Has there come a day for you that was more severe than the day of Uhud? He said: “I have met my people, and the worst I have ever met with them was on the day of Aqaba, when I presented myself to Ibn Abd Yalil bin Abd Kulal, but he did not answer me to what I wanted, so I set off with worry on my face, and I did not wake up until I was like the horn of a fox. So I looked, and there was Gabriel, and he called me and he called me and said: Allah Almighty has heard what your people say to you, and what they have responded to you, and he has sent to you the King of the Mountains so that you may command him whatever you wish regarding them. So the King of the Mountains called me, and he greeted me and then said: O Muhammad, Allah has heard what your people say to you, and I am the King of the Mountains, and my Lord has sent me to you so that you may command me to command you, so whatever you wish: if you wish, you can close upon them the two woods.’ Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Rather, I hope that from their loins will emerge someone who will worship Allah alone, not associating anything with Him.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"643","On her authority, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never struck anything with his hand, not a woman, or a servant, unless he was struggling in the cause of Allah, and nothing was ever done to him in which he would take revenge on the one who wronged him, unless he violated something of the prohibitions of Allah Almighty, in which case he would take revenge for Allah Almighty. [Muslim]."
"644","And on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he was wearing a Najran cloak with a thick border, and a Bedouin caught up with him and pulled him with his cloak tightly, so I looked at the shoulder of the Prophet (ﷺ), and the thick hem of the cloak had left a mark on his shoulder from the force of the pull. He laughed, then he said: O Muhammad, pass me some of Allah’s wealth that you have, so he turned to him and he laughed, then ordered him to do so. With a bid. (Agreed upon)"
"645","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) telling the story of one of the prophets. May Allah’s prayers and peace be upon them. His people beat him and made him bloody while he wiped the blood from his face and said: “O Allah, forgive my people, for they are ignorant of what they are doing” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"646","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The strong man is not the one who fights, but the one who controls himself when he is angry.” (Agreed upon)"
"647","And on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I am related by origin to them, and they cut me off, and I do good to them and they treat me badly, and I forbear with them and they are ignorant of me! So he said: “If you were as you said, it is as if you are pouring molten lead into their ears, and you would still have a support from Allah Almighty over them as long as you remained in that state” [Muslim] and it was previously explained in the “Chapter on Connecting the Wombs.”"
"648","On the authority of Abu Masoud Uqba bin Amr Al-Badri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: I am delaying the morning prayer because of so-and-so, which will prolong us! I have never seen the Prophet (ﷺ) get more angry in a sermon than he did that day. He said: “O people, some of you are repulsive, so which of you, the leader of the people, should be brief, for behind him are the elderly, the young, and the needy.” And the young and the needy” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"649","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came from a journey, and my niche was covered with a tapestry containing statues. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw it, he tore it down and his face changed color with disapproval, and he said: “O Aisha, the people who will be most severely tormented by Allah on the Day of Resurrection are those who are compared to Allah’s creation” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"650","On her authority, the Quraysh were concerned about the matter of the Makhzumi woman who had stolen, so they said: Who will speak to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about her? They said: Who would dare to speak to him except Usamah ibn Zayd, the beloved of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)? So Osama spoke, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do you intercede regarding one of the limits set by Allah Almighty?” Then he rose and delivered a sermon to the people, then said: “The people before you were destroyed because if the noble among them stole, they would leave him, and if the weak among them stole, they would impose punishment on him! By Allah, if Fatima, daughter of Muhammad, had stolen, her hand would have been cut off.” (Agreed upon)"
"651","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) saw phlegm in the qiblah, and it bothered him until it was seen on his face, so he stood up and scratched it with his hand and said: “When one of you stands up in his prayer, he is in conversation with his Lord, and his Lord is between him and the qiblah, so let none of you spit in the qiblah, but to his left, or under his foot.” Then he took the end of his robe and spit into it, then returned some of it to the other. He said: “Or he does it like this” (Agreed upon)."
"652","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is responsible for his flock: the imam is a shepherd and responsible for his flock, the man is a shepherd for his family and responsible for his flock, the woman is a shepherd in her husband’s house and responsible for her flock, the servant is a shepherd for his master’s property and responsible for his flock, and all of you are a shepherd and responsible for his flock.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"653","On the authority of Abu Ya’la Ma’qil bin Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “There is no servant from whom Allah has concealed a flock, who dies while he is treacherous to his flock, except that Allah forbids Paradise for him.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] [And in a narration: “But he did not encompass it with good counsel, he will not find the fragrance of Paradise”] And in a narration by Muslim: “There is no leader who takes charge of the affairs of the Muslims, and then does not strive for them and advise them, but he will not enter Paradise with them.”"
"654","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying in this house of mine: “O Allah, whoever is appointed in charge of the affairs of my nation and is harsh on them, be harsh on him, and whoever is appointed in charge of the affairs of my nation and is kind to them, be kind to him” [Muslim]."
"655","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The children of Israel were ruled by prophets. Whenever a prophet died, another prophet succeeded him, and there will be no prophet after me, and there will be many successors after me.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us to do? He said: “Fulfill the pledge of allegiance of the first to the first, then give them their right, and ask Allah to be your Protector, for Allah will ask them about what has entrusted them.” (Agreed upon)"
"656","On the authority of Aidh bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, that he entered upon Ubayd Allah bin Ziyad and said to him: My son, I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “The worst of shepherds is the one who harms/crushes the flock,” so beware of being one of them. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"657","On the authority of Abu Maryam al-Azdi, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said to Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Whoever is appointed by Allah to do any of the affairs of the Muslims, and he hides himself from their needs, their complaints, and their poverty, Allah will hide without his need, seclusion, and poverty on the Day of Resurrection.” So he made Muawiyah a man responsible for the needs of the people. [Narrated by Abu Dawud and al-Tirmidhi]."
"658","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “There are seven whom Allah will shade in His shade on the day when there is no shade but His shade: a just imam, a young man who grew up in the worship of Allah Almighty, a man whose heart was attached to the mosques, two men who loved each other for the sake of Allah, who came together for Him and separated for Him, and a man who was invited by a woman of position and beauty, and said: I fear Allah, and a man who gave charity and hid it so that his left hand did not know His left hand is what his right hand can spend, and a man who mentioned Allah alone and his eyes filled with tears.” (Agreed upon)"
"659","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Indeed, those who are just in the sight of Allah are on platforms of light: those who are just in their judgments, their families, and those to whom they are in charge” [Muslim]."
"660","On the authority of Awf bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “The best of you are the imams whom you love and who love you, and you pray for them and they pray for you, and the worst of your imams are those whom you hate and they hate you, and you curse them and they curse them!” He said: We said, O Messenger of Allah, shall we not fight them? He said: No, as long as they establish prayer among you, no. As long as they establish prayer among you” [Muslim]."
"661","On the authority of Iyad bin Himar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “The people of Paradise are three: a just and successful ruler, a merciful man who is kind-hearted to every relative and a Muslim, and a chaste and self-sufficient person with dependents.” [Muslim]."
"662","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “A Muslim person must listen and obey in what he likes and dislikes, unless he is commanded to commit a disobedience. If he is commanded to commit a disobedience, then there is neither hearing nor obedience” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"663","On his authority, he said: When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to listen and obey, he would say to us: “As much as you are able” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"664","On his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Whoever removes his hand from obedience will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection without proof for him, and whoever dies without a pledge of allegiance on his neck will die a death of pre-Islamic times” [Muslim]. And in his narration: “And whoever dies separating from the group will die a death of pre-Islamic times” [Muslim]. In his narration: “Whoever dies leaving the group will die a death of ignorance.”"
"665","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Listen and obey, even if an Ethiopian slave is appointed over you, as if his head is a raisin” [Al-Bukhari]."
"666","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “You must listen and obey in your hardship, your ease, your invigoration, your dislike, and what is difficult for you” [Muslim]."
"667","And on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey, so we camped down, and among us was someone who was repairing his tent, and among us was someone practicing archery, and among us was someone tending to his grazing animals, when the herald of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called for the congregational prayer. So we gathered to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: “There was no prophet before me except that it was his duty to guide his nation to the best of what he knows for them, and warn them of the evil of what he knows for them. And indeed, this nation of yours has set its end in its beginning, and its end will be afflicted by calamities and things that you deny, and tribulations will come, some of which will soften one another. And temptations will come and the believer will say: This is my destruction. Then it will be revealed; and tribulation will come and the believer will say: This is this. So whoever loves to be removed from Hell and enter Paradise, let his death come while he believes in Allah and the Last Day, and let him come to the people whom he loves to come to. And whoever pledges allegiance to an imam and gives him the deal of his hand and the fruit of his heart, let him obey him if he is able. If another comes and disputes with him, then strike the neck of the other.” [Muslim]. His saying “"
"668","On the authority of Abu Hunaydah, Wael bin Hajar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Salamah bin Yazid al-Ja’fi asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: O Prophet of Allah, what do you think if rulers are appointed over us asking us for their rights and denying us our rights, what do you command us to do? So he turned away from it, then asked him, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Listen and obey; for it is upon them that they bear, and upon you is what you bear.” [Muslim]."
"669","On the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “After me there will be favoritism, and things that you deny!” They said: O Messenger of Allah, how do you order those of us who have realized that? He said: “You will fulfill the right that is upon you, and you will ask Allah that is yours” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"670","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah, and whoever obeys the leader has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the leader has disobeyed me” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"671","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever dislikes something about his ruler, let him be patient, for whoever rebels against the authority even by a span will die the death of ignorance” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"672","On the authority of Abu Bakra, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Whoever insults the Sultan, Allah will insult him” [Al-Tirmidhi]. There are many hadiths in the Sahih section, some of which have been previously mentioned in chapters."
"673","On the authority of Abu Saeed Abd al-Rahman bin Samra, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “O Abd al-Rahman bin Samra: Do not ask for leadership, for if it is given to you without asking, you will be helped to fulfill its duties, and if it is given to you because you asked for it, you will be fully accountable for it, and if you swear an oath and see something else better than it, then do what is better, and atone for your oath” ((Agreed) (on him).."
"674","On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O Abu Dharr, I see that you are weak, and I love for you what I love for myself. Do not be appointed as commander over two people, and do not take charge of an orphan's property” [Muslim]."
"675","And on his authority, he said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, won’t you use me? So he struck my shoulder with his hand and then said: “O Abu Dharr, you are weak, and it is a trust, and on the Day of Resurrection it will be disgrace and regret, except for the one who took it as it was due and paid back what he owed for it” [Muslim]."
"676","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “You will strive for leadership, and you will regret it on the Day of Resurrection” [Al-Bukhari]."
"677","-On the authority of Abu Saeed and Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with them, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah has not sent a prophet, nor appointed a caliph, except that he had two inner circles, an inner circle that commanded him to do good and urged him to do it, and a inner circle that commanded him to do evil and urged him to do it, and the infallible one is among Allah’s protection” [Al-Bukhari]."
"678","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If Allah wants good for the prince, He makes for him a truthful advisor; if the ruler forgets to consult him, the advisor reminds him, and if the ruler remembers to consult him, the advisor helps him, and if He wants something other than that, He makes him a bad minister. If he forgets, he does not mention him, and when he mentions, he does not help him” [Narrated by Abu Dawud with a good chain of transmission according to the conditions of Muslim]."
"679","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (ﷺ) with two men from my cousins, and one of them said: O Messenger of Allah, command us to do some of what Allah, the Almighty, has entrusted you with. The other said the same thing, so he said: “By Allah, we will not entrust this work to anyone who asks for it, or to anyone who is keen on it” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
